li_src_agent.ts: {\n  \"agent\": \"KimiCode-defect-scan\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/defect-remediation-integration\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-remediation-integration\",\n  \"base\": \"b31ba9278c63165eefe2c58c66dfde8358b84d91\",\n  \"head\": \"e5a1402d9851d005e447c306844374e712529dd9\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-25T23:32:00Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Explicit handoff of cli/src/agent.ts for the mode-selected read-only restoration and provider-recovery session continuation fixes in the existing defect-remediation slice. Preserve existing uncommitted tests in experimental_and_readonly.test.ts and session_durable_fields.test.ts. No unrelated edits; run focused tests and independent review before integration.\",\n  \"status\": \"Handoff recorded following user update that Kimi is waiting. Existing claim directory had no owner.json; prior owner could not be verified. Kimi is now the recorded file owner; source edits remain Kimi's responsibility.\"\n}\nSUITE: free\n> build · deepseek-flash\nHandoff slice completed and independently accepted; no push or merge was performed.\n\n## Verification of environment\n- Active session directory: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-remediation-integration`\n- Branch: `v1/defect-remediation-integration`\n- Dirty files limited to the handed-off scope:\n  - `cli/src/agent.ts`\n  - `cli/src/types.ts` (comment clarification)\n  - `cli/test/experimental_and_readonly.test.ts`\n  - `cli/test/session_durable_fields.test.ts`\n- Shared checkout `/home/mike/nexus-code` was not modified.\n- `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` is held by `KimiCode-defect-scan`; `SUITE` was claimed for each focused run and released afterward.\n\n## Implementation completed\n- **Mode-selected read-only**\n  - Explicit `--read-only` and read-only roles remain authoritative across `setApprovalMode`.\n  - `--mode read-only` / `REDACTED` start enforced but can be deliberately changed.\n  - Runtime `/mode read-only` is enforced and reversible.\n  - Bridge, authority engine, skills, MCP, plugins and knowledge follow the effective posture.\n  - The transient checkpoint fallback affects only the effective posture, never `config.readOnly`; releasing it restores the queued auto/review mode.\n  - Workspace and shell switches reconstruct bridge/authority/managers with the effective posture.\n- **No extension churn**\n  - Review↔auto and other no-op posture changes no longer recreate MCP/plugin managers or reset `extensibilityInitialized`.\n  - Actual read-only transitions and workspace changes still refresh extension posture.\n- **Provider-recovery continuation**\n  - `restoreConversation` carries `providerRecovery`, `operation` and the untrusted `changeBaseline`.\n  - `checkpointDurableState` re-emits them; the recovered verifier baseline remains untrusted and invalidated.\n  - `recoverFromTaskState` restores provider recovery/operation too.\n  - `resetConversation` clears transient recovery state.\n- Tests were extended without removing existing coverage.\n\n## Verification\n- Focused slice: **13/13**\n- `readonly_home` + `repl_checkpoint_choices`: **11/11**\n- Named sidecar checkpoint-fallback regression: **pass**\n- Reviewer also ran approval/readonly/provider-recovery focused suites: **33/33**\n- `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`: pass\n- `git diff --check`: pass\n\n## Independent review\nThree review rounds; the final verdict was **ACCEPT**. Documented residuals are pre-existing and outside this slice: worktree-bound `recoverFromTaskState` still runs `setWorkspace`/reset after restoration, which wipes recovered conversation/envelope; that behavior predates this fix.\n\nChanges remain uncommitted as instructed. Integration, commit, push and merge are left to the owner.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1709,"nanos":154851939}},"started_at_ms":1792975489715,"completed_at_ms":1792977198871}}
