L_DIFF_SHA=1757ab36a6d535b1e0e039df01c09c30d7ea8ece6e0ad6fc80061e3f741e3af6\n## v1/defect-remediation-integration...origin/main [ahead 28, behind 16]\n M cli/src/agent.ts\n M cli/src/types.ts\n M cli/test/experimental_and_readonly.test.ts\n M cli/test/session_durable_fields.test.ts\n> build · deepseek-flash\n## Current snapshot\n- Worktree: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-remediation-integration`\n- Branch: `v1/defect-remediation-integration`\n- Current diff SHA-256: **`1757ab36a6d535b1e0e039df01c09c30d7ea8ece6e0ad6fc80061e3f741e3af6`** — matches the snapshot under independent review.\n- No push, merge, rebase, or commit performed.\n- Dirty scope remains exactly:\n  - `cli/src/agent.ts`\n  - `cli/src/types.ts` (comment only)\n  - `cli/test/experimental_and_readonly.test.ts`\n  - `cli/test/session_durable_fields.test.ts`\n\n## 01:12 UTC `provider_recovery_agent.test.ts` process\nI cannot truthfully report a command, environment, or result for that specific process.\n- The shared ledger records only that the process was present at **01:12:26Z**, exited before **01:12:54Z**, and that **no live SUITE `owner.json` existed at 01:12:54Z**.\n- No command line, stdout, or exit code for that 01:12 process is retained in my records, so I am not claiming it passed.\n- Therefore I cannot confirm the required atomic SUITE claim was held for that process. The known SUITE history around then is: claimed **00:45:37Z**, released **00:48:46Z** after the earlier focused set; no SUITE owner at 01:12:54Z.\n- I later ran the same test under an atomic SUITE claim and recorded the exact result:\n  - Claim: **01:15:41Z**\n  - Command: `HOME=$(mktemp -d) XDG_CONFIG_HOME=$(mktemp -d) npx tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 test/provider_recovery_agent.test.ts`\n  - Exit: **0**\n  - Result: **17/17 pass**\n  - Log: `/tmp/opencode/provider_recovery_agent-final-20261026T011541Z.log`\n\n## Final focused validation (all under SUITE ownership, isolated HOME/XDG)\n- `experimental_and_readonly.test.ts` + `session_durable_fields.test.ts`: **13/13 pass**, exit 0 — `/tmp/opencode/agent-readonly-recovery-final.log`\n- `readonly_home.test.ts` + `repl_checkpoint_choices.test.ts`: **11/11 pass**, exit 0 — `/tmp/opencode/agent-readonly-final.log`\n- Named sidecar checkpoint-fallback regression: **1/1 pass**, exit 0 — `/tmp/opencode/agent-sidecar-final.log`\n- `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`: **exit 0** — `/tmp/opencode/agent-tsc-final.log`\n- `git diff --check`: **exit 0** — `/tmp/opencode/agent-diffcheck-final.log`\n- SUITE released at **01:16:43Z**; the exact diff SHA and log paths were recorded in `nexus-claims.log`.\n\n## Implementation status\nCompleted in the current snapshot:\n- Explicit, mode-selected, runtime, role and checkpoint-fallback read-only authority is synchronized across agent, bridge, authority engine, skills, MCP, plugins and knowledge.\n- Equivalent posture changes no longer tear down extension managers or reset extensibility; actual read-only/workspace changes still refresh them.\n- Workspace and shell reconstruction use the effective read-only posture.\n- Provider recovery, operation and untrusted change baseline survive session continuation and checkpointing; durable task recovery restores recovery fields; reset clears transient recovery.\n\nNo real blocker remains in this slice. Pre-existing residual: worktree-bound `recoverFromTaskState` still runs `setWorkspace`/reset after restoration and discards recovered conversation/envelope; that behavior predates this fix and is documented for follow-up.\n\nIndependent reviewer `plan05_readonly_review` was notified that the current diff SHA is unchanged at `1757ab36…`; no new hash is needed.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":138,"nanos":480670402}},"started_at_ms":1792977274351,"completed_at_ms":1792977412832}}
