{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T01:21:54.576Z","ordinal":367014,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a175cc-bd90-79c3-b7b1-fdf7f2f353b3","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed the current diff at base `e5a1402d9851d005e447c306844374e712529dd9`; its SHA-256 is `9ee90f3711ce51d3e4d0dae7c8a443359f6afa1e193a7f969f867c0bf1b30138`.\n\nThe prior full-access finding is resolved: effective read-only posture now disables the authority engine’s full-access bypass in [agent.ts:1294–1298](/home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-remediation-integration/cli/src/agent.ts:1294), while configured full-access intent is restored only when the mode permits it. The new regression checks that read-only confinement rejects an out-of-workspace read and that full access is disabled and restored across mode and checkpoint-fallback transitions ([experimental_and_readonly.test.ts:360–376](/home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-remediation-integration/cli/test/experimental_and_readonly.test.ts:360)).\n\nI found no remaining source-level blocker in the reviewed slice. I did not edit files or run tests; the reported validation results are implementer-provided."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a175cc-b3b0-7662-b36e-ca50f56caf19","create_time":1792977714.5760458}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18065}}
