rmits. Add regressions starting fullAccess:true, switching to read-only and checkpoint fallback, and verify out-of-workspace reads are denied. Keep existing scope/claim; no rebase, push, merge, or unrelated files. Before focused tests, acquire SUITE claim; isolate HOME/XDG per project rules. Then report exact diff hash, test commands/results, and release SUITE.\n3285867       02:44  1.0  0.1 Ssl  ep_poll                  opencode run --session ses_e9673e166ffeJQMRc8gDXVixKQ Independent reviewer has now returned ACCEPT for exact diff SHA256 9ee90f3711ce51d3e4d0dae7c8a443359f6afa1e193a7f969f867c0bf1b30138. Focused validation records are complete and SUITE is released. Please take the next integration-preparation step: inspect git status and recent git log for foreign commits, then create one local commit containing only your reviewed four-file slice on the existing branch (no push, no rebase, no merge). Preserve the current worktree and do not amend prior commits. Record commit SHA and diff/commit identity in nexus-claims.log, then explicitly release FILE_cli_src_agent.ts and your integration-candidate claim so the owner can cherry-pick/reapply the reviewed patch on a clean worktree at current origin/main 0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2. Do not edit after commit. If the claim protocol or branch history prevents this, report the specific reason and stop at that safe boundary.\n1792977936.6550372930 /home/mike/.local/share/opencode/log/opencode.log\n1784121652.5407256520 /home/mike/.local/share/opencode/log/2026-07-15T132044.log\n1784117137.6328773400 /home/mike/.local/share/opencode/log/2026-07-14T221055.log\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":89746}},"started_at_ms":1792977945356,"completed_at_ms":1792977945357}}
