{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T01:30:54.010Z","ordinal":367526,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a175d4-f8ba-7f80-86dd-5c58848a3012","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Current: 2026-10-26 1:30am UTC\nThis file has prior observations — supplementary context follows. The Read result below is the full requested section.\n- **Need details on a past observation?** get_observations([IDs]) — ~300 tokens each.\n- **Need a structural map first?** smart_outline(\"cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts\") — line numbers only, cheaper than re-reading.\n### Oct 10, 2026\n15151 10:53a 🔵 Phase 20 Branch — Three Tests Still Failing After findingsOutgrown Cross-Turn Fix\n### Oct 14, 2026\n17631 12:53p 🔵 nexus run --resume Silently Restarts From Scratch — Conversation and Objective Not Recovered\n### Oct 18, 2026\n18953 11:31a 🔵 PR #30 Diff Reveals durable_continuity Tests Added — Not T3 Gate Changes\n19147 9:57p 🔵 SPEC-04 AGT-05 Text Is Stale — Describes Pre-PR-4d State; v1 Closure Requires Update\n### Oct 19, 2026\n19821 2:59p ❓ Full CodeQL annotation inventory for integration HEAD: 31 alerts across 15 files with specific vulnerability types\n### Oct 21, 2026\n20889 4:39a 🔴 PR #89 CodeQL Fixes: Polynomial ReDoS and Biased Crypto Random Resolved in Egress and Test"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a175d0-ddec-7861-9122-03a48c8a4185","create_time":1792978254.01053,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T01:30:54.878Z","ordinal":367527,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a175d0-ddec-7861-9122-03a48c8a4185","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d26fa665-9108-473d-80ee-c2a8836667c3","process_id":"7666","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -n 35 cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts; test ! -e .git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_durable_continuity.test.ts && echo NEW_TEST_CLAIM_FREE; test ! -e .git/nexus-claims/SUITE && echo SUITE_FREE || cat .git/nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print0 | xargs -0 rg -l 'durable_continuity\\.test\\.ts' || true"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/agent-readonly-current","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"tail -n 35 cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts; test ! -e .git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_durable_continuity.test.ts && echo NEW_TEST_CLAIM_FREE; test ! -e .git/nexus-claims/SUITE && echo SUITE_FREE || cat .git/nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print0 | xargs -0 rg -l 'durable_continuity\\.test\\.ts' || true"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    }\n  });\n});\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------- operation records and redaction (F1)\n\ndescribe(\"durable operation records match their start whatever the provider's call id looks like\", () => {\n  test(\"a high-entropy invocation id is redacted on disk, yet the operation is recorded as completed; recorded progress clears it\", () => {\n    const dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-cont-op-\"));\n    const ws = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-cont-ws-\"));\n    try {\n      const identity = WorkspacePath.fromSelectedWorkspace(ws);\n      const manager = new DurableStateManager({ baseDir: dir, workspacePaths: [identity] });\n      const now = new Date().toISOString();\n      manager.saveTaskState({ schemaVersion: 1, taskId: \"t1\", sessionId: \"t1\", id: \"t1\", title: \"t\", workspacePath: identity.value, workspace: identity.value, createdAt: now, updatedAt: now, status: \"in_progress\", activePlan: [], milestones: [], validationReceipts: [], messages: [] });\n      const id = highEntropyId();\n      manager.recordOperationStart(\"t1\", { invocationId: id, seq: 7, toolName: \"read_file\" });\n      assert.notEqual(manager.loadTaskState(\"t1\").currentOperation!.invocationId, id, \"precondition: persistence redacts this id\");\n      manager.recordOperationEnd(\"t1\", id, { success: true }, 7);\n      assert.equal(manager.loadTaskState(\"t1\").currentOperation!.status, \"completed\");\n      // Finished, but its result never reached the durable conversation: recovery treats it as interrupted.\n      const recovered = manager.recoverTaskState(\"t1\", { revalidateCandidate: false });\n      assert.equal(recovered.interrupted, true);\n      assert.match(recovered.interruptedOperation!.error!, /result was not recorded/);\n      manager.recordOperationStart(\"t1\", { invocationId: id, seq: 8, toolName: \"read_file\" });\n      manager.recordOperationEnd(\"t1\", id, { success: true }, 8);\n      manager.recordProgress(\"t1\", { messages: [{ role: \"system\", content: \"s\" }] });\n      assert.equal(manager.loadTaskState(\"t1\").currentOperation, null);\n      assert.equal(manager.recoverTaskState(\"t1\", { revalidateCandidate: false }).interrupted, false);\n    } finally {\n      fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n      fs.rmSync(ws, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n});\nNEW_TEST_CLAIM_FREE\nSUITE_FREE\nfind: ‘.git/nexus-claims’: Not a directory\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_BLOCKER_REMEDIATION_2026-10-08.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/context.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_PERSISTENCE_COST_SPLIT/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/findings-verification.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/review-prep.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/dispositions.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":695477262}},"started_at_ms":1792978254182,"completed_at_ms":1792978254878}}
