{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T01:33:18.717Z","ordinal":367686,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a175d7-2dfd-74a2-83b4-db9bef2aecf6","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed staged diff SHA-256 `d5ec29dda0e00e9ef617aad7282726cad83ce5db84a357872ede837a25c97ae8` against base `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`.\n\n`buildConfig({ mode: \"read-only\" })` sets `approvalMode` but leaves `readOnly` false ([config.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/agent-readonly-current/cli/src/config.ts:253)). The `AutonomousAgent` constructor still initializes its bridge, authority engine, and extension managers from `config.readOnly` ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/agent-readonly-current/cli/src/agent.ts:1105)). So a newly constructed agent is not actually read-only until a caller later invokes `setApprovalMode()`. The new test expects read-only enforcement immediately after construction ([experimental_and_readonly.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/agent-readonly-current/cli/test/experimental_and_readonly.test.ts:278)), which conflicts with the constructor logic.\n\nInitialize the bridge, authority engine, and extension managers from the effective initial mode, and record that same posture in `extensionPosture`. I did not edit files or run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a175d0-ddec-7861-9122-03a48c8a4185","create_time":1792978398.7175336}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18080}}
