{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T01:38:26.840Z","ordinal":368022,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a175db-e198-7063-9a45-566f4d6d1b90","call_id":"call_44f01003852f427d8874b01f87462337","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3449)\nTotal output lines: 62\n\n12:## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n15:- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n18:## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n20:Claims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\n24:mkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\n26:if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\n30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n37:- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n51:| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n56:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n60:| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n61:| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n62:| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n63:| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n64:| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n65:| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n66:| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n67:| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n71:| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n72:| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Clai…1449 tokens truncated…f741e3af6 after final manager/churn fixes; reviewer snapshot is current. Independent review requests no edits; evidence logs recorded, SUITE released. No push/merge/rebase.\n2026-10-26T01:16:46Z UPDATE RELEASE_PUBLISHER: PR244 exact base/head rechecked; Node22/24 test jobs pending, CodeQL/JS-TS pass, independent ACCEPT; local follow-up e4c70bf plus unstaged doc correction recorded, not pushed. Kimi remediation/SUITE and independent review remain owner-controlled; no takeover. RC7 not accepted; stable gates remain open.\n2026-10-26T01:21:14Z RELEASE SUITE agent=KimiCode-defect-scan branch=v1/defect-remediation-integration diff_sha256=9ee90f3711ce51d3e4d0dae7c8a443359f6afa1e193a7f969f867c0bf1b30138; provider_recovery_agent exit=0 17/17 log=/tmp/opencode/provider_recovery_agent-final2.log; slice exit=0 13/13 log=/tmp/opencode/agent-final2.log; tsc exit=0; diff-check exit=0; isolated HOME/XDG; SUITE released\n2026-10-26T01:21:14Z REVIEW_UPDATE plan05_readonly_review: new diff_sha256=9ee90f3711ce51d3e4d0dae7c8a443359f6afa1e193a7f969f867c0bf1b30138 adds AuthorityAdmissionEngine.fullAccess synchronization (disabled in read-only/fallback; restored in auto only when configured fullAccess was true) plus regression asserting out-of-workspace confine denial. Previous hash 1757ab... superseded. No push/merge/rebase. Please re-review this snapshot.\n2026-10-26T01:25:01Z REVIEW_ACCEPT plan05_readonly_review branch=v1/defect-remediation-integration base=e5a1402d9851d005e447c306844374e712529dd9 diff_sha256=9ee90f3711ce51d3e4d0dae7c8a443359f6afa1e193a7f969f867c0bf1b30138; prior fullAccess/read-only bypass finding resolved by synchronizing engine posture; regressions cover out-of-workspace denial and fallback/mode restoration; reviewer ran no tests; implementer evidence remains 17+13+11+1 focused tests, tsc and diff-check PASS. No push/merge/rebase; awaiting owner local commit and claim release for current-main requalification.\n2026-10-26T01:28:11Z INTEGRATION_CANDIDATE_COMMIT commit=f15618d5cbb36af79581bdd3912357a6abd5b0ee parent=e5a1402d9851d005e447c306844374e712529dd9 branch=v1/defect-remediation-integration base=0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2 diff_sha256=9ee90f3711ce51d3e4d0dae7c8a443359f6afa1e193a7f969f867c0bf1b30138 files=cli/src/agent.ts,cli/src/types.ts,cli/test/experimental_and_readonly.test.ts,cli/test/session_durable_fields.test.ts independent_review=ACCEPT; local-only commit, no push/rebase/merge; releasing FILE_cli_src_agent.ts and DEFECT_REMEDIATION_INTEGRATION_CANDIDATE_20261025 for owner cherry-pick/reapply on origin/main 0542312\n2026-10-26T01:29:35Z CLAIM_RECOVERY empty_directory=FILE_cli_test_experimental_and_readonly.test.ts owner_json=absent last_mtime=2026-10-25T17:21:51Z; no owner identity/activity record; clean slice commit f15618d5cbb36af79581bdd3912357a6abd5b0ee independently accepted; current owner release recorded at 2026-10-26T01:28:11Z\n2026-10-26T01:29:35Z CLAIM_CONFLICT name=FILE_cli_test_session_durable_fields.test.ts no files modified\n2026-10-26T01:29:57Z CLAIM_RECOVERY empty_directory=FILE_cli_test_session_durable_fields.test.ts owner_json=absent last_mtime=2026-10-25T17:21:51Z; no owner identity/activity record; current Kimi slice commit is clean, independently accepted; user-authorized takeover of genuinely stalled work\n2026-10-26T01:29:57Z CLAIM codex-root slice=DEFECT_AGENT_READONLY_RECOVERY_20261026 files=4 base=0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2 branch=v1/defect-agent-readonly-current worktree=/home