32:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:36:| REQ-AGT-31..39 | CTX-003..011 | Durable vs retrieved distinction; role policy; budget vs actual route capacity, fail closed (`ContextBudgetError`); cross-boundary failover re-admission; same-boundary failover cheap; compaction removes only disposable; admission evidence; resume≠recovery; manual==auto compaction semantics | P2 §12 | DEMONSTRATED / SBIS (CTX-006: client.ts executeWithFailover; egress.test) | P (WP05 qual for CTX-006) | 10-12 I-05 (provider context-length 400 ends turn), CTX-02 (steering truncated after compaction; fixed ee70f68), d88a897 false-absence; 10-13 compaction ledger self-assessed only |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:81:| REQ-DX-01 | Install promise | Linux x86-64 glibc≥2.35, Node≥20; installer verifies SHA-256; no root, no shell rc edits; manual uninstall keeps user data | quickstart.md:7-27,59-68; DEVELOPMENT.md:19 | Published alpha.2 (release run 38539108878) | N |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:128:| HIST-03 | S2 | Extensions, docs truth | docs/USER_MANUAL.md:294; cli/src/plugins.ts:93-96,139-145,256 | SOURCE: manual promises plugin handlers \"execute in isolated Node.js worker_threads with strict timeout boundaries and memory caps\". Plugins are loaded with in-process `await import()` and custom tools run `handler(args)` directly; `executeSandboxed` has no caller | Users trust untrusted plugins based on a nonexistent sandbox | Fix the manual (or wire the sandbox); RELEASE-REQUIRED doc correction |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:131:| HIST-06 | S3 | Install/positioning docs | docs/USER_MANUAL.md:3,14,19; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:24-25,43; quickstart.md:21-23 | SOURCE/DOC: manual claims \"direct parity with OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code\"; `harness repl` (installed binary is `nexus`); `nexus --approve` vs quickstart `nexus repl --approve`; ARCHITECTURE names homelab hardware/port 18010 and calls `repl.ts` the TUI; quickstart \"install another specific version\" example is identical to the pinned command; MCP_GUIDE link is `file:///home/mike/...` | New users get wrong commands and inflated expectations | Reconcile docs to shipped binary (RELEASE-REQUIRED) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:146:| 5 | T-06 run_tests filter not injectable | tester.ts:25-31 allowlist `^[A-Za-z0-9_:./ -]+$`, no leading `-` | HOLDS (still shell-interpolated, but charset-safe) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:22:- Capability discovery (client.ts:939-965, provider_capabilities.ts): `/models` entry -> gateway (`limits_version`, `/v1/tokenize`) or vLLM `max_model_len`; otherwise operator `--context-limit` or 65536/8192 client defaults. `/tokenize` only for gateway advertisements.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:33:| PRV-06 | S2 | standalone local inference | core/provider_capabilities.ts:29,72 (only `context_length`/`max_model_len` parsed; default 65536); agent.ts:4684-4689 (CAPACITY_REJECTED ends the turn) | SOURCE; INFERENCE on server behaviour: LM Studio `/v1/models` and llama.cpp `/v1/models` do not carry `max_model_len`, so standalone sizing is the 65536 default unless `--context-limit` is set. | On LM Studio/llama.cpp with a smaller loaded context the first large turn fails with a context error instead of compacting; user must know `--context-limit`. | Release-required: discover llama.cpp `/props` n_ctx and LM Studio `/api/v0/models` loaded context, or on CAPACITY_REJECTED compact and retry once with an actionable message. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:21:| agent.ts call sites | targeted: 1597-1640 (baseline/independence), 3315, 3385-3545 (completion oracle), 3940-3960, 4034, 4060-4090 (run_tests attempt), 4660-4705 (parse/truncation), 2236-2300 (measureAdmission), 5100-5160 (outcome) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:56:| VER-05 | S3 | Zero-test or all-skipped verifier runs | tester.ts:263-282; agent.ts:5126-5135 | RUNTIME (tester_probe). An exit-0 run with no executed tests is labelled REGRESSION_FREE (\"did not cover the modified deliverables\"), and it discharges the unverified-changes obligation (agent.ts:3520). Zero tests is no regression evidence. `hasExecutedTests` false positives: node:test \"ℹ tests 5\" with all skipped → true; jest \"5 skipped, 5 total\" → true; any output line starting `ok ` (go heuristic, e.g. \"ok all good\") → true. False negatives (conservative): mocha \"3 passing\", vitest \"Tests 5 passed (5)\". | REGRESSION_FREE overstates evidence. Exit code 2 is shared with UNVERIFIED, so the automation impact is limited. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: a pass with `!hasExecutedTests` → UNVERIFIED (reason NO_TESTS_EXECUTED), keeping the obligation. Subtract skipped counts. Anchor the go heuristic to `ok\\s+\\S+\\s+(\\d+\\.\\d+s|\\(cached\\))`. Add mocha/vitest parsers. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:59:| VER-08 | S2 | `--tdd` / `/tdd` | synthesizer.ts:239-326; agent.ts:5236-5255 | SOURCE + INFERENCE. `runAutonomousTdd` never calls `verifyRedPhase` or `verifyGreenPhase`, ignores every `agent.run` result, and contains dead code (266-272). Success is only a full-suite exit 0, with no check that tests executed. Each `agent.run` calls `resetConversation()` (AGT-01), so GREEN starts with no memory of the RED test. The RED prompt asks the model to call `task_completed` with a deliberately failing test, but the completion oracle runs the discovered verifier, which fails → completion refused (INFERENCE). The success summary claims \"RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR verified\". | The TDD mode advertises a protocol it does not enforce. RED turns likely end in NOT_ESTABLISHED or stagnation. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enforce the phases (run the repro target and require fail, then pass), carry the conversation between phases, exempt the RED phase from the completion oracle; or mark the mode experimental. Add an e2e test with a mock model. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:60:| REL-02 | S2 | docs → CLI | docs/USER_MANUAL.md:12-26 vs index.ts commands | RUNTIME. On the installed alpha.2, `nexus --approve` → `unknown option '--approve'` and `nexus -r` → `unknown option '-r'`. Through harness.sh they reach `run --approve`/`run -r`, which also fail (run requires a prompt and has no --approve). Quickstart uses the correct `nexus repl --approve`. | The documented resume and approval entry points fail on first use. | Accept the REPL flags at the top level, or fix the manual. Add a docs-command test that runs every fenced `nexus ...` line with `--help`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s3.notes.txt:5:[   5.77s] SCREEN panel-letters (80x24)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s3.notes.txt:8:[  11.18s] SCREEN after-turn (80x24)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:57:  - It enforces per-role ref policy (:343-373), a force-with-lease push (:334), and a scan to block the credential being reflected into git objects (:375-391).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:64:- Generated code is validated by `RestrictedCodeExecutor`, which runs `sudo -n setpriv --reuid=65534 ... --no-new-privs env -i` (restricted-code-executor.mjs:60-71). The integrator throws on any validation failure (integrator.mjs:71, 191, 210).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:70:- controller → generated code as uid 65534: there is no network or filesystem namespace isolation beyond the uid.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:84:| CON-007 | S3 | Generated-code containment | restricted-code-executor.mjs:52-71 | SOURCE. The isolation is uid 65534, `--no-new-privs`, cleared groups and a scrubbed env. It has no network namespace, seccomp or mount isolation, so model-generated TypeScript/tests can reach the network and read world-readable host files. The tests (RUNTIME) confirm uid, caps=0, env keys and no docker or lxd socket access. | A bounded risk on a single-user demo host. The docs already say not to use shared hosts (CONTEST.md:31). | Accept for the contest. For any non-demo use: `unshare -n` / bubblewrap. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:112:# contest Worker, built manually from its own dir (CON-010)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:128:- **Credential custody in the broker is careful.** Checks on owner, 0400 mode, nlink and inode-before/after; O_NOFOLLOW; buffers zero-filled after use; a reflection scan over all git objects; error output limited to an allowlist of codes (demo-transport.mjs:152-185,375-391). Executables are bound by file descriptor (linux-bound-exec). Git config is hardened (no system or global config, no hooks, no credential helper, `followRedirects=false`, protocol allowlist) at :192-212. Tests are RUNTIME-verified: demo-transport 8/8; artifact-token-response 14 revoke cases plus 8 post-revoke cases; credential-lifecycle 25 assertions; linux-bound-exec; classify-revoke 11 cases; worker token-response 10/10; work-state-contract 2/2.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:189:- In snap: `npm ci --prefix demo`, `npm ci --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice`, `npm audit --prefix …slice`, and `npm test --prefix demo`. All demo tests passed: adapter PASS, restricted-executor PASS (uid 65534, caps 0), runner 1/1, smoke 8 stages.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2_approval.py:16:    s.resize(40, 14); s.pump(1); s.dump(\"approval-40x14\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2_approval.py:17:    s.send(b\"y\", label=\"y at 40x14\"); s.pump(1); print(\"file after y@40:\", os.path.exists(ws + \"/hello.txt\"))\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json:17:      \"requestId\": \"1e6c5946-6630-4a7b-ad9b-5659285c3228\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json:50:      \"requestId\": \"1e6c5946-6630-4a7b-ad9b-5659285c3228\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:43:- Entry points: packaged `bin/nexus` = `node lib/cli/dist/index.js \"$@\"` (package-linux.sh:25-30); no args -> `repl`\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:60:| TUI-04 | S2 | Install -> first run | scripts/package-linux.sh:25-30; index.ts:747; live.rs:126-131; tui.ts:59-90 | SOURCE+RUNTIME: packaged `nexus` = REPL; no command reaches the live TUI; packaged `lib/core/nexus-tui --live` fails \"sidecar not found at <pkg>/cli/dist/sidecar.js\" (checkout-layout assumption `ancestors().nth(4)`). ISSUE12 UI-004 (\"TUI MUST serve as the default interactive human surface\" — Satisfied) is false for the shipped package | Release users get the weaker REPL (TUI-02/03/08 apply) and never the hardened TUI | Make `nexus` launch `nexus-tui --live` on a TTY with packaged sidecar path; resolve packaged layout |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:66:| TUI-10 | S3 | Narrow terminal | live_view.rs (approval hint/footer) | RUNTIME s2 @40x14: hint cut \"←→ approve/deny, paus\", footer \"(t…\"; @40x20 idle hint \"? for ke…\" | The instruction that explains how to decide is truncated exactly where it matters | Short-form hints under ~60 cols |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:103:`y` at 40x14, lone `y` after 2.5s quiet -> file absent each time; panel \"typing ignored · ←→ approve/deny, pause, enter\";\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:113:- Not-drawn panel cannot be answered (approval_drawn / shown, live_state.rs:1196-1202); resize to 40x14 kept the panel\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:123:- Terminal restore on panic/exit including bracketed paste and kitty flags (live.rs:270-284); SIGTERM/SIGHUP watchdog.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:133:| Kitty keyboard protocol / Shift+Enter, real terminal emulators (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code) | Manual matrix; pyte does not answer `CSI ? u` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:134:| ZWJ / emoji width correctness | Compare against a real terminal (kitty/wezterm screenshot) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:149:| TUI-R8 | Approval controls are spatially consistent and key hints remain complete at 40 cols | a11y (TUI-09/10) | POST-V1 | 40x14 screen dump contains full decision hint; ← focuses leftmost button |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:10:| src/agent.ts (5439) | full read |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:34:- Verification gate lives in the `task_completed` handler (3345-3571): open/blocked requirements refuse; configured or discovered verifier runs; prior FAILED on identical inputs is not rerun; discovered-verifier pass is VERIFIED only with fail-before/pass-after independence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:44:| AGT-01 | S2 | `nexus run --resume [id]` | core/app.ts:174-177, agent.ts:5236, index.ts:176 | RUNTIME (R2). `runTask` recovers the task (`recoverFromTaskState` restores messages/objective), then `agent.run()` calls `resetConversation()` unconditionally: the resumed request carried 2 messages (system+new prompt), none of the prior conversation; `objective` is also cleared. Only the unverified-change obligation survives (that is all `durable_continuity.test.ts:254` asserts). The result's `taskId` is captured before recovery (app.ts:174), so the result/session is keyed `task-ba261ade` while the recovered state is `task-02d1fbd5`. `--resume` with no id passes the literal `\"latest\"` → `Task state not found for task ID 'latest'` → task fails. | Headline \"resume\" for one-shot runs does not resume; a crash-resume of `run` silently restarts from scratch with a new id; `--resume` without id always fails. | Fix before v1: skip reset when resuming, use recovered id, resolve `latest` (or remove flag). Add test asserting prior messages are sent. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:46:| AGT-03 | S3 | spawn_subagent token accounting | agent.ts:5298-5431, 1869, 2863 | RUNTIME (R4): gateway received 4 inference requests, parent `getTokenStats().requests` = 2. `runSubagent` never adds to `totalTokens` and the parent never merges the child's; `recordFindings` adds tokens but not `requests`. | `/tokens`, receipts and cloud spend views under-report delegated work. | Merge child stats into parent; count findings calls. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:48:| AGT-05 | S3 | Duplicated subagent loop | agent.ts:5298-5431 vs 4401-4915 | SOURCE. Second loop diverges: no `refreshCapabilities`/`measureAdmission` (provider token counting, strict counting ignored), no empty-reply retry (first empty reply = \"stopped without a report\"), no backoff for polls, no steering, offers `[...HARNESS_TOOLS, read_findings]` (all tool groups, no MCP/plugin) while parsing against `getEffectiveTools()` names (5362) — offered and accepted tool sets differ; no cancellation-record semantics for in-flight tools. | Behaviour of delegated work differs subtly from main turns; context/strict-count guarantees don't hold inside subagents. | Refactor to one step function shared by both loops (RELEASE-REQUIRED or documented limitation). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:49:| AGT-06 | S4 | spawn_subagent obligation write | agent.ts:3610-3617 vs 3635-3641 | SOURCE. `turnMutations` added twice (try and finally). `this.hasPendingModifications = true` assigned directly, so the later `setUnverifiedChanges(true)` short-circuits (1588) and the immediate durable obligation write is skipped; it is persisted only at the next `persistProgress({messages:true})` (4893). | Small crash window where a subagent's write is not durably an obligation; counter inflation harmless today (only `>0` tested). | Use `setUnverifiedChanges` once; count once. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:81:- Outcome honesty: `buildTurnResult` is the single derivation; invariants forbid VERIFIED/REGRESSION_FREE without PASSED evidence and NOT_REQUIRED with pending changes (turn.ts:318-351). Discovered-verifier passes need fail-before/pass-after independence for VERIFIED (agent.ts:3447, 5136-5145); non-covering passes are REGRESSION_FREE (5126-5135); read-only answers resting on compacted-away output are UNVERIFIED/CONTEXT_EVIDENCE_NOT_RETAINED (5165-5171). `verified` requirements must bind a passing, unfiltered, deliverable-bound, independent run (objective.ts applyRequirementUpdates).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:86:- Steering: queued, applied once at step boundaries, never dropped silently (cancelled + reported), survives restore (1935-1973, 1553-1557).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2.notes.txt:10:[   6.64s] RESIZE 40x14\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2.notes.txt:11:[   7.64s] SCREEN approval-40x14 (40x14)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2.notes.txt:12:[   7.64s] SEND y at 40x14\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py:38:        \"TERM\": \"xterm-256color\", \"COLORTERM\": \"truecolor\", \"LANG\": \"C.UTF-8\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py:84:                chunk = os.read(self.fd, 65536)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s3.screens.txt:2:===== panel-letters @ 5.78s (80x24) =====\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s3.screens.txt:28:===== after-turn @ 11.19s (80x24) =====\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s4a.notes.txt:10:[  15.35s] SEND Esc\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2.screens.txt:98:===== approval-40x14 @ 7.64s (40x14) =====\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:14:  bracketed paste \"y\\ny\\nyes\\n\", unbracketed burst \"yyyyyyyy\\r\\r\\r\", 'y' at 40x14, and a lone 'y' after 2.5s quiet\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:23:  at 80x24. Result banner \"! Done · not verified ... → next: /diff or /test\" (good recovery guidance).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:24:- 40x14: approval hint truncated mid-word (\"…←→ approve/deny, paus\"), footer \"(t…\" — the key instruction is cut.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:36:- Launcher: packaged `bin/nexus` = `node lib/cli/dist/index.js` (scripts/package-linux.sh:25-30); no code path in\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:51:| SEC-03 | S2 | fetch_web (unapproved even in review mode) | tools.ts:52-111, 653-658 | RUNTIME (Repro R4). The SSRF guard is a hostname-string check with no DNS resolution and no redirect control (`fetch` follows redirects). `http://localtest.me:18731/` and `http://[::ffff:127.0.0.1]:18731/` both fetched a loopback-only server. Also not blocked: fd00::/8, fe80::/10, 100.64/10. The response body is read fully before truncation (tools.ts:662). | The model can reach loopback and LAN services (homelab gateway, admin UIs) and exfiltrate data in the URL query. There is no approval prompt, because fetch_web is non-mutating. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: resolve and pin the IP, check every redirect hop (`redirect: \"manual\"`), block all of v4/v6 private, ULA, link-local and mapped ranges, and cap the body size. Consider requiring approval for egress in review mode. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:54:| SEC-06 | S3 | protected paths | security.ts:25-32, 91-108; tools.ts:446-469 | RUNTIME (Repro R2). The name-pattern check misses `.env.local`, `.env.production`, `secrets/.npmrc`, and `.GIT/config` (case-insensitive FS). A symlink to `.env` inside the workspace is not checked. `run_command cat .env` is not checked. `notes.env` is over-blocked. | Protection of `.env`-style secrets is advisory only. | POST-V1 hardening. Document it as advisory. Match `.env*` and canonical target names. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":81184}},"started_at_ms":1792978785966,"completed_at_ms":1792978785967}}
