I-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:189:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:191:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:276:| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:332:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:36:| REQ-AGT-31..39 | CTX-003..011 | Durable vs retrieved distinction; role policy; budget vs actual route capacity, fail closed (`ContextBudgetError`); cross-boundary failover re-admission; same-boundary failover cheap; compaction removes only disposable; admission evidence; resume≠recovery; manual==auto compaction semantics | P2 §12 | DEMONSTRATED / SBIS (CTX-006: client.ts executeWithFailover; egress.test) | P (WP05 qual for CTX-006) | 10-12 I-05 (provider context-length 400 ends turn), CTX-02 (steering truncated after compaction; fixed ee70f68), d88a897 false-absence; 10-13 compaction ledger self-assessed only |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:81:| REQ-DX-01 | Install promise | Linux x86-64 glibc≥2.35, Node≥20; installer verifies SHA-256; no root, no shell rc edits; manual uninstall keeps user data | quickstart.md:7-27,59-68; DEVELOPMENT.md:19 | Published alpha.2 (release run 38539108878) | N |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:128:| HIST-03 | S2 | Extensions, docs truth | docs/USER_MANUAL.md:294; cli/src/plugins.ts:93-96,139-145,256 | SOURCE: manual promises plugin handlers \\\"execute in isolated Node.js worker_threads with strict timeout boundaries and memory caps\\\". Plugins are loaded with in-process `await import()` and custom tools run `handler(args)` directly; `executeSandboxed` has no caller | Users trust untrusted plugins based on a nonexistent sandbox | Fix the manual (or wire the sandbox); RELEASE-REQUIRED doc correction |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:131:| HIST-06 | S3 | Install/positioning docs | docs/USER_MANUAL.md:3,14,19; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:24-25,43; quickstart.md:21-23 | SOURCE/DOC: manual claims \\\"direct parity with OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code\\\"; `harness repl` (installed binary is `nexus`); `nexus --approve` vs quickstart `nexus repl --approve`; ARCHITECTURE names homelab hardware/port 18010 and calls `repl.ts` the TUI; quickstart \\\"install another specific version\\\" example is identical to the pinned command; MCP_GUIDE link is `file:///home/mike/...` | New users get wrong commands and inflated expectations | Reconcile docs to shipped binary (RELEASE-REQUIRED) |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:146:| …3352 tokens truncated…T_RETAINED (5165-5171). `verified` requirements must bind a passing, unfiltered, deliverable-bound, independent run (objective.ts applyRequirementUpdates).\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:86:- Steering: queued, applied once at step boundaries, never dropped silently (cancelled + reported), survives restore (1935-1973, 1553-1557).\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2.notes.txt:10:[   6.64s] RESIZE 40x14\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2.notes.txt:11:[   7.64s] SCREEN approval-40x14 (40x14)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2.notes.txt:12:[   7.64s] SEND y at 40x14\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py:38:        \\\"TERM\\\": \\\"xterm-256color\\\", \\\"COLORTERM\\\": \\\"truecolor\\\", \\\"LANG\\\": \\\"C.UTF-8\\\",\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py:84:                chunk = os.read(self.fd, 65536)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s3.screens.txt:2:===== panel-letters @ 5.78s (80x24) =====\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s3.screens.txt:28:===== after-turn @ 11.19s (80x24) =====\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s4a.notes.txt:10:[  15.35s] SEND Esc\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2.screens.txt:98:===== approval-40x14 @ 7.64s (40x14) =====\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:14:  bracketed paste \\\"y\\\\ny\\\\nyes\\\\n\\\", unbracketed burst \\\"yyyyyyyy\\\\r\\\\r\\\\r\\\", 'y' at 40x14, and a lone 'y' after 2.5s quiet\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:23:  at 80x24. Result banner \\\"! Done · not verified ... → next: /diff or /test\\\" (good recovery guidance).\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:24:- 40x14: approval hint truncated mid-word (\\\"…←→ approve/deny, paus\\\"), footer \\\"(t…\\\" — the key instruction is cut.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:36:- Launcher: packaged `bin/nexus` = `node lib/cli/dist/index.js` (scripts/package-linux.sh:25-30); no code path in\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:51:| SEC-03 | S2 | fetch_web (unapproved even in review mode) | tools.ts:52-111, 653-658 | RUNTIME (Repro R4). The SSRF guard is a hostname-string check with no DNS resolution and no redirect control (`fetch` follows redirects). `http://localtest.me:18731/` and `http://[::ffff:127.0.0.1]:18731/` both fetched a loopback-only server. Also not blocked: fd00::/8, fe80::/10, 100.64/10. The response body is read fully before truncation (tools.ts:662). | The model can reach loopback and LAN services (homelab gateway, admin UIs) and exfiltrate data in the URL query. There is no approval prompt, because fetch_web is non-mutating. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: resolve and pin the IP, check every redirect hop (`redirect: \\\"manual\\\"`), block all of v4/v6 private, ULA, link-local and mapped ranges, and cap the body size. Consider requiring approval for egress in review mode. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:54:| SEC-06 | S3 | protected paths | security.ts:25-32, 91-108; tools.ts:446-469 | RUNTIME (Repro R2). The name-pattern check misses `.env.local`, `.env.production`, `secrets/.npmrc`, and `.GIT/config` (case-insensitive FS). A symlink to `.env` inside the workspace is not checked. `run_command cat .env` is not checked. `notes.env` is over-blocked. | Protection of `.env`-style secrets is advisory only. | POST-V1 hardening. Document it as advisory. Match `.env*` and canonical target names. |\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"result\":{\"chunk_id\":\"099d85\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00005434,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":527,\"output\":\"## v1/readiness-rc7-current-state...origin/v1/readiness-rc7-current-state [ahead 1]\\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\\ne4c70bf docs(release): record RC7 provider and stale PR state\\n6dee7e6 docs(release): reconcile RC7 and post-PR243 status\\nce3c323 docs(release): label prior readiness snapshot superseded\\n{\\n  \\\"agent\\\": \\\"/root\\\",\\n  \\\"host\\\": \\\"mike-dev\\\",\\n  \\\"branch\\\": \\\"v1/rc7-version-bump\\\",\\n  \\\"worktree\\\": \\\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc7-version-bump\\\",\\n  \\\"base\\\": \\\"431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1\\\",\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": \\\"Release publisher owns RC lifecycle and exact-source/artifact acceptance coordination; no held-out access, no stable publication until every release gate passes.\\\",\\n  \\\"pr\\\": 241,\\n  \\\"independent_review\\\": \\\"ACCEPT by rc5_candidate_review at exact base-to-head diff SHA-256 06ac7420c9901f4c9d77367900de7ce3e9b4eae3fa3535144501dd614a71f5a0\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"Main source 0542312 remains CI/CodeQL/requirements PASS. PR #244 is open on exact base 0542312 at remote head 6dee7e6744f21eaf4f25517ca161e05628bdfc81; CodeQL and JS/TS pass, Node22/24 CLI test jobs still running; independent review ACCEPT. Local readiness worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc7-current-state branch v1/readiness-rc7-current-state HEAD e4c70bfea92d1a470344fd9f5d5d9abd3a0bcc71 has one local follow-up commit plus one uns