{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T01:40:17.121Z","ordinal":368121,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adeaf7e5ffc81a08fd93069b0499395","status":"completed","call_id":"call_e3ae05623516405cb1eb91a23f4a927d","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /tmp/nexus-agent-readonly-pr.md <<'EOF'\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Apply the effective read-only posture selected by the launch mode immediately to the bridge, authority admission engine, knowledge graph, and extension managers.\\n- Preserve mode-selected read-only as a deliberate, changeable mode while keeping explicit `--read-only` launches locked.\\n- Port the accepted session recovery regression into the current `durable_continuity.test.ts` suite, since the older test file was removed from current main.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `npm run build` — passed.\\n- `test/experimental_and_readonly.test.ts` — 8/8 passed.\\n- Focused durable session-continuity regression — 1/1 passed.\\n- `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` — passed.\\n- Independent source review — ACCEPT on exact diff SHA-256 `d2d17c7c36072a0c310e998d67df69821007a2085990f84ca9342556610df853`.\\n\\nA broader two-file diagnostic run before building generated CLI artifacts ended with 13 failures, including absent `cli/dist/index.js` and Rust-core daemon disconnections in unrelated durable-continuity fixtures. The targeted tests were rerun after a successful build; repository CI is required for the full exact-head result.\\n\\n## Base\\n\\n`0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2` (`origin/main` at branch creation)\\nEOF\\ngh pr create --base main --head v1/defect-agent-readonly-current --title 'fix: initialize mode-selected read-only posture' --body-file /tmp/nexus-agent-readonly-pr.md\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/agent-readonly-current\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":600});text(JSON.stringify(r));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a175dc-b598-7d13-970c-9