{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T01:43:39.571Z","ordinal":368319,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a175dc-b598-7d13-970c-920bc98c4a88","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9afd1a45-966f-4884-9680-660b2881857e","process_id":"23836","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'openrouter|chatgpt|provider|standalone|live inference|E5|Gateway' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/plans docs/v1.0.0/specs | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -i 'openrouter|chatgpt|provider|standalone|live inference|E5|Gateway' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/plans docs/v1.0.0/specs","query":"openrouter|chatgpt|provider|standalone|live inference|E5|Gateway","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:43:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:46:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:113:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:114:| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:122:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:133:   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:134:4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:135:5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:137:### 4.2 Standalone matrix\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:141:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:149:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:151:| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:153:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:175:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:209:Environment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:307:2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:1:# SPEC-05: Standalone local inference and provider robustness\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:5:| Status | Ready. Provider tiers resolved by [DEC-06](../DECISIONS.md#dec-06-supported-providers-for-v1). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER**: standalone context sizing + live standalone qualification. RELEASE-REQUIRED: error bounding, timeouts, stream fixes, startup diagnosis, docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:9:| Plan | [PLAN-05](../plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:10:| Acceptance | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-10, plus the standalone qualification matrix in ACCEPTANCE §4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:14:Local inference is the product's first-class mode. The quickstart first-run path is LM Studio or vLLM at `localhost:1234`. The code is gateway-optional by design (B §5): `/tokenize`, capacity headers and `limits_version` are all optional and absent-safe. The gaps are below.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:16:### 1.1 No live standalone evidence\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:18:Every live run on record is against the homelab gateway: llama.cpp behind aihost (HIST-08). Local requests are never receipted (`client.ts:561-569`), so there is no machine-readable local evidence (B §6 G1).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:22:Only `context_length` and `max_model_len` are parsed (`core/provider_capabilities.ts:29,72`). LM Studio's and llama.cpp's `/v1/models` do not carry these fields (INFERENCE on server behaviour; verify in G1). On those servers sizing falls back to 65536. If the loaded window is smaller, the first large turn ends with a capacity error and no compaction-and-retry (`agent.ts:4684-4689`; PRV-06). On top of that, llama.cpp's overflow body is classified as REQUEST_REJECTED, not CAPACITY_REJECTED (PRV-07, reproduced).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:36:| PRV-13 | `addFallbackEndpoint` ignores provider pins. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:37:| PRV-14 | A key-less `compatible` provider never appears in the picker. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:43:- **PRV-18.** A custom CA for an HTTPS gateway is undocumented, so users will reach for `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:59:3. **REQ-PRV-103.** Every provider/endpoint error string is bounded (≤ 2000 chars) and redacted on every path: inference, listModels, embeddings, tokenize, OAuth.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:68:6. **REQ-PRV-106.** **Standalone qualification** (DEC-16; the environment provides no inference path except the gateway).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:69:   - **(a) Live:** Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration, through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`. The proxy strips every gateway extension and, in a second profile, emulates the llama.cpp, vLLM and Ollama `/models` and overflow shapes. In both profiles, Nexus passes the standalone T2 subset and the T4 subset at the ACCEPTANCE §4.2 threshold, and turns are recorded with receipts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:74:   - the gateway token path becomes configurable (`NEXUS_GATEWAY_TOKEN_FILE`), with the homelab path read only if explicitly configured;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:75:   - `X-Task-Class` is sent only to origins that advertise support (gateway capability) or when configured;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:82:- **Discovery.** Add a `ServerKind` probe in `provider_capabilities.ts`: `gateway | vllm | llamacpp | lmstudio | ollama | unknown`. It inspects the `/models` response shape, and the `/props`, `/api/v0/models` and `/api/version` endpoints. Each probe has a timeout of 2 s and is cached per endpoint per session. Report the kind and the context source in `/status` and in doctor.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:84:- **Error bounding.** A single `boundedProviderText(body)` is used at `client.ts:903,1636,1689`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:86:- **Never-reachable bound.** In `provider_recovery.ts`, add a `everSucceeded` flag per endpoint per session. When it is false, the deadline is `NEXUS_FIRST_CONTACT_DEADLINE_MS` (default 120000).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:106:| ACC-INF-10 | ACCEPTANCE §4.2 passes: the live stripped-proxy profiles (plain, plus emulated llama.cpp/vLLM/Ollama shapes) on the standalone T2 and T4 subsets, and server-kind conformance fixtures in CI. Receipts are archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:110:- DEC-06 (resolved) sets the provider tiers.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:112:- SPEC-10 provides the standalone task set and runner.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:1:# PLAN-05: Standalone local inference and provider robustness\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:3:Implements [SPEC-05](../specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md). Milestone **M3**. Code tasks run in M3; live qualification runs in M5.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:10:- `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:11:- `cli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:14:- `cli/src/providers.ts`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:26:| 1 | `ServerKind` probe (gateway / vllm / llamacpp / lmstudio / ollama / unknown). Context discovery through `/props`, `/api/v0/models` and `/api/show`, with 2 s timeouts, cached per endpoint. Source label shown in `/status` and doctor. | `provider_capabilities.ts:29,72,184-195`; `client.ts:939-977` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:27:| 2 | Capacity rules cover llama.cpp (`exceed_context_size_error`), LM Studio and Ollama bodies. Build the table test from recorded bodies. | `provider_recovery.ts:82,106` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:29:| 4 | `boundedProviderText` on every error path (inference, listModels, embeddings, tokenize, OAuth). | `client.ts:903,1636,1689`; `oauth.ts` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:30:| 5 | First-byte, idle and total timeouts with a watchdog. Default total timeout is 0 for local endpoints and 900 s for cloud. At most one replay of a timed-out generation, visible to the user. Timeouts on listModels, catalog, embeddings and tokenize. Embeddings are disabled for the session after a 404 or 501. | `client.ts:744-747,890-913,1627-1630,1676`; `embeddings.ts:299-305`; `model_catalog.ts:93-100`; `provider_recovery.ts:331-337` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:32:| 7 | Server-kind conformance fixtures, built from each project's published API docs with version and source references recorded: llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama. Covers `/models`/`/props`/`/api/v0/models`/`/api/show` shapes, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies. Also record real SSE through the gateway (llama.cpp workers) with `scripts/record_sse.mjs`. Add a replay test. | `cli/test/fixtures/sse/<server>/<case>.sse`; `inference_transport.test.ts` | — (no extra hardware; DEC-16) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:35:| 10 | Startup endpoint probe (3 s) in the TUI and REPL, with the startup message and fix hint. In `ProviderRecoveryController`, the first-contact deadline (`everSucceeded=false`) defaults to 120 s. | `sidecar.ts` session start; `repl.ts` banner; `protocol.ts:306-325` notice text; `provider_recovery.ts` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:36:| 11 | Remove homelab coupling: `NEXUS_GATEWAY_TOKEN_FILE` replaces the hardcoded token path; send `X-Task-Class` only when the gateway capability is advertised or configured; neutral doc examples. | `client.ts:63-69,644-647,947`; `providers.ts:161`; `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`; `ARCHITECTURE.md` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:38:| 13 | Small fixes: egress denial throws `InferenceError(\"policy_denied\")` (PRV-12); `addFallbackEndpoint` uses `normalizeEp` and checks pins (PRV-13); key-less `compatible` provider listed (PRV-14); Responses `incomplete` reasons mapped (PRV-16). | `client.ts:785-793,865,1091-1113,1226-1229,1490-1494`; `model_catalog.ts:128-136,170`; `protocols/openai_responses.ts:108` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:39:| 14 | Docs: standalone setup per server kind (LM Studio, llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama), with how context is discovered and how to override it. | `quickstart.md`, `USER_MANUAL.md`, new `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md` | 1,12 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:45:| PR-5a | 1, 2, 3 | Standalone context sizing (blocker core) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:54:- **Context discovery:** `provider_capabilities.test.ts` gets a fixture per server-kind response shape (ACC-INF-01).\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:55:- **Capacity:** `provider_recovery.test.ts` gets a table of recorded capacity bodies (ACC-INF-02). `provider_recovery_agent.test.ts` covers compact-and-retry once.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:63:There is no inference path except the gateway (DEC-16):\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:65:1. Record real SSE through the gateway (llama.cpp-served models): `node scripts/record_sse.mjs --endpoint <gateway> --case {text,tool,parallel_tools,think,overflow}`. The script is new: a thin `fetch` that tees the body to a file. Commit the redacted files.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:71:The matrix in ACCEPTANCE §4.2, run through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` (PLAN-10 task 13) in both profiles: plain, and emulated server shapes. Archive receipts, transcripts and `/status` output per profile under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/standalone/`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:45:2. **REQ-REL-102.** Every `nexus …` command line in README.md, quickstart.md, docs/USER_MANUAL.md, docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md and docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md parses on the packaged install. \"Parses\" means `--help`, or a dry-safe invocation, exits without \"unknown option/command\". This is enforced in CI.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:49:| AGT-03 | Subagent and findings-distillation inference is not counted in token/request stats. Reproduced: 4 gateway requests, stats showed 2. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:144:| ACC-CONT-01 | Gateway fixture: the second request of `run --resume <id>` contains the first turn's messages, and `result.taskId` equals the recovered id. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:148:| ACC-CONT-05 | R4 reproduction: parent `requests` equals gateway requests, and the task file count increases by 1 only. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:18:`parser.ts:382-434` executes any JSON object in the reply text whose `name`, `tool` or `action` is an offered tool. This happens even when the provider supports native tool calls. Reproduced cases:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:80:| Parser | `parseModelResponse(reply, { nativeTools: boolean })`. The capability comes from the provider protocol: Responses, Anthropic and Chat Completions with `tools` accepted are native. Steps 4–5 run only when `!nativeTools` and are restricted as in REQ-AGT-112. The reasoning stripper handles the lone-close and unclosed-open cases. Remove the `json {\"tool\":…}` exemplars from `fewshots.ts` for native connections. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:33:The deadline recorded in the contest docs is 2026-10-14. The owner confirmed the submission is complete; operator work state records submission id `e05006b6-…` at revision `ce7e58b9`. Contest submission readiness is therefore **closed as submitted**. The findings below describe the state of the submitted tree: reproducibility of the submission is limited to the operator host (CON-002, CON-005). They are a hardening backlog, not a submission gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:75:- **Live (M5):** one standalone session per server kind verifies the banner and the first-verifier approval.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:50:4. **REQ-DX-105.** User-facing docs (README, quickstart, USER_MANUAL, CLIENT_GUIDE, ARCHITECTURE, CLOUD_PROVIDERS, MCP_GUIDE, SKILLS_AND_PLUGINS, DOCTOR_TROUBLESHOOTING):\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:76:| `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md` | Use neutral examples. Correct the redaction and catalog claims. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:19:| 5 | Remove the parity claim, homelab identifiers, and the `file:///` link. Correct the ARCHITECTURE controls-and-limits section. | `USER_MANUAL.md:3`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `MCP_GUIDE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md` | M0 (cheap, standalone) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:168:| ACC-SAFE-01 | Fresh HOME, `nexus` (TUI) and `nexus repl`, mock gateway scripted to call `run_command \"echo x > ../outside\"`: in an untrusted workspace the call is not executed without an approval panel. After `nexus trust .` it runs without a panel (DEC-01 option C). | PTY |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:34:| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (8×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:35:| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:44:- **PR-10e:** task 13 (standalone proxy).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:37:Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal coverage (kitty, tmux, VS Code, xterm) is not established. pyte emulation cannot answer kitty keyboard queries (D §6).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:65:   1. gateway refuses connections mid-turn;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:82:7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:111:- Hardware: the homelab inference host, reached through its gateway only, is the sole inference path (DEC-16). Every agent's runs are serial on it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:18:| Workspace `.env` | Loaded with `override:true` and no key filter (`cli/src/config.ts:36-39`). `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0` from a repo disables TLS verification for every later fetch, including cloud API keys. Reproduced. It can also set timeouts, recovery policy, `LOCAL_LLM_FALLBACK_ENDPOINTS` and provider key vars, because `credentials.ts:243` reads live env. | PRV-01 (S2) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:67:Replace every `process.env.X` read in `client.ts`, `credentials.ts`, `config.ts` and `provider_recovery.ts` with `effective.get(\"X\")`. `grep -n \"process.env\" cli/src` gives the inventory. The credential-authority snapshot that already exists (`client.ts:77-101`) becomes the `operator*` layer.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:117:| Stop loading the project `.env` entirely | Breaks the documented per-project endpoint/model workflow (CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md). An allowlist keeps it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:127:| ACC-TRUST-04 | Untrusted fixture repo with `skills/x/SKILL.md` and `.nexus/knowledge.json`: neither appears in the system prompt sent to the mock gateway. After `nexus trust .` both appear, with a source annotation. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:13:- `cli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts` (env reads)\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:29:| 2 | Inventory every `process.env.` read (`grep -rn \"process.env\" cli/src`). Route Nexus keys through `EffectiveConfig`, and leave genuine OS keys (HOME, PATH) on the operator env. | `client.ts`, `credentials.ts`, `provider_recovery.ts`, `config.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts` | 1 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:38:| 11 | Docs: CLOUD_PROVIDERS (authority, locality, `NEXUS_LOCAL_ORIGINS`), USER_MANUAL §4 (trust covers skills and knowledge; plugin trust model; directories), release notes (migration of project `.env` keys). | docs | all |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":35022}},"started_at_ms":1792979019571,"completed_at_ms":1792979019571}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T01:43:40.510Z","ordinal":368320,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a175e0-aade-7c72-8b5a-63824e95e63c","call_id":"call_017720a3d3bc455b9c14fd5a9150ca78","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5485)\nTotal output lines: 93\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:43:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:46:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:113:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:114:| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:122:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:133:   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:134:4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:135:5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:137:### 4.2 Standalone matrix\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:141:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:149:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:151:| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:153:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:175:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:209:Environment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:307:2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:1:# SPEC-05: Standalone…3485 tokens truncated…NCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:35:| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:44:- **PR-10e:** task 13 (standalone proxy).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:37:Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal coverage (kitty, tmux, VS Code, xterm) is not established. pyte emulation cannot answer kitty keyboard queries (D §6).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:65:   1. gateway refuses connections mid-turn;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:82:7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) i