: direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-83-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-84-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-85-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-86-Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-87-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-88-| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-89-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-90-| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-91-| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-92-| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-93-| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-94-| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-109-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-110-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-111-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-112-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:113:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-114-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-115-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-116-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-117-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-118-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-119-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-120-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-121-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-122-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-123-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-124-### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-125-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-147-ACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-148-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-149-### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-150-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:151:| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-152-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:153:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-155-| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-156-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-157-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-158-## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-159-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-160-### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-161-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-162-These must pass:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-163-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-164-- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-165-- `tui_diff_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-166-- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-337-- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-338-  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-339-  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-340-- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-342-- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-343-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-344-After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-345-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-346-**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-10-| [DEC-02](#dec-02-role-of-the-repl) | Role of the REPL | Supported secondary surface; TUI primary; top-level flags implemented | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-11-| [DEC-03](#dec-03-team-and-operation-scope-in-v1) | `/team` and `nexus operation` in v1 | Shipped as **experimental**; data-loss fix still a blocker | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-12-| [DEC-04](#dec-04-issue-12-open-normative-blockers) | Issue #12 open blockers | EXT-004 implemented; CTX-001 partially implemented; CTX-002 descoped post-v1 | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-13-| [DEC-05](#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds) | Evaluation protocol and thresholds | 40 held-out T2 tasks, 5 runs, 2 peers, thresholds below | Needs an external author (see actions) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:14:| [DEC-06](#dec-06-supported-providers-for-v1) | Supported providers | Local OpenAI-compatible + OpenRouter supported; others experimental until live-verified | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-15-| [DEC-07](#dec-07-experimental-surfaces-nexus-eval-tdd-team-roles) | `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles | eval and tdd experimental; eval's workspace mutation fixed; role tool sets enforced | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-16-| [DEC-08](#dec-08-version-identity-and-stale-v1x-tags) | Version identity, stale v1.x tags | `package.json` is the source of truth; local v1.x tags deleted (owner action) | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-17-| [DEC-09](#dec-09-release-provenance-mechanism) | Release provenance | GitHub artifact attestations | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-18-| [DEC-10](#dec-10-tracking-of-clidist) | Tracking of `cli/dist` | Untrack | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-19-| [DEC-11](#dec-11-retention-defaults) | Retention defaults | 90 days / 2 GB; audit log 10 MB × 5; first GC needs acknowledgement | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-20-| [DEC-12](#dec-12-platform-scope) | Platform scope | Linux x86-64 glibc only for v1.0.0 | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-21-| [DEC-13](#dec-13-contest-track-disposition) | Contest track | Submission already completed; it is frozen until judging ends, then PLAN-C1 runs as post-contest hardening | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-22-| [DEC-14](#dec-14-free-text-on-the-command-line) | Free text on the command line | Explicit `nexus run` required | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-23-| [DEC-15](#dec-15-knowledge-auto-extraction) | Knowledge auto-extraction | Off by default, opt-in | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-24-| [DEC-16](#dec-16-standalone-qualification-under-a-gateway-only-environment) | Standalone qualification with no direct worker access | Stripping proxy over the gateway for live runs, plus server-kind conformance fixtures | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-25-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-26----\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-100-| `run`-mode operator interventions | 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-101-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-102-**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-103-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:104:**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-105-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-106-**Rationale.** These figures are the pilot's pre-registered thresholds (eval/README), tightened where the pilot showed weakness: false VERIFIED, crash accounting. The absolute floor prevents \"beat a weak peer\" from passing. Thresholds are fixed **before** the RC run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-107-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:108:## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-109-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-110-| Tier | Providers | Condition |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-111-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-112-| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-113-| **Supported (optional integration)** | homelab-ai gateway | Never required (standalone gate). |\nCLOUD <unclaimed>\nGATEWAY <unclaimed>\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":72019}},"started_at_ms":1792979028986,"completed_at_ms":1792979028986}}
