 already completed; it is frozen until judging ends, then PLAN-C1 runs as post-contest hardening | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-22-| [DEC-14](#dec-14-free-text-on-the-command-line) | Free text on the command line | Explicit `nexus run` required | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-23-| [DEC-15](#dec-15-knowledge-auto-extraction) | Knowledge auto-extraction | Off by default, opt-in | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-24-| [DEC-16](#dec-16-standalone-qualification-under-a-gateway-only-environment) | Standalone qualification with no direct worker access | Stripping proxy over the gateway for live runs, plus server-kind conformance fixtures | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-25-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-26----\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-100-| `run`-mode operator interventions | 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-101-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-102-**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-103-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:104:**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-105-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-106-**Rationale.** These figures are the pilot's pre-registered thresholds (eval/README), tightened where the pilot showed weakness: false VERIFIED, crash accounting. The absolute floor prevents \"beat a weak peer\" from passing. Thresholds are fixed **before** the RC run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-107-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:108:## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-109-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-110-| Tier | Providers | Condition |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-111-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-112-| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-113-| **Supported (optional integration)** | homelab-ai gateway | Never required (standalone gate). |\nCLOUD <unclaimed>\nGATEWAY <unclaimed>\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a175dc-b598-7d13-970c-920bc98c4a88","create_time":1792979029.9868565}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
