{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T01:49:18.411Z","ordinal":368633,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a175e5-d2cb-74d0-b48b-772ef7c7de83","call_id":"call_6695e2991b9e419290d75fed08de83f4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 16226)\nTotal output lines: 223\n\nEVIDENCE.md\nREADINESS.md\nREQUIREMENTS.md\n# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 00:58 UTC at `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`)\n\n**Release state:** GitHub published signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7`; signed tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) succeeded. The published Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`; `SHA256SUMS` SHA-256 is `7b8a5fd1d214919ae939275e59b76406d393fae31cdf4b184c33883b02dc64a9`. RC7 is an unaccepted prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is not published.\n\n**Exact `main` source gates:** `origin/main` is `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, merging PR #243's checkpoint index-lock diagnostic fix. Exact-main CI [40248550055](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248550055) and CodeQL [40248550144](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248550144) both passed on that SHA. A clean detached checkout with isolated HOME/XDG passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals. The PR #243 diff SHA-256 `fb6b7d5d81d66cb237799b4d7a41c3dfd59f931eeaa84e75117a38bf9fc97928` matched its independently accepted diff exactly. RC7 predates this merge and cannot qualify the updated source.\n\n**RC7 artifact evidence:** The tag's release workflow produced the public assets and attestations. `gh attestation verify` passed for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS` under the exact repository, workflow, tag, and source constraints; the checksum-index attestation is [59728626](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/attestations/59728626). Cross-runner workflow [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Both manifests validated, and the archive, checksum manifest, notices, compatibility file, installer, and CycloneDX SBOM matched byte-for-byte across the two runner outputs and the public release. An isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)`. These are artifact and installation checks, not product qualification.\n\n**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest comment is coordinator-authored at 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible held-out corpus disposition. Held-out T2 has not started, and no private payload was accessed. Provider/standalone qualification and T3/T4 evidence remain incomplete. The five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15, with no per-cell verdicts or required screenshots. The `cli/src/agent.ts` remediation handoff remains with KimiCode-defect-scan; implementation is still pending in that claimed lane.\n\n**Disposition:** Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is not accepted and no stable release is claimed. The next release candidate must include the merged checkpoint fix, pass exact-source CI and qualification gates, and be installed and identified before product qualification. Remaining gates include independent held-out custody and T2, provider/standalone behavior, T3/T4, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted once every required gate passes.\n\n## Superseded release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-25 23:43 UTC at `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`)\n\n## Earlier release checkpoint (superseded; observed 2026-10-25 23:43 UTC at `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`)\n\n**Release state:** GitHub lists `v1.0.0-rc.6` as the latest published prerelease. Signed tag `v1.0.0-rc.7` (tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824`) now points to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`; Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) is in progress. GitHub has not published an RC7 release or assets yet. RC6 is not an accepted RC, and no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed.\n\n**Exact `main` source gates:** Current `origin/main` is `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Post-merge CodeQL run [40243331241](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331241) passed on this exact SHA. Post-merge CI run [40243331324](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331324) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility, SBOM, smoke, and installer checks passed. At this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed…13826 tokens truncated…tes, deterministic double-build packaging, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke). Source CI is green; installed-RC product qualification has not yet executed.\n- **Sealed held-out T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`, PR [#16](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/16), merged at `f776903`):**\n  - Committed public manifest: `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`), containing 40 external-repository T2 tasks pinned to full 40-hex baseline commits across Go (10), JavaScript (10), Python (10), and Rust (10), and across bugfix (10), debug (10), feature (10), and refactor (10).\n  - Custody record: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` (updated at `ce3f590`).\n  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n- **Evaluator isolation and kernel resource contract (PRs [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), [#18](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/18), [#19](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/19)):**\n  - `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10) runs private oracle checks outside the candidate workspace while mounting the candidate workspace read-only (`--ro-bind`), superseding the historical shared-workspace oracle exposure noted in the 2026-10-17 review below.\n  - Repository workspace history isolation (`96aeef2`, PR #18, `eval/workspace.mjs`) stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`) without `--shared`, `objects/info/alternates`, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits, preventing candidates from reading upstream fix commits in git history.\n  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\n- **Governance, tokenizer, and acceptance lifecycle reconciliations (PRs [#11](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/11)–[#15](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/15), [#17](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/17)):**\n  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\n  - `DEC-17` (`f771a3c`, PR #11), `REQ-AGT-118` reconciliation (`d2c4bfc`, PR #12), and published independent review records (`19dedc6`, PR #14; `f8e19e4`, PR #15; `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/`) resolve the CJK/Hangul admission-safety floor vs `≤ 1.5×` accuracy band conflict: the `≥ 1` token/character safety floor takes precedence, `≤ 1.5×` applies to corpora not dominated by the floor, and recorded Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) exceptions remain preserved. `REQ-AGT-118` is `tested` at the source level (`tokens.test.ts` 3/3 pass); this does not claim installed-RC product qualification.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a175dc-b598-7d13-970c-920bc98c4a88","create_time":1792979358.4113739}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
