failed export ended `status=failed` with `CONTEXT_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED` at step 36: `54582+8192+4096>65536`; it had 99 requests, 203 archived records, and 16 findings. This is evidence of context admission exhaustion, not of the speculative test/SSE causes asserted during the run. [Task 1]\n    77\t- `make test` runs Rust tests, `npm --prefix cli test`, then `bash scripts/security_gates.sh`. A timeout establishes only that the command exceeded its deadline; record command, deadline, exit status, and partial output, then run focused checks before diagnosing a failing/stalled test. [Task 1]\n    78\t- `cli/src/agent.ts` now states that `maxSteps` is per-segment, prioritizes direct status questions, and requires evidence-bounded timeout diagnosis. `cli/test/agent_prompt.test.ts` covers these rules; the 310-write continuity regression completed step 311 over 11 segments without a runtime exhaustion notice. [Task 2]\n    79\t\n    80\t## Failures and how to do differently\n    81\t\n    82\t- Symptom: truncated output or a timeout is reported as a specific root cause. Cause: observation was conflated with causal diagnosis. Fix: report the execution evidence separately and verify the suspected check directly before editing. [Task 1]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":26018}},"started_at_ms":1792979495837,"completed_at_ms":1792979495837}}
