{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:02:37.687Z","ordinal":369284,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a175f0-a051-7293-adf5-5b3650d75759","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7415cbd9-3b5f-4529-899d-aac3dabcd9fc","process_id":"12302","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -C 5 'standalone|OpenRouter|ChatGPT|provider verify|small live|bugfix' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -C 5 'standalone|OpenRouter|ChatGPT|provider verify|small live|bugfix' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","query":"standalone|OpenRouter|ChatGPT|provider verify|small live|bugfix","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"38-\n39-| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n40-|---|---|---|\n41-| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n42-| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n43:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n44-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n45-| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n46-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n47-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n48-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n49:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n51-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n52-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n53-\n54-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n--\n76-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n77-|---|---|---|\n78-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 20, 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n79-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20 and Node 22. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n80-| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n81:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n82:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n83-\n84-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n85-\n86-Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n87-\n--\n129-   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n130-   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n131-   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n132-\n133-   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n134:4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n135-5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n136-\n137-### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n138-\n139-| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n--\n148-\n149-### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n150-\n151-| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n152-|---|---|---|\n153:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n154:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n155-| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n156-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n157-\n158-## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n159-\n--\n251-\n252-| Metric | Gate |\n253-|---|---|\n254-| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n255-| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n256:| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n257-| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n258-| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n259-| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n260-| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n261-| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n--\n326-\n327-G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n328-\n329-- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n330-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n331:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n332-- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\n333-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n334-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n335-- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n336-- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n337-- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n338-  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\n339-  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n340-- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\n341:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n342-- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\n343-\n344-After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\n345-\n346-**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":25958}},"started_at_ms":1792980157686,"completed_at_ms":1792980157686}}
