{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:02:54.260Z","ordinal":369300,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a175f0-a051-7293-adf5-5b3650d75759","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dcd60805-b08a-43bd-b091-6f0ec4b4ba75","process_id":"25474","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -A8 -B2 'DEC-16|E4|Homelab-ai' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; rg --files eval/standalone | sort"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -A8 -B2 'DEC-16|E4|Homelab-ai' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","query":"DEC-16|E4|Homelab-ai","path":"DECISIONS.md"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"rg --files eval/standalone","path":"standalone"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-79-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20 and Node 22. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-80-| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-82-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-83-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-84-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-85-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-86-Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-87-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-88-| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-89-|---|---|---|\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-145-| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-146-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:147:ACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-148-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-149-### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-150-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-151-| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-152-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-153-| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-154-| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-155-| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-207-## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-208-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:209:Environment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-210-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-211-### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-212-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-213-- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-214-- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-215-- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-216-- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-217-- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-339-  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-340-- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-342-- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-343-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-344-After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-345-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-346-**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-22-| [DEC-14](#dec-14-free-text-on-the-command-line) | Free text on the command line | Explicit `nexus run` required | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-23-| [DEC-15](#dec-15-knowledge-auto-extraction) | Knowledge auto-extraction | Off by default, opt-in | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:24:| [DEC-16](#dec-16-standalone-qualification-under-a-gateway-only-environment) | Standalone qualification with no direct worker access | Stripping proxy over the gateway for live runs, plus server-kind conformance fixtures | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-25-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-26----\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-27-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-28-## DEC-01: Default execution posture\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-29-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-30-**Question.** What protects the user by default from model-initiated command execution and network egress? See SEC-01, VER-01, HIST-05 and TUI-07.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-31-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-32-| Option | Description | Tradeoffs |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-174----\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-175-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:176:## DEC-16: Standalone qualification under a gateway-only environment\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-177-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-178-**Constraint (owner, 2026-10-14):** there is no separately accessible worker and no extra GPU. Gateway access to the workers must be sufficient, and direct workload requests to workers are not allowed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-179-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-180-**Options:**\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-181-\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-182-| Option | Description | Assessment |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-183-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-184-| A | Require a second GPU host running plain servers | Not available. Rejected. |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-212-| X1 | ~~`git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`~~ **Done by the owner on 2026-10-14.** Verified: `git tag -l` now lists only `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`. | DEC-08 | Done |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-213-| X2 | ~~Provide an independent task author~~. **Resolved 2026-10-14:** agent authorship authorized for T2 (DEC-05). Remaining action: approve the T3 task author (agent authorship is assumed to extend to T3 unless the owner objects). | DEC-05 | Before M5 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:214:| X3 | ~~Separate standalone host~~. **Withdrawn:** no worker or GPU is available apart from the gateway. Replaced by DEC-16 (stripping proxy plus conformance fixtures). Remaining action: none. Optional: approve a CPU-only llama.cpp container on the dev box for the protocol smoke test. | DEC-16 | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-215-| X4 | **Partly resolved 2026-10-14:** the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections are authorized for small-spend checks; both were live-verified at db1ca55. Optional: add OpenAI API-key or Anthropic keys if those providers should be listed as supported. | DEC-06 | M5 (optional) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-216-| X5 | Independent reviewer for continuity/compaction acceptance and RC acceptance | REQ-AGT-110, ACCEPTANCE §8 | M5/M6 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-217-| X6 | After judging: provide a clean Cloudflare account and VM for CON-106. During judging: check whether contest rules permit an erratum (default: no change) | DEC-13 | Post-contest |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-218-| X7 | Approve publishing `v1.0.0-rc.N` and `v1.0.0` (tag push triggers public release) | Release | M6 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md-219-| X8 | Decide whether to clean the 52k test-polluted records in the real `~/.nexus/tasks` (PER-03). Safe to remove: `task-*.json` whose `workspacePath` starts with `/tmp/nexus-app-test-`. | Hygiene | Any time |\nrg: eval/standalone: IO error for operation on eval/standalone: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":44945}},"started_at_ms":1792980174260,"completed_at_ms":1792980174260}}
