{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:03:04.291Z","ordinal":369309,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a175f0-a051-7293-adf5-5b3650d75759","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a94d67aa-cd05-466e-8f54-68d813f221db","process_id":"13608","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '125,178p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md; git ls-tree --name-only origin/main | rg '^(eval|experiments|docs)$'; git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main | rg '^eval/standalone/' | head -n 20"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc7-checkpoint","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '125,178p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md; git ls-tree --name-only origin/main | rg '^(eval|experiments|docs)$'; git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main | rg '^eval/standalone/' | head -n 20"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"\n## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n\n- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\n- **`/tdd` / `--tdd`.** Labelled experimental. Fixing the phase enforcement is post-v1.\n- **Team roles.** Reviewer and researcher units run with a **read-only tool set** (cheap and safety-relevant). Other role allowlists are post-v1.\n\n## DEC-08: Version identity and stale v1.x tags\n\n- `package.json` is the single source of truth. `scripts/sync-version.mjs` updates `cli/package.json` and `core/Cargo.toml`. Release CI asserts that all three equal the tag.\n- Release line: `v1.0.0-rc.N` prereleases, then `v1.0.0`.\n- The local-only tags `v1.1.0`, `v1.2.0` and `v1.2.1` are to be **deleted locally**: `git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`. The owner confirmed on 2026-10-14 that they never existed on the remote, and the audit's `git ls-remote --tags origin` agrees. They are not ancestors of main. Their impact is local only. They sort above v1.0.0 and would confuse `git describe` and the tooling. This is an owner action (see the last section) because it removes local references.\n\n## DEC-09: Release provenance mechanism\n\n**Chosen:** GitHub artifact attestations (`actions/attest-build-provenance`). Users verify with `gh attestation verify`. SHA256SUMS is kept. There is no separate GPG or minisign key to manage.\n\n**Tradeoff:** verification needs the `gh` CLI or the Sigstore tooling. The installer verifies only when `gh` is present, and checksums are always verified.\n\n## DEC-10: Tracking of `cli/dist`\n\n**Chosen:** stop tracking `cli/dist`. Remove it from git, add it to `.gitignore`, and build it in CI and packaging. Checkout users already need `make build` for the Rust binaries.\n\n**Tradeoff:** a fresh clone needs one build step for the TS side too; the docs already state `make build`.\n\n## DEC-11: Retention defaults\n\n**Chosen:**\n- Keep tasks, sessions, checkpoints and flights for 90 days or up to 2 GB in total, whichever limit is hit first. Never remove the current session or pinned sessions.\n- Rotate `audit.log` at 10 MB, keeping 5 files.\n- Automatic GC runs at most daily. The first run after upgrade needs acknowledgement, or `NEXUS_GC=auto`.\n\n## DEC-12: Platform scope\n\n**Chosen:** Linux x86-64, glibc ≥ 2.35, Node ≥ 22 for v1.0.0. The owner selected Node 22 as the minimum on 2026-10-22 because Node 20 reached end of life on 2026-04-30; v1.0.0 must not require or build on an end-of-life Node runtime. Validate Node 22 and 24 in the source CI matrix, with release and reproducibility builds on Node 22. The docs keep the conservative glibc \"≥ 2.35\" claim; the binaries reference glibc symbols ≤ 2.34. macOS, arm64 and musl are post-v1 roadmap items.\n\nThis supersedes the earlier Node ≥ 20 decision. The immutable `v1.0.0-rc.2` tag targets `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`, whose package engine and workflows still use Node 20; that tag is not a qualifying RC under this decision.\n\n## DEC-13: Contest track disposition\n\n**Context:** the owner confirmed on 2026-10-14 that the contest entry submission is complete. Operator work state records submission id `e05006b6-…` at revision `ce7e58b9ca3f…`.\n\n**Chosen:**\n- The contest is a separate track (SPEC-C1). It never gates the client.\n- **Historical freeze (ended):** while judging was open, the submitted material (contest docs, `experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/`, `demo/`, contest CI job) was not changed because post-deadline edits could have been read as amending the entry. The audit findings CON-001 to CON-014 were recorded during that period.\n- After judging concluded, PLAN-C1 proceeded as **post-contest hardening**. Its first task is the CON-001 correction, with a dated \"post-submission correction\" note in CONTEST.md.\n- During that historical freeze, one exception was considered: if contest rules permitted errata, an erratum could state that the documented deploy builds the legacy Experiment-1 Worker and reproduction is operator-host only. That restriction ended with judging; it does not limit current maintenance.\n- Client work that touched `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs` (PLAN-01 task 8, `--yes`) was deferred while judging was open. That deferral has ended; update the demo alongside the client where needed. The runner may continue to pass `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` when required by the current CLI contract.\n\n**Tradeoff:** judges who follow the documented deploy may deploy the legacy Worker. That Worker deploys into their own account, so the exposure is confined to their own test deployment.\n\n**Status amendment (2026-10-21):** The contest has concluded. The release coordinator confirmed that no contest freeze applies. The historical freeze above is no longer a restriction; PLAN-C1 and other contest-related maintenance may proceed through normal claims, review, and validation. Preserve submitted tags, run records, and manifests as historical evidence, and do not represent changed current sources as the original submission. The retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` check remains retired and must not be reintroduced as a release gate.\n\n## DEC-14: Free text on the command line\ndocs\neval\nexperiments\neval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":703069973}},"started_at_ms":1792980183584,"completed_at_ms":1792980184288}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:03:05.265Z","ordinal":369310,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a175f2-70b1-7c71-bdd1-d89c05c24b2a","call_id":"call_748e0f8226dc48e9a282622ae10b95f3","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1355)\nTotal output lines: 58\n\n\n## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n\n- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\n- **`/tdd` / `--tdd`.** Labelled experimental. Fixing the phase enforcement is post-v1.\n- **Team roles.** Reviewer and researcher units run with a **read-only tool set** (cheap and safety-relevant). Other role allowlists are post-v1.\n\n## DEC-08: Version identity and stale v1.x tags\n\n- `package.json` is the single source of truth. `scripts/sync-version.mjs` updates `cli/package.json` and `core/Cargo.toml`. Release CI asserts that all three equal the tag.\n- Release line: `v1.0.0-rc.N` prereleases, then `v1.0.0`.\n- The local-only tags `v1.1.0`, `v1.2.0` and `v1.2.1` are to be **deleted locally**: `git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`. The owner confirmed on 2026-10-14 that they never existed on the remote, and the audit's `git ls-remote --tags origin` agrees. They are not ancestors of main. Their impact is local only. They sort above v1.0.0 and would confuse `git describe` and the tooling. This is an owner action (see the last section) because it removes local references.\n\n## DEC-09: Release provenance mechanism\n\n**Chosen:** GitHub artifact attestations (`actions/attest-build-provenance`). Users verify with `gh attestation verify`. SHA256SUMS is kept. There is no separate GPG or minisign key to manage.\n\n**Tradeoff:** verification needs the `gh` CLI or the Sigstore tooling. The installer verifies only when `gh` is present, and checksums are always verified.\n\n## DEC-10: Tracking of `cli/dist`\n\n**Chosen:** stop tracking `cli/dist`. Remove it from git, add it to `.gitignore`, and build it in CI and packaging. Checkout users already need `make build` for the Rust binaries.\n\n**Tradeoff:** a fresh clone needs one build step for the TS side too…355 tokens truncated…parate track (SPEC-C1). It never gates the client.\n- **Historical freeze (ended):** while judging was open, the submitted material (contest docs, `experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/`, `demo/`, contest CI job) was not changed because post-deadline edits could have been read as amending the entry. The audit findings CON-001 to CON-014 were recorded during that period.\n- After judging concluded, PLAN-C1 proceeded as **post-contest hardening**. Its first task is the CON-001 correction, with a dated \"post-submission correction\" note in CONTEST.md.\n- During that historical freeze, one exception was considered: if contest rules permitted errata, an erratum could state that the documented deploy builds the legacy Experiment-1 Worker and reproduction is operator-host only. That restriction ended with judging; it does not limit current maintenance.\n- Client work that touched `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs` (PLAN-01 task 8, `--yes`) was deferred while judging was open. That deferral has ended; update the demo alongside the client where needed. The runner may continue to pass `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` when required by the current CLI contract.\n\n**Tradeoff:** judges who follow the documented deploy may deploy the legacy Worker. That Worker deploys into their own account, so the exposure is confined to their own test deployment.\n\n**Status amendment (2026-10-21):** The contest has concluded. The release coordinator confirmed that no contest freeze applies. The historical freeze above is no longer a restriction; PLAN-C1 and other contest-related maintenance may proceed through normal claims, review, and validation. Preserve submitted tags, run records, and manifests as historical evidence, and do not represent changed current sources as the original submission. The retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` check remains retired and must not be reintroduced as a release gate.\n\n## DEC-14: Free text on the command line\ndocs\neval\nexperiments\neval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a175f0-a051-7293-adf5-5b3650d75759","create_time":1792980185.2653594}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
