{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:03:26.562Z","ordinal":369319,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a175f2-c3e2-7071-a303-ebb0248a201b","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2649)\nTotal output lines: 108\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...381 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-26 2:03am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (13,880t read) | 63,808t work | 78% savings\n\n### Oct 23, 2026\nS1689 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session monitoring CI for PR #175 (HTML control injection fix) and main branch while holding CR bypass as release blocker (Oct 23, 11:14 PM)\nS1690 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session running requirements gate check on main and monitoring CI for PR #175 and main branch (Oct 23, 11:15 PM)\nS1692 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session investigating missing startup feature while monitoring active CI runs for post-PR177 main and PR #175 (Oct 23, 11:17 PM)\nS1693 User set approval mode to \"Default to review\" — session continuing RC.4 release gate monitoring (Oct 23, 11:19 PM)\nS1694 RC.4 release gate monitoring — CI status check on main and PR #175 while holding CR bypass blocker (Oct 23, 11:21 PM)\nS1701 RC.4 release gate session recovery — assess PR #175 CR bypass blocker and CI status across main and PR #175 branches (Oct 23, 11:22 PM)\nS1707 RC.4 release gate — monitoring CI for PR #175 (CR bypass fix needed) and main branch while holding merge pending blocker resolution (Oct 23, 11:25 PM)\nS1709 RC.4 release gate — PR #175 CR bypass fix blocked on safe-boundary handoff; monitoring main CI while waiting for claim transfer confirmation (Oct 23, 11:26 PM)\nS1718 Kimi agent handover for agent.ts — monitoring CI for PR #240 refreshed branch while main CI run 40227786412 completes (Oct 23, 11:30 PM)\n### Oct 25, 2026\n22180 8:28p ○ PR #240 CI npm test Step Start Times Confirmed — ~9 Minutes Elapsed\nS1723 Kimi agent waiting for agent.ts handover — PR #240 REPL checkpoint failure recovery review and CI monitoring (Oct 25, 8:36 PM)\n22185 8:36p ○ PR #240 CodeQL Workflow Run 40230534030 Confirmed Completed Successfully on 2a95ec2\n22187 8:42p ○ PR #240 test-matrix (24) Node 24 Job Passed — Only Node 22 Remaining\n22189 \" ○ PR #240 Both test-matrix Jobs Passed — New linux-x86_64 Job Triggered, Still BLOCKED\n22191 8:43p ○ PR #240 linux-x86_64 Job Started at 20:42 UTC — At cargo test Step\n22192 \" ○ PR #240 Review Carry-Forward Comment Confirms Patch Identity on Rebased Head\n22194 8:44p ○ PR #240 linux-x86_64 Job Advanced to cargo build Step — cargo test Completed\n22196 \" ○ PLAN-10 Issue #1 — Held-Out T2/T3 Corpus Qualification Blocked, Custodian Unresponsive Since Oct 22\n22197 \" ○ Agent Pool Status Enumerated — Three Completed Agents Plus Root Running\n22199 8:46p ○ PR #240 linux-x86_64 Job Advanced to npm test Step — Started 20:45:48 UTC\n22201 \" ○ Active T4 Qualification Branch Claim Found — v1/plan-10-pr10c-t4-qualification at base 05994a40\n22202 \" ○ T4 Qualification Branch Current State — HEAD at c8d374a, PID 4097078 No Longer Running\n22203 \" ○ T4 Branch Is 41 Commits Ahead of origin/main — Last Commit 2026-10-25T09:50 UTC\n22204 \" ○ T4 Branch Has No PR Open — 41 Commits Unmerged with No Pull Request\n22208 8:57p ○ RC7_VERSION_BUMP Claim Confirmed — Worktree at /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc7-version-bump on base d79f18a\n22209 8:58p ○ RC7 Version Bump Worktree Does Not Exist Yet — Claim Pre-Staged Before Worktree Creation\n22211 9:00p ○ CI Workflow Has No timeout-minutes for npm test Step — No Hard Timeout on Long-Running Tests\n22219 \" ○ PR #240 New CI Run linux-x86_64 Reached package-linux.sh — npm test Completed\n22213 \" ○ PR #240 linux-x86_64 npm test Completed — Now at package-linux.sh Re…180 tokens truncated…n 40230534022 Completed with Success\n22224 \" ○ PR #240 Merge Confirmed — Main Branch Advanced to b31ba92, Post-Merge CI Triggered\n22225 \" ◆ RC7 Version Bump Worktree Created at b31ba92 — Work Starting on v1/rc7-version-bump Branch\n22229 \" ○ Post-PR-#240-Merge CI Runs Started on b31ba92\n22226 \" ○ RC7_VERSION_BUMP Claim Scope and File Claims Enumerated\n22231 \" ✓ REPL_CHECKPOINT_FAILURE_RECOVERY_20261025 Claim Released\n22227 \" ○ Pre-Bump State Confirmed — All Components at v1.0.0-rc.6, Requirements Gate at 108/6/2/7\n22233 9:06p ○ Requirements Gate on b31ba92 — 30+ Open Failures and Missing sync-version.mjs\n22228 \" ○ RC7 File Claims Confirmed Held — cli/package-lock.json Released by Prior RC6 Bump\n22230 \" ○ Active Claims After PR #240 Merge — 6 Claims Still Held Including Merged PR Files\n22235 \" ○ Requirements Gate Passes in RC7 Version Bump Worktree — All Components at rc.6\n22232 \" ○ RC6 Version Bump History Traced — RC7 Lane Authorized After PR239+PR240 Integration\n22234 \" ✓ RC7 Version Bump File Claims Fully Acquired — 6 Hot-File Claims Updated to b31ba92 Base\n22236 \" ○ RC7 Changelog Commits Identified — 7 Commits Since RC6 Tag on Main\n22237 9:07p ○ Open PRs Against Main Are All Dependabot — No Feature PRs Pending\n22239 9:08p ○ Post-Merge CodeQL Run 40233817651 Completed Successfully on b31ba92\n22241 \" ○ T4 Qualification Branch Is 44 Commits Ahead of Main With Zero File Diffs\n22238 \" ○ Post-Merge Main CodeQL Run 40233817651 Completed Successfully on b31ba92\n22242 \" ○ T4 Branch Merge Base Is Branch Tip — Branch Already Reachable From Main\n22243 \" ○ T4 Qualification Work Merged Via PR #215 — No Unmerged T4 Commits Exist\n22244 \" ○ Active Claims Include PLAN-10_HOST_PREFLIGHT_CURRENT_SOURCE and Three eval File Claims\n22245 9:09p ○ PR #215 T4 Fault Qualification Merged With All CI Checks Passing\n22246 \" ✓ eval File Claims Released After PR #215 T4 Merge Confirmed\n22240 9:12p ○ RELEASE_PUBLISHER Claim Updated — RC Lifecycle State Confirmed Post-PR240 Merge\n\nAccess 64k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n⚠️ Heads up: claude-mem is paused while a provider quota cooldown is active.\n\nMemory capture is paused on claude (five_hour) to preserve your Claude allowance, until 2026-10-26T02:15:05.047Z (12 minutes from now).\n\nReason: Memory capture paused: five-hour Claude usage is 99.0%, at or above the 95% pause threshold. This reserves allowance for interactive work.\n\nThis is not a failure. Incoming observations stay queued in memory and are written\nwhen the cooldown clears — the worker is intentionally not starting the generator\nso interactive work keeps the remaining allowance.\n\nRestarting will NOT help here: it does not replenish the allowance or clear the\npersisted cooldown — so please leave the worker alone.\n\n(Assistant: tell the user that memory capture is paused for a quota cooldown\nat the very start of your first reply. Do NOT restart the worker and do NOT\nsuggest restarting it.)\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only.\nServer runtime: use Smart search by default in three steps—search({query}) for an index, timeline({anchor: ID}) for context, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records selected after reviewing the index and timeline. These tools use the configured server project; optional projectId selects another authorized server project. No auto or guided modes. Dumb search is unavailable in this runtime.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed.\n\nFull hook output saved to: /tmp/hook_outputs/01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92/813a8c35-c585-4073-92ac-a8d34858afe7.txt"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a175f0-a051-7293-adf5-5b3650d75759","create_time":1792980206.562168,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
