{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:14:59.002Z","ordinal":369828,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a175fc-3a2e-74f1-a3b4-8a558745a90a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2ae476d4-84fb-4aea-a256-2e9f0228cabc","process_id":"20937","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'PR #243|index lock|checkpoint.*lock|checkpoint' /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc7-checkpoint/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -n 25 && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc7-checkpoint status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc7-checkpoint log -3 --oneline"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i 'PR #243|index lock|checkpoint.*lock|checkpoint' /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc7-checkpoint/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -n 25 && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc7-checkpoint status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc7-checkpoint log -3 --oneline"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"101:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports that every attempt to start Nexus RC1 fails with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is consistent with RC1's exact source predating PR #147's checkpoint-choice flow. PR #147 is integrated in current main and its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed; the interactive TUI now offers read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint anyway with a sensitivity warning, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. RC1 and RC2 are immutable and do not contain this behavior. The next candidate must include the fix, and the installed candidate must be exercised to verify the choices before any acceptance claim.\n121:## Historical release checkpoint (2026-10-22 09:32 UTC; superseded by the integration update above)\n127:**Evaluator containment and Git isolation:** Source tests cover CPU, memory, process-count, storage limits, process cleanup, solution-bearing Git refs/reflogs/dangling objects, and external canary stores in `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts`. PR #140 records a separate exact-source synthetic host preflight with 10/10 checks; its merge and CI do not establish held-out qualification. The public held-out manifest records 40 T2 tasks, ten each across four task classes and four languages; this metadata does not prove private digest re-derivation, author-session independence, effective access controls, custody acceptance, or qualification readiness. No private payloads or validators were accessed for this checkpoint.\n131:**Runtime floor:** The merged DEC-12 and current `main` specify Node `>=20`; the upstream release schedule lists Node 20 end of life as 2026-04-30. Open PR #143 proposes to correct that date in the RC1 release note; its exact checks passed on the prior base, and it still needs a refresh against current `main`. README, quickstart, and the development guide still contain the old date on `main`; edits to those files are part of the separate Node 22 lane. PR #137 is open and ready for review, implementing its stated owner-directed `>=22` target. It remains based on old base `8935918` and needs a current-main refresh. Its Node 22/24, Linux packaging, and CodeQL checks pass on that prior base, but the required `test-matrix (20)` context is absent and it has no independent review. The proposed source change is not integrated and conflicts with accepted DEC-12 and REQ-REL-111, which still specify `>=20` and a Node 20/22/24 matrix. The active ruleset requires `test-matrix (20)`, which this candidate omits; its checks are on the prior base and no independent review is recorded. Do not treat `>=22` as v1 policy until the policy records and required checks are formally reconciled. No runtime-floor change is made by this checkpoint.\n135:This checkpoint supersedes the earlier 2026-10-22 and 2026-10-21 updates below for current source and release status. Historical reports remain bound to their recorded revisions.\n140:- The source requirements gate remains a clean-worktree pass on exact integration `7d6673f`; eleven requirements remain deferred to exact-RC qualification as listed in the checkpoint below. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; this CI progression does not establish RC readiness or acceptance.\n144:**Authoritative integration:** `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`, merged from PR #102. The shared checkout remains on `main@db1ca558086014912b20dae8232af111ccb21d67` with unrelated local modifications; it was not changed for this checkpoint.\n157:This update supersedes the 14:56 UTC `8f4504e` checkpoint below for current state. Earlier evidence remains bound to its recorded revisions.\n167:This checkpoint reconciles the candidate ledger and acceptance procedure against recorded source and test evidence. It is not a release approval. Historical inspection sections below are preserved as audit evidence and do not represent current branch state where superseded by the 2026-10-21 update.\n172:- **PR and contest state:** PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-`main` candidate. Its CI and CodeQL checks are green, but it is not a release acceptance or publication. PR #102 is open at `3756afe05dbd75c4e6929d87cd50facbb8ab1748`, based on `8f4504e`, to record a synthetic qualification-host preflight; its CodeQL and TypeScript checks passed and its Node matrix was still running at this checkpoint. The preflight report records 10/10 checks using only an empty synthetic marker store; it does not establish private corpus custody or qualification acceptance. The contest has concluded; no contest freeze applies. Historical contest artifacts remain historical evidence only.\n179:The 2026-10-18 checkpoint sections below remain historical evidence. The previously closed PR #46 was never merged; its two readiness commits remain available on the preserved closed-PR branch, not in this reconciliation branch's history, and are superseded by this exact `8f4504e` update.\n183:The 17:16 checkpoint's phrase “nothing has been tagged or published” was too broad. GitHub lists the existing pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`, with corresponding tags `7e46bb0da88d06552a66ef703f53a05d1de1f37d` and `c3dcafac93b5f52d913b4dfb6eb292bbcede4566`. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` and CodeQL passed on exact integration `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`. No v1.0.0 release candidate or stable v1.0.0 publication exists. The superseded 17:16 text below is retained verbatim as historical evidence; this correction is authoritative for current release status.\n187:- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`, merge commit for PR #45, whose only changed file was `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md`. PR #45 exact-head CI run `39144798481` and CodeQL run `39144798415` passed; independent read-only review accepted exact head `8041c0dbe1a982b2a9e275083f336eb4c5b768b3`. Post-merge CodeQL run `39146982807` passed. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` is in progress on exact `6a16cb6`: Cloudflare and Node 20/22/24 passed; Linux `linux-x86_64` is still executing the CLI suite. This checkpoint does not combine its status with results from another revision.\n188:- **PR and evaluator state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, #44, and #45 are integrated. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c` on stale base `faf95803714a3c543f5c59bc0610ca6291a6184d`. Its exact CI run `39141771002` passed on that old head, but independent review found qualification preflight does not account for host-source mounts created unconditionally by `agentSandboxArgv`. The finding is recorded in comment `6252102243`; a read-only source inventory and shared-mount-plan remediation target are in comment `6252621855`. Owner handoff request `6252543078` has no response as of this checkpoint. The evaluator claim remains protected. Do not execute held-out tasks until this boundary is fixed, exact-head validated, and independently accepted.\n193:The 16:19 UTC `4bce876` checkpoint below remains as historical evidence for that revision.\n198:- **PR state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, and #44 are integrated. PR #9's stale readiness changes were merged earlier and are retained in history. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c`, based on now-stale `faf9580`; its exact CI run `39141771002` passed all five jobs, including 1,243 CLI tests with zero failures, resource enforcement fixtures, staged Git-history/external-store canaries, security gates, deterministic package/SBOM comparison, and installer/package smoke. Independent review found a release-critical gap: preflight does not compare protected corpus paths with the evaluator's unconditional system mounts such as `/usr/local/lib`. The reviewer requested refusal of protected paths beneath every mounted host path and regression coverage. The evaluator claim remains active; no transfer or remediation checkpoint has been reported. Do not run held-out qualification. PR #33 must incorporate `4bce876`, fix this finding, pass exact-head checks, and receive independent re-review.\n200:- **Evaluator boundary and T2 custody:** PR #33's exact source CI passes resource-bound and Git-history canary fixtures, but the independent unconditional-system-mount finding remains open. Separately, the custodian report accepts the sealed manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, its custody, author-session provenance, private digest validation, and reference validation; private payloads were not inspected for this checkpoint. The sealed tasks use legacy `hidden: { dir, into, command }` checks, while evaluator qualification requires `blackbox-v1`. Custody acceptance does not resolve this format mismatch or evaluator-boundary acceptance. No T2 qualification has started.\n201:- **Qualification host and terminal:** Qualification-host tooling is integrated through PR #31 (`8c0ab7b`), but this checkpoint has no evidence that the qualification host was provisioned and validated at `4bce876`. Terminal acceptance procedure is integrated; the required human matrix remains unexecuted. It requires five environments × three sizes on the exact installed RC, with per-cell PASS/FAIL and screenshots of the approval panel and post-exit state.\n204:The 10:44 UTC checkpoint below is historical and preserved verbatim. Its `5193984` integration candidate and in-progress CI status are superseded by this exact `4bce876` update.\n209:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was run from a clean archive of exact `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`; it exited 1 as required. The ledger has 121 rows (107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below-threshold rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` is now `tested` with the DEC-17 accuracy exceptions preserved. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its `CTX-001` blocking marker/mapping is under owner reconciliation against DEC-04. No requirement was promoted by this checkpoint.\n210:- **PR #26 evaluator boundary:** PR #26 head `c019575` contains the independently reviewed dedicated-tmpfs preflight and adversarial staged-Git/external-store canary; it is rebased on `886766b`, while integration has since advanced to `5193984`. Exact-head CI run [39119705161](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119705161) is still running its Node 20/22/24 CLI suites at this checkpoint. It must be rebased and requalified on `5193984` before merge. A local synthetic permission probe passed (0711 accepted; 0755 and 0721 rejected); the targeted TypeScript test could not run on this host because no dedicated tmpfs was mounted, and the shared `/dev/shm` correctly failed preflight. That failed local attempt is not counted as a pass.\n217:## Superseded checkpoint (2026-10-18, `a7126aa`)\n270:## Historical evidence: Earlier state checkpoint (2026-10-17 02:51 UTC)\n334:## RC5 qualification checkpoint (2026-10-25)\n341:- **PR #216:** merged to that source revision after exact-head checks and independent source review. The unrelated shared checkout remains dirty and was not used or modified for this checkpoint.\n## v1/readiness-rc7-checkpoint...origin/main [ahead 1]\ncf5ef34 docs: refresh v1 release readiness checkpoint\n62e541c Merge pull request #244 from mikeholownych/v1/readiness-rc7-current-state\n6dee7e6 docs(release): reconcile RC7 and post-PR243 status\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":30021}},"started_at_ms":1792980899001,"completed_at_ms":1792980899002}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:14:59.990Z","ordinal":369829,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a175fd-5896-7672-ae7d-1609ab649e28","call_id":"call_91376068ba484489a66d35a79ced8229","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2899)\nTotal output lines: 29\n\n101:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports that every attempt to start Nexus RC1 fails with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is consistent with RC1's exact source predating PR #147's checkpoint-choice flow. PR #147 is integrated in current main and its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed; the interactive TUI now offers read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint anyway with a sensitivity warning, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. RC1 and RC2 are immutable and do not contain this behavior. The next candidate must include the fix, and the installed candidate must be exercised to verify the choices before any acceptance claim.\n121:## Historical release checkpoint (2026-10-22 09:32 UTC; superseded by the integration update above)\n127:**Evaluator containment and Git isolation:** Source tests cover CPU, memory, process-count, storage limits, process cleanup, solution-bearing Git refs/reflogs/dangling objects, and external canary stores in `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts`. PR #140 records a separate exact-source synthetic host preflight with 10/10 checks; its merge and CI do not establish held-out qualification. The public held-out manifest records 40 T2 tasks, ten each across four task classes and four languages; this metadata does not prove private digest re-derivation, author-session independence, effective access controls, custody acceptance, or qualification readiness. No private payloads or validators were accessed for this checkpoint.\n131:**Runtime floor:** The merged DEC-12 and current `main` specify Node `>=20`; the upstream release schedule lists Node 20 end of life as 2026-04-30. Open PR #143 proposes to correct that date in the RC1 release note; its exact checks passed on the prior base, and it still needs a refresh against current `main`. README, quickstart, and the development guide still contain the old date on `main`; edits to those files are part of the separate Node 22 lane. PR #137 is open and ready for review, implementing its stated owner-directed `>=22` target. It remains based on old base `8935918` and needs a current-main refresh. Its Node 22/24, Linux packaging, and CodeQL checks pass on that prior base, but the required `test-matrix (20)` context is absent and it has no independent review. The proposed source change is not integrated and conflicts with accepted DEC-12 and REQ-REL-111, which still specify `>=20` and a Node 20/22/24 matrix. The active ruleset requires `test-matrix (20)`, which this candidate omits; its checks are on the prior base and no independent review is recorded. Do not treat `>=22` as v1 policy until the policy records and required checks are formally reconciled. No runtime-floor change is made by this checkpoint.\n135:This c…1499 tokens truncated…r-boundary acceptance. No T2 qualification has started.\n201:- **Qualification host and terminal:** Qualification-host tooling is integrated through PR #31 (`8c0ab7b`), but this checkpoint has no evidence that the qualification host was provisioned and validated at `4bce876`. Terminal acceptance procedure is integrated; the required human matrix remains unexecuted. It requires five environments × three sizes on the exact installed RC, with per-cell PASS/FAIL and screenshots of the approval panel and post-exit state.\n204:The 10:44 UTC checkpoint below is historical and preserved verbatim. Its `5193984` integration candidate and in-progress CI status are superseded by this exact `4bce876` update.\n209:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was run from a clean archive of exact `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`; it exited 1 as required. The ledger has 121 rows (107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below-threshold rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` is now `tested` with the DEC-17 accuracy exceptions preserved. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its `CTX-001` blocking marker/mapping is under owner reconciliation against DEC-04. No requirement was promoted by this checkpoint.\n210:- **PR #26 evaluator boundary:** PR #26 head `c019575` contains the independently reviewed dedicated-tmpfs preflight and adversarial staged-Git/external-store canary; it is rebased on `886766b`, while integration has since advanced to `5193984`. Exact-head CI run [39119705161](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119705161) is still running its Node 20/22/24 CLI suites at this checkpoint. It must be rebased and requalified on `5193984` before merge. A local synthetic permission probe passed (0711 accepted; 0755 and 0721 rejected); the targeted TypeScript test could not run on this host because no dedicated tmpfs was mounted, and the shared `/dev/shm` correctly failed preflight. That failed local attempt is not counted as a pass.\n217:## Superseded checkpoint (2026-10-18, `a7126aa`)\n270:## Historical evidence: Earlier state checkpoint (2026-10-17 02:51 UTC)\n334:## RC5 qualification checkpoint (2026-10-25)\n341:- **PR #216:** merged to that source revision after exact-head checks and independent source review. The unrelated shared checkout remains dirty and was not used or modified for this checkpoint.\n## v1/readiness-rc7-checkpoint...origin/main [ahead 1]\ncf5ef34 docs: refresh v1 release readiness checkpoint\n62e541c Merge pull request #244 from mikeholownych/v1/readiness-rc7-current-state\n6dee7e6 docs(release): reconcile RC7 and post-PR243 status\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a175fc-3a2e-74f1-a3b4-8a558745a90a","create_time":1792980899.9907854}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
