cords without initialization/reset; existing valid state is preserved and conflicts fail closed. [Task 5]\n492:- Symptom: initialization leaves Vault initialized/sealed without recoverable handoff material. Cause: the helper assumed the wrong Vault CLI JSON field. Fix: inspect actual CLI JSON and verify durable recovery handoff before progressing; never initialize again over existing state without explicit destructive authorization. [Task 1]\n777:# Task Group: Nexus v1 CI prerequisite integration and release qualification handoff\n809:- At handoff the version remained `0.1.0-alpha.2`; there was no RC, release tag, publication, or qualification run. `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` failed 12 rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-118`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. [Task 1]\n812:- The readiness claims were `FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json` and `PLAN-10_READINESS_T2/owner.json`; at handoff the owner PID was absent but the claim was younger than 24 hours. Resume after release or the documented stale-claim procedure, update against `2c70d39`, and rerun fresh branch CI. [Task 2]\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8186)\nTotal output lines: 129\n\n## main...origin/main [behind 1087]\n M AGENTS.md\n M cli/dist/agent.js\n M cli/src/agent.ts\n M cli/src/core/state.ts\n M cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\nA  docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nA  docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\nA  scripts/check_requirements.mjs\n?? cli/test/agent_prompt.test.ts\n?? docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/README.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/SHA256SUMS\n?? docs/v1.0.0/evidence/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/plans/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/specs/\n?? jsf/\n?? nex