{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:47:47.944Z","ordinal":371061,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e07ef3e3-b410-426d-ba99-c1ea7ffd986a","process_id":"37678","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 mike@10.0.8.3 '\"$HOME/.local/bin/nexus\" --version; \"${HOME}/.local/bin/nexus\" connect --help 2>&1 | head -40; \"${HOME}/.local/bin/nexus\" provider --help 2>&1 | head -40' ; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 1 -iname '*gateway*' -o -iname '*cloud*' -o -iname '*provider*' | sort; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 3 'OpenRouter|pinned|live task|E5'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=5 mike@10.0.8.3 '\"$HOME/.local/bin/nexus\" --version; \"${HOME}/.local/bin/nexus\" connect --help 2>&1 | head -40; \"${HOME}/.local/bin/nexus\" provider --help 2>&1 | head -40' ; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 1 -iname '*gateway*' -o -iname '*cloud*' -o -iname '*provider*' | sort; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 3 'OpenRouter|pinned|live task|E5'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)\nUsage: nexus connect [options] <provider>\n\nConnect a cloud provider: save an API key (verified first) or sign in\n\nArguments:\n  provider       openrouter, openai, anthropic, chatgpt, copilot, compatible\n\nOptions:\n  --method <id>  api-key (default where offered), openrouter-oauth,\n                 chatgpt-oauth, copilot-device\n  -h, --help     display help for command\nUsage: nexus [options] [command]\n\nNexus Code - Custom Autonomous Coding Harness for Local AI (LM Studio / vLLM)\n\nOptions:\n  -V, --version                                output the version number\n  --repl                                       Start interactive coding session (REPL)\n  --live                                       Start live TUI\n  -r, --resume [id]                            Resume previous session (defaults to latest if id omitted)\n  --approve                                    Require human approval before destructive actions (edits, shell commands)\n  -y, --yes                                    Run non-interactively without approval prompts (forces auto mode)\n  --mode <mode>                                Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\n  --read-only                                  Reject all mutating tool executions and commands\n  -e, --endpoint <url>                         Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\n  -m, --model <name>                           Model name identifier (default: active model in vLLM)\n  -w, --workspace <path>                       Workspace directory (default: current directory)\n  -s, --max-steps <number>                     Steps per segment; continuation checkpoints there instead of stopping (default: 30)\n  --max-total-steps <number>                   Continuation: an explicit total-step limit for one turn (default: none; progressing work continues)\n  --strict-token-count                         Refuse a request the connection could not count on a worker (default: proceed on the labelled estimate)\n  --max-turn-minutes <number>                  Continuation: an explicit wall-clock limit for one turn in minutes (default: none)\n  --stagnation-steps <number>                  Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\n  --no-continuation                            End a turn at --max-steps instead of continuing while it makes progress\n  -t, --temperature <number>                   Model temperature (default: 0.2)\n  --shell <type>                               Linux shell to use: bash, zsh, or sh (default: bash) (default: \"bash\")\n  --fallback <urls>                            Comma-separated fallback LLM endpoints if primary is unavailable\n  --context-limit <tokens>                     Context window limit in tokens; below the provider's advertised capacity it is kept, above it the advertised capacity applies (default: advertised capacity, else 65536)\n  --dry-run                                    Simulate file modifications without writing changes to disk\n  --sandbox [mode]                             Isolate command execution using bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default: auto)\n  --worktree                                   Isolate execution inside an ephemeral git worktree under .nexus/worktrees/<task-id>\n  --authoritative-verifier <command>           Trusted command that must pass before any task completion; its success may authorize automatic worktree merge\n  --deliverable-file <path>                    Operator-declared workspace-relative product file used for VERIFIED binding (repeatable) (default: [])\n  --record-flight                              Record execution into an append-only deterministic .flightlog\n  --planner-model <name>                       Deep reasoning model for architecture planning (o3, R1, Sonnet)\n  --planner-endpoint <url>                     Dedicated inference endpoint for planner model\n  --coder-model <name>                         High-throughput model for surgical code implementation (Qwen 2.5 Coder)\n  --coder-endpoint <url>                       Dedicated inference endpoint for coder model\n  --provider <id>                              Cloud inference provider: openrouter, openai, anthropic, compatible (default: appliance endpoint)\n  --base-url <url>                             Override the provider's base URL (operator-only; required for 'compatible')\n  --planner-provider <id>                      Cloud provider for the planner model (requires --planner-model)\n  --coder-provider <id>                        Cloud provider for the coder model (requires --coder-model)\n.git/nexus-claims/DEFECT_PROVIDER_STREAM_INTEGRATION_20261026\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_core_provider_recovery.ts\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_provider_cli.ts\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_provider_cli.test.ts\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_provider_robustness.test.ts\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_e5-openrouter-live-task-20261023.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.3_providers_provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_agent-collab-worker_package.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_fork-worker_package.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_package-lock.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_package.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_trusted-broker-bundle_package-lock.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_trusted-broker-bundle_package.json\n.git/nexus-claims/SEC_CODEQL_PROVIDER_CLI_REDACTION\n76-\n77-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n78-|---|---|---|\n79:| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81-| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n--\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n--\n147-\n148-ACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n149-\n150:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n151-\n152-| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n153-|---|---|---|\n154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n155-| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n156:| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n158-\n159-## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n--\n280-| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n281-| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n282-| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n283:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n284-| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n285-\n286-## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":702145474}},"started_at_ms":1792982866236,"completed_at_ms":1792982867939}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:47:49.015Z","ordinal":371062,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1761b-6417-7bf0-be59-ef224f874d93","call_id":"call_30902bcdeb3a4fd5bccbf8ed6bd1117c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2556)\nTotal output lines: 108\n\n1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)\nUsage: nexus connect [options] <provider>\n\nConnect a cloud provider: save an API key (verified first) or sign in\n\nArguments:\n  provider       openrouter, openai, anthropic, chatgpt, copilot, compatible\n\nOptions:\n  --method <id>  api-key (default where offered), openrouter-oauth,\n                 chatgpt-oauth, copilot-device\n  -h, --help     display help for command\nUsage: nexus [options] [command]\n\nNexus Code - Custom Autonomous Coding Harness for Local AI (LM Studio / vLLM)\n\nOptions:\n  -V, --version                                output the version number\n  --repl                                       Start interactive coding session (REPL)\n  --live                                       Start live TUI\n  -r, --resume [id]                            Resume previous session (defaults to latest if id omitted)\n  --approve                                    Require human approval before destructive actions (edits, shell commands)\n  -y, --yes                                    Run non-interactively without approval prompts (forces auto mode)\n  --mode <mode>                                Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\n  --read-only                                  Reject all mutating tool executions and commands\n  -e, --endpoint <url>                         Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\n  -m, --model <name>                           Model name identifier (default: active model in vLLM)\n  -w, --workspace <path>                       Workspace directory (default: current directory)\n  -s, --max-steps <number>                     Steps per segment; continuation checkpoints there instead of stopping (default: 30)\n  --max-total-steps <number>                   Continuation: an explicit total-step limit for one turn (default: none; progressing work continues)\n  --strict-token-count                         Refuse a request the connection could not count on a worker (default: proceed on the labelled estimate)\n  --max-turn-minutes <number>                  Continuation: an explicit wall-clock limit for one turn in minutes (default: none)\n  --stagnation-steps <number>                  Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\n  --no-continuation                            End a turn at --max-steps instead of continuing while it makes progress\n  -t, --temperature <number>                   Model temperature (default: 0.2)\n  --shell <type>                               Linux shell to use: bash, zsh, or sh (default: bash) (default: \"bash\")\n  --fallback <urls>                            Comma-separated fallback LLM endpoints if primary is unavailable\n  --context-limit <tokens>                     Context window limit in tokens; below the provider's advertised capacity it is kept, above it the advertised capacity applies (default: advertised capacity, else 65536)\n  --dry-run                                    Simulate file modifications without writing changes to disk\n  --sandbox [mode]                             Isolate command execution using bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default: auto)\n  --worktree                                   Isolate execution inside an ephemeral git worktree under .nexus/worktrees/<task-id>\n  --authoritative-verifier <command>           Trusted command that must pass before any task completion; its success may authorize automatic worktree merge\n  --deliverable-file <path>                    Operator-declared workspace-relative product file used for VERIFIED binding (repeatable) (default: [])\n  --record-flight                              Record execution into an append-only deterministic .flightlog\n  --planner-model <name>                       Deep reasoning model for architecture planning (o3, R1, Sonnet)\n  --planner-endpoint <url>                     Dedicated inference endpoint for planner model\n  --coder-model <name>                         High-throughput model for surgical cod…556 tokens truncated…Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81-| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n--\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n--\n147-\n148-ACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n149-\n150:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n151-\n152-| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n153-|---|---|---|\n154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n155-| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n156:| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n158-\n159-## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n--\n280-| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n281-| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n282-| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n283:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only