{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:48:00.092Z","ordinal":371077,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f069eaa3-9d69-4a97-bb0f-67a505a12c5c","process_id":"8786","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -in \"openrouter\" origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification-rc.7 | head -80; git grep -in 'providers verify' origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 docs/reviews/evidence | head -100; git grep -in 'PINNED_MODEL\\|pinned model' origin/main -- eval docs/v1.0.0 scripts | head -60"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"git grep -in openrouter origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification-rc.7","query":"openrouter","path":"main"},{"type":"search","cmd":"git grep -in 'providers verify' origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 docs/reviews/evidence","query":"providers verify","path":"main"},{"type":"search","cmd":"git grep -in \"PINNED_MODEL\\\\|pinned model\" origin/main -- eval docs/v1.0.0 scripts","query":"PINNED_MODEL\\|pinned model","path":"main"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:25:| Runtime services | The local inference gateway is configured in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`: endpoint `https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1`, model `engineering/b0`, key redacted, `LOCAL_HARNESS_SHELL=bash`. The repo-tracked `cli/.env` holds LM Studio defaults (`localhost:1234`, key \"local\"). **The audit sent no requests to the gateway.** With owner authorization (2026-10-14, small spend), it made live cloud calls through the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections: two `providers verify` runs and one `nexus run` bug-fix task. See EVIDENCE §3. | RT (values redacted) |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:26:| External dependencies | Node ≥ 20 (runtime), GitHub Releases (installer), optional bubblewrap/Docker (sandbox), optional cloud providers (OpenRouter, OpenAI, Anthropic, ChatGPT/Copilot OAuth, compatible), optional MCP servers, DuckDuckGo (default `search_web`). | SRC |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:14:| [DEC-06](#dec-06-supported-providers-for-v1) | Supported providers | Local OpenAI-compatible + OpenRouter supported; others experimental until live-verified | No |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:112:**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:122:| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:248:| X4 | **Partly resolved 2026-10-14:** the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections are authorized for small-spend checks; both were live-verified at db1ca55. Optional: add OpenAI API-key or Anthropic keys if those providers should be listed as supported. | DEC-06 | M5 (optional) |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:28:| Live cloud client | Checkout build `db1ca55` (`/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/dist`), using the operator's existing provider connections: ChatGPT via the Codex CLI sign-in; OpenRouter via the crush credential. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:47:| L2 | `nexus providers verify --provider openrouter -m openrouter/free -j` | PASS. The effective model varied per request (nemotron-3-super, then laguna-xs-2.1, then laguna-s-2.1), which shows `openrouter/free` is unsuitable for matched evaluation. | `49b71fc3…`, `b05711f6…`, `2b9cc6c5…` | `evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json` |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:291:| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:342:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:75:| REQ-PRV-004 | CLOUD_PROVIDERS | Cloud spend limits and receipts; disclosure notice on first request. | `usage.ts`; `client.ts:509-569` | TEST (mock); HIST live (openrouter, chatgpt); RT 2026-10-14 receipts written with provider-reported usage | tested | N | Other providers mock-only | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | SPEC-05 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/SHA256SUMS:63:d569652b3b153a3d90a3f8a1de092f60942734226408dec8eb1db951bca339ea  evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:19:- Two connection kinds: (a) legacy \"appliance/endpoint\" path (no provider id): OpenAI Chat Completions, `/v1` appended,