v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:112:**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:122:| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:248:| X4 | **Partly resolved 2026-10-14:** the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections are authorized for small-spend checks; both were live-verified at db1ca55. Optional: add OpenAI API-key or Anthropic keys if those providers should be listed as supported. | DEC-06 | M5 (optional) |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:28:| Live cloud client | Checkout build `db1ca55` (`/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/dist`), using the operator's existing provider connections: ChatGPT via the Codex CLI sign-in; OpenRouter via the crush credential. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:47:| L2 | `nexus providers verify --provider openrouter -m openrouter/free -j` | PASS. The effective model varied per request (nemotron-3-super, then laguna-xs-2.1, then laguna-s-2.1), which shows `openrouter/free` is unsuitable for matched evaluation. | `49b71fc3…`, `b05711f6…`, `2b9cc6c5…` | `evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json` |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:291:| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:342:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:75:| REQ-PRV-004 | CLOUD_PROVIDERS | Cloud spend limits and receipts; disclosure notice on first request. | `usage.ts`; `client.ts:509-569` | TEST (mock); HIST li