{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:48:53.262Z","ordinal":371126,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1b84d3c6-48f1-438c-874a-337a5e3a159f","process_id":"71448","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n 'NEXUS_CONFIG_HOME\\|NEXUS_HOME\\|credentials.json' origin/main -- cli/src | head -100; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '150,210p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '115,132p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git grep -n 'NEXUS_CONFIG_HOME\\|NEXUS_HOME\\|credentials.json' origin/main -- cli/src | head -100; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '150,210p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '115,132p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:cli/src/credentials.ts:5: * 2. Nexus's own store, ~/.config/nexus/credentials.json (mode 0600), written by `nexus connect` and the TUI.\norigin/main:cli/src/credentials.ts:49:  return path.join(credentialStorageHome(), \".config/nexus/credentials.json\");\norigin/main:cli/src/doctor.ts:108:const PACKAGED_HOME = process.env.NEXUS_HOME ? path.resolve(process.env.NEXUS_HOME) : undefined;\norigin/main:cli/src/doctor.ts:916:  const file = ctx.home === credentialStorageHome() ? credentialsPath() : path.join(ctx.home, \".config/nexus/credentials.json\");\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:100:if (!startupReadOnly && startupArgs[0] !== \"upgrade\" && process.env.NEXUS_UPGRADE_HEALTH_CHECK !== \"1\" && process.env.NEXUS_HOME) {\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:102:  const packagedPrefix = path.resolve(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"../../..\");\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:141:  if (process.env.NEXUS_HOME) {\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:142:    const packaged = path.join(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"lib\", \"core\", \"nexus-tui\");\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:157:  if (process.env.NEXUS_HOME) {\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:158:    const packaged = path.join(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"lib\", \"cli\", \"dist\", \"sidecar.js\");\norigin/main:cli/src/tools.ts:24:  const packagedCoreDir = process.env.NEXUS_HOME ? path.join(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"lib\", \"core\") : undefined;\norigin/main:cli/src/tools.ts:41:  if (process.env.NEXUS_HOME) return path.resolve(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"lib\", \"core\", \"Cargo.toml\");\norigin/main:cli/src/tui.ts:66:    const packagedHome = process.env.NEXUS_HOME;\norigin/main:cli/src/upgrade.ts:243:  const nexusHome = customOptions?.nexusHome ?? process.env.NEXUS_HOME;\norigin/main:cli/src/upgrade_health.ts:55:      const env = { ...process.env, HOME: home, XDG_CONFIG_HOME: path.join(home, \".config\"), XDG_STATE_HOME: path.join(home, \".local/state\"), NEXUS_HOME: absolute, NEXUS_UPGRADE_HEALTH_CHECK: \"1\" };\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\n\n| Tier | Providers | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\n| **Supported (optional integration)** | homelab-ai gateway | Never required (standalone gate). |\n| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\n| **Experimental → Supported if live-verified at RC** | OpenAI API key (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic compatible cloud | Not connected on the owner's install. They stay experimental unless keys are added and `nexus providers verify` passes at RC. |\n| **Experimental (always)** | ChatGPT sign-in (the owner's OpenAI OAuth connection), Copilot sign-in | They use unofficial OAuth flows with terms-of-service and stability risk. Opt-in with a visible warning. ChatGPT sign-in was live-verified on 2026-10-14 (`evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json`), and a live end-to-end run reached a correct VERIFIED (`evidence/live/run1_chatgpt_bugfix.log`). It is still labelled experimental because the sign-in flow is unofficial. |\n\n## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n\n- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\n- **`/tdd` / `--tdd`.** Labelled experimental. Fixing the phase enforcement is post-v1.\n- **Team roles.** Reviewer and researcher units run with a **read-only tool set** (cheap and safety-relevant). Other role allowlists are post-v1.\n\n## DEC-08: Version identity and stale v1.x tags\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27778}},"started_at_ms":1792982933261,"completed_at_ms":1792982933262}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:48:54.455Z","ordinal":371127,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1761c-63b6-77e0-a6a1-77e4807eb586","call_id":"call_6b849d7ad8694bbe87118387da067981","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1645)\nTotal output lines: 94\n\norigin/main:cli/src/credentials.ts:5: * 2. Nexus's own store, ~/.config/nexus/credentials.json (mode 0600), written by `nexus connect` and the TUI.\norigin/main:cli/src/credentials.ts:49:  return path.join(credentialStorageHome(), \".config/nexus/credentials.json\");\norigin/main:cli/src/doctor.ts:108:const PACKAGED_HOME = process.env.NEXUS_HOME ? path.resolve(process.env.NEXUS_HOME) : undefined;\norigin/main:cli/src/doctor.ts:916:  const file = ctx.home === credentialStorageHome() ? credentialsPath() : path.join(ctx.home, \".config/nexus/credentials.json\");\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:100:if (!startupReadOnly && startupArgs[0] !== \"upgrade\" && process.env.NEXUS_UPGRADE_HEALTH_CHECK !== \"1\" && process.env.NEXUS_HOME) {\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:102:  const packagedPrefix = path.resolve(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"../../..\");\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:141:  if (process.env.NEXUS_HOME) {\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:142:    const packaged = path.join(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"lib\", \"core\", \"nexus-tui\");\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:157:  if (process.env.NEXUS_HOME) {\norigin/main:cli/src/index.ts:158:    const packaged = path.join(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"lib\", \"cli\", \"dist\", \"sidecar.js\");\norigin/main:cli/src/tools.ts:24:  const packagedCoreDir = process.env.NEXUS_HOME ? path.join(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"lib\", \"core\") : undefined;\norigin/main:cli/src/tools.ts:41:  if (process.env.NEXUS_HOME) return path.resolve(process.env.NEXUS_HOME, \"lib\", \"core\", \"Cargo.toml\");\norigin/main:cli/src/tui.ts:66:    const packagedHome = process.env.NEXUS_HOME;\norigin/main:cli/src/upgrade.ts:243:  const nexusHome = customOptions?.nexusHome ?? process.env.NEXUS_HOME;\norigin/main:cli/src/upgrade_health.ts:55:      const env = { ...process.env, HOME: home, XDG_CONFIG_HOME: path.join(home, \".config\"), XDG_STATE_HOME: path.join(home, \".local/state\"), NEXUS_HOME: absolute, NEXUS_UPGRADE_HEALTH_CHECK: \"1\" };\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The e…145 tokens truncated… Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\n\n| Tier | Providers | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\n| **Supported (optional integration)** | homelab-ai gateway | Never required (standalone gate). |\n| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\n| **Experimental → Supported if live-verified at RC** | OpenAI API key (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic compatible cloud | Not connected on the owner's install. They stay experimental unless keys are added and `nexus providers verify` passes at RC. |\n| **Experimental (always)** | ChatGPT sign-in (the owner's OpenAI OAuth connection), Copilot sign-in | They use unofficial OAuth flows with terms-of-service and stability risk. Opt-in with a visible warning. ChatGPT sign-in was live-verified on 2026-10-14 (`evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json`), and a live end-to-end run reached a correct VERIFIED (`evidence/live/run1_chatgpt_bugfix.log`). It is still labelled experimental because the sign-in flow is unofficial. |\n\n## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n\n- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\n- **`/tdd` / `--tdd`.** Labelled experimental. Fixing the phase enforcement is post-v1.\n- **Team roles.** Reviewer and researcher units run with a **read-only tool set** (cheap and safety-relevant). Other role allowlists are post-v1.\n\n## DEC-08: Version identity and stale v1.x tags\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","create_time":1792982934.4549663}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
