{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:49:44.553Z","ordinal":371179,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adebfc720f081a0a95c9ce4f69df414","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I confirmed the OpenRouter pinned-model verification passed on installed RC7, with the expected streamed response and tool round trip; no key or response body was exposed. For the upgrade screenshot, no upgrade process is currently running on Ubuntu, and the durable state there is only about 24 KB. The same RC7 backup routine completes in 20 ms on a synthetic fixture, so I’m checking the actual install’s control flow while I run the authorized isolated provider task. The new screenshots also show “Appliance” failing model discovery and no local provider entry; I’ll reconcile that against the provider setup contract after this qualification step."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792982983153,"completed_at_ms":1792982984553}}
