li/test/team_convergence.test.ts:740:    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(home, \".config/nexus/config.env\"), `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=${gatewayUrl}\\nLOCAL_LLM_MODEL=engineering/lead\\n`);\norigin/main:cli/test/team_convergence.test.ts:768:        process.env.LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT = aihost.url;\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:130:   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:18:- Config (config.ts:16-40): env load order = install `cli/.env` (no override) -> `~/.config/nexus/config.env` (override) -> **cwd `.env` (override:true, any key)**. Credential authority snapshot (operator env + config.env) taken before cwd `.env` (client.ts:77-101); provider selection, provider base URL, disclosure authorization and stored-token binding use that snapshot. Everything else (TLS/Node env, timeouts, recovery policy, LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT/FALLBACKS, provider key env vars) reads live `process.env`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:19:- Two connection kinds: (a) legacy \"appliance/endpoint\" path (no provider id): OpenAI Chat Completions, `/v1` appended, fallback list, `X-Task-Class`, gateway token file / config.env key scoped by origin (client.ts:123-133), no receipts, no spending limits; (b) provider connections (providers.ts:46-116): openrouter, openai (Responses), anthropic (Messages), compatible, chatgpt (unofficial OAuth), copilot (unofficial OAuth); pinned endpoint, own key only, `redirect:\"error\"`, receipts in `<ws>/.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl`, spending limits (usage.ts).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:38:| PRV-11 | S4 | homelab assumptions | client.ts:63-69 (`~/.config/opencode/t5820-client-token`), providers.ts:161 + client.ts:644-647 (X-Task-Class to every endpoint), client.ts:947 (`X-Nexus-Purpose`), CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md (`/model appliance engineering/b0`) | SOURCE | Harmless for standalone (token scoped to config.env origin; servers ignore headers) but homelab names leak into product