`LOCAL_LLM_TASK_CLASS`, `NEXUS_CONTEXT_LIMIT`, plus any key in the documented `NEXUS_PROJECT_*` namespace. All other keys are ignored, with one warning per key at startup and in `nexus doctor`. In particular it may not set `NODE_*`, `*_PROXY`, `HOME`, `PATH`, `SSL_*`, credential variables, timeouts, recovery policy or fallback endpoints. Project values are kept in a separate map and are never written into `process.env`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:78:10. **REQ-TUI-105.** At session start (TUI and REPL) the endpoint is probed with a 3 s `GET /models`. An unreachable or misconfigured endpoint is reported with the URL, the cause, and the fix (`nexus doctor`, `~/.config/nexus/config.env`, `/connect`). A never-reachable endpoint ends the turn with guidance after a bounded wait (default 2 minutes for \"never succeeded this session\", versus the existing 20-minute recovery deadline for \"was working\").\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","create_time":1792982999.068613}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
