{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:50:57.034Z","ordinal":371239,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec01015c881a0a9cdf0b4d7619fa7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Got it—the upgrade screenshot is from `mike-dev` (`10.0.8.95`), while `10.0.8.3` is only where OpenRouter was connected. My backup-size and synthetic timing checks were on the Ubuntu desktop, so they don’t explain the hang on mike-dev. I’m switching the diagnosis to the actual host and won’t treat those Ubuntu observations as evidence about that upgrade run."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792983056112,"completed_at_ms":1792983057034}}
