{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:56:42.294Z","ordinal":371527,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5e2a53f2-338c-4f09-af15-4da4aef6aa60","process_id":"64793","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"Appliance|LOCAL_LLM|local provider|local endpoint|could not list models|connect.*provider|provider.*connect\" cli/src cli/test docs | head -160"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-backup-progress","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Appliance|LOCAL_LLM|local provider|local endpoint|could not list models|connect.*provider|provider.*connect' cli/src cli/test docs","query":"Appliance|LOCAL_LLM|local provider|local endpoint|could not list models|connect.*provider|provider.*connect","path":"cli"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:98:- **Route Fallback Re-Admission (`CTX-006`):** In `LocalLlmClient.executeWithFailover`, each endpoint attempt evaluates egress against the specific `currentEp` for that attempt. If failover switches from a local endpoint to a public endpoint, the payload is dynamically re-admitted and sanitized against the new destination boundary.\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:269:| **SUBP-002** | Accidental ambient host authority MUST NOT silently exceed configured execution authority. In bounded or restricted execution domains, subprocesses MUST NOT inherit ambient host credentials, private keys, or sensitive configuration secrets by default unless explicitly injected. An execution domain policy MAY explicitly authorize an inherited credential set for broad or full-access domains without requiring per-invocation confirmation, but credential availability within a domain MUST NOT confer disclosure authority. | In bounded execution domains, sensitive host environment variables (e.g., `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY`) are scrubbed by default unless the domain policy explicitly authorizes their presence. |\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:385:- **Multi-Provider Failover**: Specify secondary fallback endpoints via `--fallback <url1,url2>` or `$LOCAL_LLM_FALLBACK_ENDPOINTS`. Automatic failover occurs if the primary LLM server drops connection or runs out of GPU VRAM (HTTP 503).\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:138:1. **Host Authentication & Cloud Credentials:** SSH private keys (`~/.ssh/id_*`), AWS tokens (`~/.aws/credentials`), Git credentials (`~/.gitconfig`, `.token`), local config API keys (`LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY`).\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:354:  1. In `cli/src/client.ts` (lines 72–87, 209–247), `LocalLlmClient` accepts a list of fallback endpoints (`config.fallbackEndpoints`, `process.env.LOCAL_LLM_FALLBACK_ENDPOINTS`).\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:359:- **Undesirable Outcome:** Proprietary source code, local file paths, and unredacted sensitive data are silently transmitted across the network to external cloud APIs during an unannounced local endpoint failure.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:360:- **Preconditions / Reachability:** Primary endpoint local; fallback endpoint remote; local endpoint suffers connection error or timeout.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:542:- **Local Appliance vs Remote Cloud:** A local model running on localhost (e.g. vLLM or Ollama) resides inside the host/local network trust boundary. A remote provider (OpenAI, Anthropic) resides outside it.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:735:   *Add:* *\"Inference failover pools must not span different trust boundaries. Automatic fallback from a local provider to an external cloud provider is prohibited unless the request is fully re-processed through the egress data-protection pipeline.\"*\ndocs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md:22:The quickstart configures an OpenAI-compatible local endpoint. Nexus also supports explicit providers and provider-specific authentication; see [Cloud providers](CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md) for model selection, API keys, sign-in flows, endpoint disclosure, credential storage, and failure recovery. Keep credentials in the operator environment or `~/.config/nexus/config.env` with mode 0600. Never commit keys, put them in task prompts, or use real keys in examples. Project `.env` files cannot choose a cloud destination.\ndocs/DOCTOR_TROUBLESHOOTING.md:96:  \"effectiveConfig\": [{ \"key\": \"LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT\", \"value\": \"https://…/v1\", \"source\": \"~/.config/nexus/config.env\" }],\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-11.md:38:generation from gpt-5 on and Codex models; and a provider connection that is told an optional parameter is\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONVERGENCE_INVARIANT_REMEDIATION.md:60:whose `.env` holds only `LOCAL_LLM_CREDENTIAL_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:18557`, and once from an empty cwd.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONVERGENCE_INVARIANT_REMEDIATION.md:104:  (override) into the one flat `process.env`. `storedCredentialFor(url)` read `LOCAL_LLM_CREDENTIAL_ORIGINS` and\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONVERGENCE_INVARIANT_REMEDIATION.md:105:  `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT` from that `process.env`.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONVERGENCE_INVARIANT_REMEDIATION.md:107:  token goes. The same was true of `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT`, which re-homed the token-file gateway when `config.env`\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONVERGENCE_INVARIANT_REMEDIATION.md:108:  named none and the operator-env key binding. An operation spec's `apiKeyEnv: LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` could also bind\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONVERGENCE_INVARIANT_REMEDIATION.md:154:     operator `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY`).\ndocs/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md:156:- The stored token and config.env's `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` belong to config.env's `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT` origin (else\ndocs/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md:157:  `$LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT`), plus any origins listed in `LOCAL_LLM_CREDENTIAL_ORIGINS`. `$LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` belongs to\ndocs/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md:158:  `$LOCAL_L