d in another client —\ncli/src/config.ts:163: * bound to the connection's origin and never sent anywhere else. Sign-in (OAuth) providers resolve their token per\ncli/src/config.ts:219:  // `appliance: true` resolves the appliance connection regardless of any provider selection (the model picker's\ncli/src/config.ts:222:  const endpoint = provider ? providerBaseUrl(provider, options.baseUrl) : options.endpoint || effectiveSetting(\"LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT\") || DEFAULT_ENDPOINT;\ncli/src/config.ts:223:  // A cloud model is named explicitly; the appliance's LOCAL_LLM_MODEL never selects a billable cloud model.\ncli/src/config.ts:224:  const model = provider ? options.model || operatorSetting(\"NEXUS_MODEL\") || \"\" : options.model || effectiveSetting(\"LOCAL_LLM_MODEL\") || \"local-model\";\ncli/src/config.ts:226:  const operatorKey = operatorSetting(\"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\");\ncli/src/config.ts:227:  const projectApiKey = REDACTED;\ncli/src/config.ts:266:  if (provider && options.fallback) warnOnce(`--fallback is ignored for provider '${provider}': a provider connection is pinned to its own endpoint.`);\ncli/src/config.ts:293:  if (provider || options.endpoint || operatorChose(\"LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT\")) authorize(endpoint);\ncli/src/config.ts:303:  const taskClass = effectiveSetting(\"NEXUS_TASK_CLASS\") || effectiveSetting(\"LOCAL_LLM_TASK_CLASS\") || undefined;\ndocs/reviews/evidence/supervised-dogfooding-2026-10-03/dogfood3.py:8:env = dict(os.environ, HOME=f\"{S}/home\", TERM=\"xterm\", COLUMNS=\"140\", LINES=\"50\", LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=\"http://127.0.0.1:19501/v1\")\ndocs/reviews/evidence/supervised-dogfooding-2026-10-03/dogfood3.py:21:env[\"LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT\"]=\"http://127.0.0.1:19502/v1\"\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:53:| SUBP-002 | 06: Subprocess & Effect | Accidental ambient host authority MUST NOT silently exceed configured execution authority. In bounded or restricted execution domains, subprocesses MUST NOT inherit ambient host credentials, private keys, or sensitive configuration secrets by default unless explicitly injected. An execution domain policy MAY explicitly authorize an inherited credential set for broad or full-access domains without requiring per-invocation confirmation, but credential availability within a domain MUST NOT confer disclosure authority. | In bounded execution domains, sensitive host environment variables (e.g., `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY`) are scrubbed by default unless the domain policy explicitly authorizes their presence. | Phase 2 §10 | `core/src/runner.rs, cli/src/sandbox.ts, cli/src/agent.ts, cli/src/mcp.ts`; cli/test/harness.test.ts, core/tests/segregation_boundary.rs, npm test | SATISFIED_BY_INTEGRATED_SYSTEM | None | Satisfied |\ncli/src/credentials.ts:233: * The credential a provider connection uses: its environment variable, else Nexus's store, else a connection\ncli/src/credentials.ts:236:/** The API key a provider connection uses (env, Nexus store, or another client); undefined for sign-in providers. */\ndocs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/manifest-opencode.json:15:      \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/manifest-rerun-nexus-ed17e99.json:15:      \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\"\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:27:   - A repository `.env` can set `HOME`. The authority snapshot pins the `LOCAL_LLM_*` settings, but the stored\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:192:- Every run used `env -u LOCAL_LLM_*`, so this shell's operator settings never leaked in.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:198:| c. cwd `.env` `LOCAL_LLM_CREDENTIAL_ORIGINS=foreign` (original vector) | **FAKE_STORED** | none |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:199:| d. cwd `.env` `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=foreign` (re-home) | none | none |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:201:| f. dead home gateway, cwd `.env` `LOCAL_LLM_FALLBACK_ENDPOINTS=foreign` (recovery/failover) | none | none |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:205:| j. operation spec `apiKeyEnv: LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` (operator key = stored token) on a foreign resource | **FAKE_STORED** | none |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:227:  - optionally choose `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT` in the same `.env`.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:235:  `apiKeyEnv: LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` sends the frozen operator key to the project's origin even without a symlink.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md:245:- *Minor.* An unparsable operator `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT` leaves the credential origin undefined, and the client\ndocs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/manifest-aider.json:15:      \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\"\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:15:## Choosing a model and connecting providers in the live view\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:17:- `/model` opens the picker: **Recent**, then the appliance and each connected provider with its models (the current\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:18:  one marked ●) and where its credential comes from; providers not yet connected show **+ Connect …**. Type to\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:20:- **ctrl+p** in the picker (or `/connect`) opens **Connect a provider**: ✓/○ status per provider, then its methods:\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:26:  After connecting, the picker reopens on that provider's models. **ctrl+d** removes Nexus's saved credential.\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:28:  (`/model appliance qwen2.5-coder` returns to the appliance), `nexus connect <provider> [--method <id>]` (key typed\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:29:  hidden or piped on stdin) and `nexus disconnect <provider>`.\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:73:connection unless an operation spec resource names `\"providerId\"`. Embeddings are never sent to a cloud provider\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:87:  are never written into `process.env`. Only allowlisted keys (`LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT`, `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL`,\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:88:  `LOCAL_LLM_TASK_CLASS`, `NEXUS_CONTEXT_LIMIT`, and `NEXUS_PROJECT_*`) are accepted from project `.env`. All other\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:122:Each provider's key is bound to its connection's origin. A provider connection never receives the appliance gateway\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:123:token, `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY`, or another provider's key, and the appliance never receives a cloud key. Provider requests\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:145:Process-wide limits, shared by all roles and subagents and enforced before each provider-connection request (a plain\ndocs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/manifest-nexus.json:15:      \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/tui_surface_baseline/tui_surface.metrics.json:674:      \"› Fix the pa│  /model           choose a model from the appliance or any connected cloud provider          │\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/tui_surface_baseline/tui_surface.metrics.json:675:      \"            │  ctrl+p           in /model: connect a provider (API key or sign-in); /connect opens it direc│\",\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:11:Recommended first release: retain the existing appliance integration and add OpenRouter, OpenAI API, and Anthropic API through explicit provider configurations. Introduce Gemini next. Add Azure, Bedrock, and Vertex only after the provider/auth contract is stable and there is a concrete need. Start with API credentials; account OAuth/subscription connectivity is a separate integration with its own refresh, entitlement, and endpoint behavior.\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:59:Deliver a delta assessment: capabilities already present, gaps requiring change, and the smallest insertion point. If Nexus already has a provider abstraction, extend it. If the appliance gateway already exposes configured cloud routes, document that option and compare it with direct connectivity before implementing duplicate routing.\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:71:- Model reference: connection/provider plus model or deployment ID, optional variant, context/output limits, and capability overrides with provenance.\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:72:- Credential resolver: provider/connection-scoped resolution, validation, and optional refresh. No unrelated provider or appliance token fallback.\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:99:Classify authentication, permission, billing/quota, transient rate limit, overload, transport, context overflow, invalid request, protocol corruption, refusal, and operator cancellation distinctly. Apply bounded same-target retries to eligible transient failures with jitter and Retry-After support. Allow a bounded provider-owned credential refresh; do not substitute credentials from another connection. Ordinary retries must not reset task deadlines or cost budgets. A refusal must not automatically trigger provider switching to bypass the refusal.\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:113:Receipts should identify selected/effective provider, connection, model, protocol, role, attempt, reason for routing, time, usage, and cost confidence. Do not record raw auth headers or sensitive request bodies. The UI should expose usable models, credential status, selected/effective destination, and actionable errors without exposing implementation details.\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:136:Live qualification records provider/connection/model, protocol, date, test outcome, sanitized request identifiers, and usage. A source review or mock test is not a live-inference qualification. Do not infer task completion-rate improvements from connectivity support.\ndocs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:142:Suggested starting instruction: “Implement cloud inference provider support using this plan. First inspect the actual Nexus checkout and document its current appliance connectivity and all inference callers. Adapt the plan to existing abstractions; the old source snapshot is historical only. Preserve local defaults, scope credentials to each connection, require explicit cloud disclosure policy, and deliver incremental changes with the acceptance evidence listed here.”\ncli/test/provider_recovery.test.ts:133:    const e = recoveryPolicyFromEnv({ LOCAL_LLM_RECOVERY_DEADLINE_MS: \"0\", LOCAL_LLM_RECOVERY_MAX_DELAY_MS: \"5000\", LOCAL_LLM_RECOVERY_BASE_DELAY_MS: \"-3\" });\ndocs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/manifest-goose.json:15:      \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/manifest-serial-goose.json:15:      \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/manifest-rerun-nexus-4fcbe68.json:15:      \"var\": \"LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:28:| Live cloud client | Checkout build `db1ca55` (`/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/dist`), using the operator's existing provider connections: ChatGPT via the Codex CLI sign-in; OpenRouter via the crush credential. |\ncli/test/readonly_mode_escalation.test.ts:67:    await server.handleLine(JSON.stringify({ v: 1, type: \"provider.connect\", id: \"provider-1\", provider: \"openai\", method: \"api-key\", key: \"synthetic-test-key\" }));\ncli/test/readonly_mode_escalation.test.ts:70:    assert.equal(providerResult?.success, false, \"provider connections must stay disabled in read-only mode\");\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:123:| **Experimental → Supported if live-verified at RC** | OpenAI API key (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic compatible cloud | Not connected on the owner's install. They stay experimental unless keys are added and `nexus providers verify` passes at RC. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:248:| X4 | **Partly resolved 2026-10-14:** the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections are authorized for small-spend checks; both were live-verified at db1ca55. Optional: add OpenAI API-key or Anthropic keys if those providers should be listed as supported. | DEC-06 | M5 (optional) |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOGFOODING_READINESS_REVIEW_2026-10-03.md:250:5