{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T03:01:08.640Z","ordinal":371723,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17627-97a0-74a1-b26d-ec7c3300517d","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed the updated diff against base `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`; SHA-256 `2b63bb93e242cb148c8d6d0f0f1081d083ea9439018e38c1bbb79771a0672fb8`.\n\nProgress is now reported from successful write chunks, so a large single file can generate updates before it finishes. The new regression forces the reporting interval during that copy and checks for an update with `filesCopied=0` before the final count. Progress remains limited to aggregate byte and file counts. The existing file-fsync-before-directory-fsync ordering and batched directory sync remain intact.\n\nNo tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","create_time":1792983668.640156}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18238}}
