_060b64278a9dfb15016adec15b97d481a0a92d03664c204f67","order":18229,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17623-50d0-7612-a599-a618617930ea","text":"The source change now batches directory-entry syncing only after every file in that directory has been individually flushed, and sends aggregate file/byte counts without filenames or contents. I’ve added a regression case for the progress payload and directory-flush behavior; I’m checking the current upgrade’s I/O and existing test ownership before running validation.","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec21a040881a0a860bf870dc6988e","order":18234,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17626-3a31-7712-b7ff-9d011860eafb","text":"Independent review confirmed the durability ordering and privacy of the aggregate progress, and flagged one gap: a single large file could still leave the screen unchanged. I’ve updated progress to account for bytes as they are written and added a single-large-file regression. I’m keeping validation queued until the live upgrade finishes so it does not add disk pressure to the run you asked to complete.","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec27fa06c81a09454ba15c249b5a5","order":18239,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17627-c3f6-7131-b2ec-0c0518762aff","text":"The independent reviewer now accepts the backup fix, including the large-file progress case. The live upgrade is still writing (about 1.05 GB recorded so far) and remains on RC6; I’m leaving it untouched and will run the isolated regression/type checks once it exits.","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec300917c81a08518ae4ba3c833a4","order":18242,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17629-bbd0-7d93-bc62-ce396e532e40","text":"The RC6 upgrade process has exited and the upgrade lock is gone. I’m verifying the resulting journal and active launcher now; I won’t infer success from process exit alone.","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec321bb3c81a0b536db57f0ab3a30","order":18245,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1762a-3e94-7833-be5a-b54d205dc56f","text":"The backup did finish, but the upgrade rolled back before switching the launcher: it remains RC6, the lock is gone, and the completed 1.2 GB backup was retained. The journal doesn’t record the triggering error, so I’ve asked what the terminal displayed. I’m now validating the isolated fix against its focused regression tests.","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec33e281881a0bfabf7ac45965f1d","order":18246,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1762a-ac88-7063-90cf-6a6c7476117d","text":"The focused regression tests pass: all three checks passed, including in-progress byte reporting, one directory sync for a batch of files, and the existing fsync durability check. I’m checking for active suite ownership before running broader upgrade tests and the TypeScript check.","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec34d4dd481a084c146795fdc589b","order":18248,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1762a-e91b-79c0-843c-9383d0b8bebb","text":"That error pinpoints the rollback: the backup completed, then RC6 rejected GitHub’s signed release-asset redirect host as a disallowed download origin. The launcher stayed on RC6. I’ll trace the installer’s URL policy and fix it so verified GitHub asset redirects are accepted without broadening downloads to arbitrary hosts.","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":18251,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"0