{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T03:11:12.785Z","ordinal":372190,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17605-0c8f-7f42-8d4b-980a6c519c84","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec4ce7a1081a0801588a7d02d5da4","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The RC6 upgrade failure is identified: the backup finished, but RC6 rejected GitHub’s signed release-asset redirect and rolled back before switching versions. The existing backup is retained, and RC6 remains installed.\n\nI’ve prepared a fix in the isolated worktree [upgrade.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-backup-progress/cli/src/upgrade.ts) and [upgrade_journal.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-backup-progress/cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts). It narrowly allows GitHub’s HTTPS release-asset redirect, keeps signed query strings out of errors, and reports backup progress while reducing per-file directory sync overhead. An independent reviewer accepted the current diff.\n\n**This fix is not integrated yet.** Kimi owns the exclusive test-suite claim. I requested a safe-boundary release and will not take over that active claim. The focused checks passed, but I discovered they overlapped the claim, recorded the protocol incident, and will rerun them after the owner releases it. The candidate is also based on `62e541c`, behind current `origin/main` at `468646b`, so it needs rebasing and exact-revision checks before integration.\n\nAcceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; no RC or release acceptance is claimed."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792984270550,"completed_at_ms":1792984272785}}
