sor path is planned.\\n3. Whether the required coverage, author-session independence, setup/reference validation, private digest re-derivation, effective access restrictions, and immutable corpus identity have been rechecked for that path.\\n4. The next expected checkpoint or a concrete blocker requiring operator help.\\n\\nPlease do not post task payloads, hidden answers, validator contents, or private digests here. No held-out qualification will start until the custodian confirms the corpus and the evaluator boundary is independently accepted.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T02:33:48Z\"},\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-26T02:33:48Z\"}\n{\"lastComment\":{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"T4 denominator reconciliation (2026-10-22, source check at `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`): the inconsistency described in the October 18 note is no longer present in current main. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 specifies nine fault classes × five runs, including SIGTERM/resume, and PLAN-10 task 11 now says `T4 (9×5)`. The separate run-wall-time table still contains the old `8×5` estimate, but explicitly labels it historical and says it predates the nine-class correction; it is not an execution denominator.\\n\\nThis resolves the planning-text discrepancy only. T4 qualification has not run and remains gated on an accepted installed RC, frozen workload, provider/standalone prerequisites, and the other stated qualification dependencies. No threshold or denominator was changed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"},\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","create_time":1792984484.027517}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
