{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T03:15:34.167Z","ordinal":372322,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6c351646-2f0b-43f3-9fe6-76aa83d6b27a","process_id":"87309","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -120 docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.7.md; rg -n 'IN_PROGRESS|blocked|custod|T2|T3|T4|terminal|cross.runner|exact.RC|RC7' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-backup-progress","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"tail -120 docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.7.md; rg -n 'IN_PROGRESS|blocked|custod|T2|T3|T4|terminal|cross.runner|exact.RC|RC7' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -100"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.7 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\n\n## Changes since RC6\n\n- **Checkpoint recovery:** when a turn checkpoint cannot be saved, Nexus now asks how to proceed instead of silently changing permission mode or stopping without offering a choice. Depending on the failure, choices include read-only operation, continuing in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, retrying, cancelling, or entering a different instruction. If the user explicitly permits sensitive persistence and protected Git verification still fails, Nexus asks again; retry continues to use normal protected-Git verification.\n- **Terminal output safety:** streamed assistant text and echoed task prompts are sanitized at the terminal display boundary. Control and bidirectional characters, including sequences split across stream chunks, are shown as visible placeholders; secret patterns are redacted within each chunk. Known limitation: inference-server error text, the repository verifier command, worktree merge errors, and skill names still have diagnostic output paths that are not sanitized by this display boundary.\n- **Provenance reporting:** in automatic mode, the installer and upgrade attempt verification when a trusted GitHub CLI is available and report when verification cannot be performed. This replaces the RC5 and RC6 installer default, which required provenance verification; set `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` to keep requiring it or `=0` to skip it without the automatic-mode notice. Empty or invalid values are rejected, and a shell setting takes precedence over `config.env`.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.7` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n5:**Release state:** GitHub published signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7`; signed tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) succeeded. The published Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`; `SHA256SUMS` SHA-256 is `7b8a5fd1d214919ae939275e59b76406d393fae31cdf4b184c33883b02dc64a9`. RC7 is an unaccepted prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is not published.\n7:**Exact `main` source gates:** `origin/main` is `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, merging PR #243's checkpoint index-lock diagnostic fix. Exact-main CI [40248550055](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248550055) and CodeQL [40248550144](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248550144) both passed on that SHA. A clean detached checkout with isolated HOME/XDG passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals. The PR #243 diff SHA-256 `fb6b7d5d81d66cb237799b4d7a41c3dfd59f931eeaa84e75117a38bf9fc97928` matched its independently accepted diff exactly. RC7 predates this merge and cannot qualify the updated source.\n9:**RC7 artifact evidence:** The tag's release workflow produced the public assets and attestations. `gh attestation verify` passed for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS` under the exact repository, workflow, tag, and source constraints; the checksum-index attestation is [59728626](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/attestations/59728626). Cross-runner workflow [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Both manifests validated, and the archive, checksum manifest, notices, compatibility file, installer, and CycloneDX SBOM matched byte-for-byte across the two runner outputs and the public release. An isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)`. These are artifact and installation checks, not product qualification.\n11:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest comment is coordinator-authored at 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible held-out corpus disposition. Held-out T2 has not started, and no private payload was accessed. Provider/standalone qualification and T3/T4 evidence remain incomplete. The five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15, with no per-cell verdicts or required screenshots. The `cli/src/agent.ts` remediation handoff remains with KimiCode-defect-scan; implementation is still pending in that claimed lane.\n13:**Disposition:** Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is not accepted and no stable release is claimed. The next release candidate must include the merged checkpoint fix, pass exact-source CI and qualification gates, and be installed and identified before product qualification. Remaining gates include independent held-out custody and T2, provider/standalone behavior, T3/T4, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted once every required gate passes.\n19:**Release state:** GitHub lists `v1.0.0-rc.6` as the latest published prerelease. Signed tag `v1.0.0-rc.7` (tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824`) now points to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`; Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) is in progress. GitHub has not published an RC7 release or assets yet. RC6 is not an accepted RC, and no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed.\n21:**Exact `main` source gates:** Current `origin/main` is `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Post-merge CodeQL run [40243331241](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331241) passed on this exact SHA. Post-merge CI run [40243331324](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331324) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility, SBOM, smoke, and installer checks passed. At this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in a detached worktree with isolated HOME/XDG: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source gates do not constitute installed-RC acceptance.\n23:**Candidate changes:** PR #241 merged source/version preparation at `431cb194`, and signed RC7 tag `v1.0.0-rc.7` points to that exact source. PR #243 is refreshed onto exact base `431cb194` at head `a563eee0206d1287f5375a0ae113b1ca392fffd1`. Its CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed; its exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs are running in CI run [40244800085](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40244800085). Independent source review accepted the exact candidate diff. PR #244 updates only this readiness document at head `0618fbc9d123043506f76eacf9753892cdd06963`; its CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript, Node 22, and Node 24 checks passed, while Linux packaging is running in [40243816407](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243816407). PR #245 updates four manifests/lockfiles for the completed Cloudflare experiment at head `13a955dbe156daec996fd97cfe6946024a3f0b48`; CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript, Node 22, and Node 24 passed, and Linux packaging is running in [40244355480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40244355480). An independent source review accepted PR #245's exact diff. No PR has been merged on the strength of checks from another commit.\n25:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest status has no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible corpus disposition. No held-out qualification is evidenced. The Ubuntu/GNOME terminal host is now connected and its five requested terminal applications were found in a setup-only preflight; the worksheet still has all 15 cells blank, no exact RC is installed there, and no screenshot evidence exists. The five-environment by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; independent exact-RC acceptance and stable-release gates are incomplete.\n27:**Next evidence:** Finish the RC7 Release workflow and verify its exact artifact identity and provenance. Finish exact-head CI for PRs #243–245, integrate only after required review and checks, and requalify resulting main before constructing a subsequent candidate. The `cli/src/agent.ts` defect-remediation handoff is recorded for KimiCode-defect-scan; its implementation is not yet present in that branch. Resolve independent held-out custody and evaluator compatibility before beginning protected qualification; then qualify an eligible installed RC and complete the manual terminal matrix. Keep source gates, RC construction, installed-RC qualification, and stable-release checks distinct.\n31:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `1f3c655971ade086f55347926db16cf2ecd52d1f`, merging PR #161's pinned Linux builder/reproducibility changes. Exact-main CI [39957281380](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281380) completed successfully: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 jobs all passed, including the full CLI suite, security gates, requirements check, reproducible package builds, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. Exact-main CodeQL [39957281390](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281390) also passed. On a clean detached checkout of this exact SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`. These are source-gate results; the CI package is validation output, not a new published RC.\n37:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n39:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\n41:**Release disposition and next actions:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is published but unaccepted; no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL now pass on `1f3c655`; the pinned-builder documentation claim still needs a safe owner handoff and reconciliation. Continue the installed-candidate qualification lanes, resolve held-out corpus compatibility with the independent custodian, and prepare a new versioned RC only through the accepted process after its prerequisites pass. Exact-RC qualification, independent acceptance, and final publication remain gated by their evidence. Publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n45:**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\n49:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\n51:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n53:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is a published candidate, not an accepted RC. No stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. The installed command now uses RC3; RC1 remains available by its versioned path. The next critical dependency is accepted held-out custody and runner compatibility; other exact-RC gates can proceed independently where their required providers and environments are available.\n59:**Source gates:** PR #159 (`a81f79df35a76207751ffd8a86640baafca98eeb`) merged as `1b9791f`. Its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux package/reproducibility/install-smoke, and CodeQL checks passed; independent source review accepted the change. The focused Doctor schema-2 empty-history regression passed 1/1 with isolated HOME. At exact post-merge source `1b9791f`, `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes with all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`; `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passes with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. Post-merge CI run [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL run [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) are running on the exact merge commit; do not claim post-merge CI complete until both terminate successfully.\n63:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n65:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Next source action is to finish exact post-merge CI on `1b9791f`; after it passes, proceed through the accepted RC3 workflow and exact-artifact qualification. Held-out qualification remains dependent on the independent custodian and cannot start before custody and runner compatibility are accepted.\n69:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\n71:**Source requirements gate:** At exact main `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in the isolated readiness worktree with isolated HOME/XDG. It reported 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. This is the pre-RC source gate only; it does not qualify an installed RC or change any acceptance threshold.\n81:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n85:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\n89:**Source requirements gate:** At exact main `fa16045`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in a clean detached Git worktree with isolated HOME/XDG. Retained stdout is in the [exact-main enforcement record](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/requirements-enforce-main-fa16045.txt). It reported 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows are explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification. This is the pre-RC source gate only. It does not qualify an installed RC or change any requirement's acceptance threshold.\n95:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n99:The authoritative source is `origin/main@269d611ca0a0c8a55244bf70d89fa4a918b9d218`. The Node 22 convergence branch was refreshed without rewriting history and its current candidate head is `v1/node22-floor-converged@658ace9d4ab67901b5b2db1c090f6b01537be27a`; the Node `>=22` source implementation was validated at `fb798a1bd517ac85fd3c99f76d3fda1709540a8d`, and the candidate adds reviewed ruleset and acceptance-stage reconciliations. It is not yet integrated. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at version `1.0.0-rc.2`. The source requirements check currently fails because REQ-REL-111 remains partial pending exact-candidate checks; REQ-REL-003 remains partial for installed-RC platform qualification and is now explicitly mapped to ACC-PLAT in the exact-RC stage. No threshold or qualification evidence was changed.\n103:PR #149 is open at `1972adb8a6d4b9bacf9974f33974b61d751de8ab` on base `269d611`; Node 20/22/24 matrix checks and CodeQL pass, while its exact-head Linux packaging job is still running. Its independent source review accepted the T3 symlink hardening, but it is not integrated until the required job concludes.\n105:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n109:`origin/main` is now `dceac980b3d77c99a26bb9ddedb61c443168952a`, after PR #142 merged as `08861feb2c6a164a89f4c0573e1c7793c9f938e5` and PR #143 merged as `dceac980b3d77c99a26bb9ddedb61c443168952a`. PR #143 corrects the Node 20 EOL date in the RC1 release note; independent review accepted its exact net diff, and exact-head CI `39769489238` plus CodeQL `39769489243` passed on PR head `5e1f221e920bf6738fb3d62296199f34c8db53a0` against base `08861fe`. Post-merge CI `39773603423` and CodeQL `39773603376` are running on exact `main@dceac980`; no post-merge conclusion is claimed yet. Contest work is over and no contest freeze applies. Campaign status remains `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC1 remains an older artifact, and no stable v1.0.0 release is asserted.\n115:**Requirements and acceptance:** I reran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` at 09:34 UTC from a clean detached worktree at exact source `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, with isolated HOME/XDG; it exited 0 and reported 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 requirements explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification in `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1. The checker output is reproducible from that source revision. This is a source-stage gate only; it does not establish RC qualification or acceptance. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.\n117:**Evaluator containment and Git isolation:** Source tests cover CPU, memory, process-count, storage limits, process cleanup, solution-bearing Git refs/reflogs/dangling objects, and external canary stores in `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts`. PR #140 records a separate exact-source synthetic host preflight with 10/10 checks; its merge and CI do not establish held-out qualification. The public held-out manifest records 40 T2 tasks, ten each across four task classes and four languages; this metadata does not prove private digest re-derivation, author-session independence, effective access controls, custody acceptance, or qualification readiness. No private payloads or validators were accessed for this checkpoint.\n119:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n130:- The source requirements gate remains a clean-worktree pass on exact integration `7d6673f`; eleven requirements remain deferred to exact-RC qualification as listed in the checkpoint below. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; this CI progression does not establish RC readiness or acceptance.\n138:**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n143:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n145:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\n153:**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n155:Exact-source CI and requirements enforcement pass on `8f4504e`, but held-out custody and corpus compatibility, installed-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and final publication remain incomplete. No v1.0.0 RC or stable release exists. Publication authorization is granted and remains gated on acceptance.\n162:- **PR and contest state:** PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-`main` candidate. Its CI and CodeQL checks are green, but it is not a release acceptance or publication. PR #102 is open at `3756afe05dbd75c4e6929d87cd50facbb8ab1748`, based on `8f4504e`, to record a synthetic qualification-host preflight; its CodeQL and TypeScript checks passed and its Node matrix was still running at this checkpoint. The preflight report records 10/10 checks using only an empty synthetic marker store; it does not establish private corpus custody or qualification acceptance. The contest has concluded; no contest freeze applies. Historical contest artifacts remain historical evidence only.\n163:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\n164:- **Evaluator and qualification-host boundary:** Source fixtures for cgroup resource limits, process-tree cleanup, workspace storage, and staged Git-history isolation are in the integration source suite and passed its exact-source CI. A synthetic host preflight at source `8f4504e` recorded 10/10 checks and is being documented in PR #102. Neither source fixtures nor the synthetic-host report establish access separation against the custodian's real store or permit held-out execution before custody acceptance.\n165:- **Held-out corpus and custody:** Public T2 manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` remains the 40-task identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`; T3 public manifest identity remains `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4bfa0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response since 2026-10-21 12:21 UTC. Current evaluator qualification rejects the sealed T2 corpus's legacy `hidden.command` format; the documented path requires a custodian-owned compatible immutable successor and repeated custody checks. Private digest re-derivation, exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective access separation, and current custody acceptance remain unverified here. No payload, validator, reference solution, or hidden answer was accessed, and no held-out run has started.\n166:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n180:- **Held-out custody and qualification:** The custodian previously accepted the sealed 40-task manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b` and its private digest/reference validation. This does not establish evaluator acceptance or T2 qualification. The implementing agent has not accessed private payloads. No held-out run has started because evaluator confidentiality preflight remains unaccepted and corpus/evaluator schema compatibility is unresolved.\n181:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\n190:- **Evaluator boundary and T2 custody:** PR #33's exact source CI passes resource-bound and Git-history canary fixtures, but the independent unconditional-system-mount finding remains open. Separately, the custodian report accepts the sealed manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, its custody, author-session provenance, private digest validation, and reference validation; private payloads were not inspected for this checkpoint. The sealed tasks use legacy `hidden: { dir, into, command }` checks, while evaluator qualification requires `blackbox-v1`. Custody acceptance does not resolve this format mismatch or evaluator-boundary acceptance. No T2 qualification has started.\n191:- **Qualification host and terminal:** Qualification-host tooling is integrated through PR #31 (`8c0ab7b`), but this checkpoint has no evidence that the qualification host was provisioned and validated at `4bce876`. Terminal acceptance procedure is integrated; the required human matrix remains unexecuted. It requires five environments × three sizes on the exact installed RC, with per-cell PASS/FAIL and screenshots of the approval panel and post-exit state.\n192:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\n198:- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`. The earlier reported `2c70d39` and `d2c4bfc` are ancestors of this revision; they are not competing integration heads. PR #9 and PR #23 are integrated as `64ee88b` and `886766b`; PR #24's terminal acceptance kit is integrated at `5193984`. Exact-head integration CI run [39120013759](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39120013759) is in progress, so there is no current-head green claim yet. PR #24's checks passed on its exact head `91eaee9` in run [39117464186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39117464186); its accepted procedure does not replace the human terminal matrix.\n201:- **Qualification host:** PR #22 is still based on `a7126aa` (head `7d30494`); its historical exact-head CI passed, but it is not current-base evidence. The owner confirmed the file split with PR #26 and requested owner approval before running `eval/host/provision.sh`. No host account, sudoers, mount unit, or runtime directory has been provisioned. Resource-limit qualification and held-out execution remain blocked until this host boundary is installed and validated.\n202:- **Held-out T2 custody:** The custodian reported re-derived manifest, 40 task, and 40 private-payload digest matches; isolated author-session audits; and 40/40 reference validation. The public manifest identity is `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`. At 10:38:44 UTC the custodian recorded moving the store and quarantine to `root:root` mode `0700` (task/reference subdirectories `0500`) without changing contents or manifest identity, and explicitly accepted sealed-manifest custody under this boundary. Coordinator verification was limited to metadata (`stat`, `namei`, and a denied `ls` as uid `mike`); private payloads were not inspected. This is custody evidence, not T2 qualification: held-out execution remains blocked on host provisioning, frozen resources, and an installed RC.\n204:- **T3 and terminal lanes:** PR #27 T3 harness head `12edf74` has independent code review ACCEPT. Its CI run [39119197191](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119197191) has the contest-contract and Node 20/22/24 jobs successful; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress. The custodian recorded an 8/8-task T3 corpus seal at 10:43:02 UTC, with corrected private manifest digest `dcbd794ed2998423787fdead4957b38b0c4a8a641855d87304d065d01c3fae37` at 10:43:22 UTC, and released both authoring claims. This is sealed, custodian-validated corpus evidence; no T3 qualification run has occurred. PR #24's real-terminal procedure is integrated, but all required five environments × three sizes still require the exact installed RC and genuine operator evidence; no matrix cell is claimed complete.\n205:- **RC and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-main candidate. No RC artifact, exact-RC test, cross-runner RC comparison, installed provider/standalone run, T2/T3/T4 qualification, or independent RC acceptance exists. Final stable publication remains authorized but gated on all mandatory exact-RC acceptance and release checks.\n210:- **Sealed held-out T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`, PR [#16](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/16), merged at `f776903`):**\n211:  - Committed public manifest: `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`), containing 40 external-repository T2 tasks pinned to full 40-hex baseline commits across Go (10), JavaScript (10), Python (10), and Rust (10), and across bugfix (10), debug (10), feature (10), and refactor (10).\n212:  - Custody record: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` (updated at `ce3f590`).\n213:  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n217:  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\n219:  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\n254:## Historical evidence: Security and T2 update (2026-10-17)\n266:- The earlier v12 (`82886448799cb9c63d28a8f5f28b940229b981a51982c49bad80b7f7d2c73092`), v15 (`6f78983cc860a4ed616f5aa5375b8d3fec5b7335ea6bac47a448924dc91af06d`), and v16 T2 pilot packages and their failed Docker validation attempts remain historical evidence only.\n274:- Automated PTY acceptance tests are included in the passing CLI suite. This is not human interaction in each required terminal emulator.\n275:- The source suite includes the T1 evaluator smoke and two-fault T4 smoke. These do not establish the full T2, T3, T4 qualification thresholds.\n281:| `REQ-AGT-002` | partial | Zero false `VERIFIED` across the frozen qualification workloads; source regression tests pass (`1,152/1,152` at `a7126aa`) but no held-out evaluation exists. | T2/T3/T4 RC runs | Qualification operator | Run the preregistered acceptance set on an installed RC and retain per-run evidence; fix and repeat any false `VERIFIED`. |\n286:| `REQ-REL-005` | partial (RR) | Candidate source security gates passed on `a7126aa` (run `39108774170`); exact-RC artifact/security evidence is pending RC tag construction. `security_gates.sh` requires `cargo-deny` or `cargo-audit` and fails closed when neither is installed (`ACC-SUP-04`). | Exact RC and `ACC-SUP-05` release CI matrix | Release engineering | On the frozen RC tag, run and archive the release workflow security evidence. |\n293:| `REQ-QUAL-101` | tested (corpus sealed at `f776903`; live T2 run pending) | The 40-task external-repository T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`) is sealed and committed in `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, PR #16 `f776903`, custody record `ce3f590`). Independent metadata review (`codex-lead`) accepted the public manifest structure/digest; private payload validation (40/40, 2 rounds each) and author-isolation audits are custodian-recorded with store permissions `0700`/`0500`. | Qualification-host provisioning, frozen resource config, installed RC, peer calibration | Custodian and qualification operator | Keep `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` restricted from implementation agents; complete qualification-host provisioning and execute the 5-run T2 matrix on the installed RC. |\n295:| `REQ-QUAL-102` | tested as harness control | Missing fingerprint and mismatched comparison settings are rejected by tests; no live matched model/configuration record exists. | Frozen RC, identified model/server, task corpus | Qualification operator | Before each comparison, record and verify exact RC, weights hash, server build, sampling, context/output limits, allowlisted environment and equal task budgets in every run manifest. |\n296:| `REQ-QUAL-103` | tested as harness control | Five-run pair validation and peer configuration forwarding are tested; no live matched T2 results exist. | Sealed T2 set, RC, peers on same model | Qualification operator | Run five serial repetitions for each task/configuration for Nexus, Goose and OpenCode; retain original and replacement records and paired score inputs. |\n297:| `REQ-QUAL-104` | tested as scorer control | The separate metrics and scorer are tested; threshold outcomes and zero-false-`VERIFIED` have not been measured on qualification workloads. | Completed T2/T3/T4 evidence | Qualification operator | Score every preregistered metric separately and apply the fixed thresholds and confidence intervals; any false `VERIFIED` fails the hard gate. |\n300:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\n301:| `REQ-QUAL-109` | open | No T3 evidence for 8 tasks × 5 runs, each ≥60 steps with ≥2 compactions and steering; thresholds are false-absence 0 and steering ≥95%. | Frozen T3 workload, RC, gateway capacity | Qualification operator | Freeze/register T3 tasks before execution, then run all repetitions and score using the accepted rules. |\n311:| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n312:| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\n321:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\n328:- **Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`. **Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`. RC5 is a public prerelease; neither an accepted RC nor stable v1.0.0 is claimed.\n330:- **Source CI:** run [40190718023](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40190718023) and CodeQL [40190718020](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40190718020) passed on the exact main revision. Requirements enforcement passed: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; the 12 mapped exact-RC qualification rows remain deferred and enforced as such.\n337:- E2 is **partial**: all eight fresh-install/minimum-runtime cells and eight expected negative preflight cells passed across the prepared Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 images. One Ubuntu 22.04 / Node 22 lifecycle cell passed alpha.2 upgrade, repair, rollback and uninstall. The remaining lifecycle cases are not complete. Current-source evaluator host preflight passed 10/10 using synthetic markers only; this is not held-out custody or qualification evidence.\n338:- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\n344:- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n350:| T2/T3 held-out custody | Blocked. Issue #1 has no custodian reply; the public 40-task manifest does not establish private custody acceptance, and the legacy validator contract is incompatible with the current evaluator. No private payload was accessed or run. | Independent custodian confirms author/handoff, compatible immutable corpus or successor, validation, access separation, digests and custody acceptance; only then prepare and execute the approved runs. |\n351:| Evaluator resource/secret boundary | Synthetic current-source host preflight 10/10; no accepted qualification-host/custody result. | Complete independent host and custody acceptance before any held-out execution. |\n352:| Standalone profiles | Not run on the installed RC; T2 subset dependency remains unmet. | After custody and frozen configuration, execute §4.2 profiles and archive exact-artifact receipts. |\n353:| T4 and long-task T3 | Not run. T4 remains nine fault classes × five runs; T3 remains eight tasks × five runs. | Freeze approved workload/configurations and prerequisites, then run exact RC serially with independent scoring. |\n355:| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\n356:| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":956588429}},"started_at_ms":1792984533210,"completed_at_ms":1792984534167}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T03:15:35.608Z","ordinal":372323,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17634-d237-7230-ae4d-25324965c945","call_id":"call_54497af6637046ee84276f99766c6f96","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12741)\nTotal output lines: 112\n\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.7 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\n\n## Changes since RC6\n\n- **Checkpoint recovery:** when a turn checkpoint cannot be saved, Nexus now asks how to proceed instead of silently changing permission mode or stopping without offering a choice. Depending on the failure, choices include read-only operation, continuing in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, retrying, cancelling, or entering a different instruction. If the user explicitly permits sensitive persistence and protected Git verification still fails, Nexus asks again; retry continues to use normal protected-Git verification.\n- **Terminal output safety:** streamed assistant text and echoed task prompts are sanitized at the terminal display boundary. Control and bidirectional characters, including sequences split across stream chunks, are shown as visible placeholders; secret patterns are redacted within each chunk. Known limitation: inference-server error text, the repository verifier command, worktree merge errors, and skill names still have diagnostic output paths that are not sanitized by this display boundary.\n- **Provenance reporting:** in automatic mode, the installer and upgrade attempt verification when a trusted GitHub CLI is available and report when verification cannot be performed. This replaces the RC5 and RC6 installer default, which required provenance verification; set `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` to keep requiring it or `=0` to skip it without the automatic-mode notice. Empty or invalid values are rejected, and a shell setting takes precedence over `config.env`.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.7` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n5:**Release state:** GitHub published signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7`; signed tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) succeeded. The published Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`; `SHA256SUMS` SHA-256 is `7b8a5fd1d214919ae939275e59b76406d393fae31cdf4b184c33883b02dc64a9`. RC7 is an unaccepted prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is not published.\n7:**Exact `main` source gates:** `origin/main` is `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, merging PR #243's checkpoint index-lock diagnostic fix. Exact-main CI [40248550055](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248550055) and CodeQL [40248550144](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248550144) both passed on that SHA. A clean detached checkout with isolated HOME/XDG passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals. The PR #243 diff SHA-256 `fb6b7d5d81d66cb237799b4d7a41c3dfd59f931eeaa84e75117a38bf9fc97928` matched its independently accepted diff exactly. RC7 predates this merge and cannot qualify the updated source.\n9:**RC7 artifact evidence:** The tag's release workflow produced the public assets and attestations. `gh attestation verify` passed for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS` under the exact repository, workflow, tag, and source constraints; the checksum-index attestation is [59728626](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/attestations/59728626). Cross-runner workflow [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Both manifests validated, and the archive, checksum manifest, notices, compatibility file, installer, and CycloneDX SBOM matched byte-for-byte across the two runner outputs and the public release. An isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)`. These are artifact and installation checks, not product qualification.\n11:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest comment is coordinator-authored at 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible held-out corpus disposition. Held-out T2 has not started, and no private payload was accessed. Provider/standalone qualification and T3/T4 evidence remain incomplete. The five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15, with no per-cell verdicts or required screenshots. The `cli/src/agent.ts` remediation handoff remains with KimiCode-defect-scan; implementation is still pending in that claimed lane.\n13:**Disposition:** Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is not accepted and no stable release is claimed. The next release candidate must include the merged checkpoint fix, pass exact-source CI and qualification gates, and be installed and identified before product qualification. Remaining gates include independent held-out custody and T2, provider/standalone behavior, T3/T4, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted once every required gate passes.\n19:**Release state:** GitHub lists `v1.0.0-rc.6` as the latest published prerelease. Signed tag `v1.0.0-rc.7` (tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824`) now points to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`; Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) is in progress. GitHub has not published an RC7 release or assets yet. RC6 is not an accepted RC, and no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed.\n21:**Exact `main` source gates:** Current `origin/main` is `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Post-merge CodeQL run [40243331241](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331241) passed on this exact SHA. Post-merge CI run [40243331324](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331324) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility, SBOM, smoke, and i…9241 tokens truncated…cord and verify exact RC, weights hash, server build, sampling, context/output limits, allowlisted environment and equal task budgets in every run manifest. |\n296:| `REQ-QUAL-103` | tested as harness control | Five-run pair validation and peer configuration forwarding are tested; no live matched T2 results exist. | Sealed T2 set, RC, peers on same model | Qualification operator | Run five serial repetitions for each task/configuration for Nexus, Goose and OpenCode; retain original and replacement records and paired score inputs. |\n297:| `REQ-QUAL-104` | tested as scorer control | The separate metrics and scorer are tested; threshold outcomes and zero-false-`VERIFIED` have not been measured on qualification workloads. | Completed T2/T3/T4 evidence | Qualification operator | Score every preregistered metric separately and apply the fixed thresholds and confidence intervals; any false `VERIFIED` fails the hard gate. |\n300:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\n301:| `REQ-QUAL-109` | open | No T3 evidence for 8 tasks × 5 runs, each ≥60 steps with ≥2 compactions and steering; thresholds are false-absence 0 and steering ≥95%. | Frozen T3 workload, RC, gateway capacity | Qualification operator | Freeze/register T3 tasks before execution, then run all repetitions and score using the accepted rules. |\n311:| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n312:| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\n321:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\n328:- **Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`. **Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`. RC5 is a public prerelease; neither an accepted RC nor stable v1.0.0 is claimed.\n330:- **Source CI:** run [40190718023](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40190718023) and CodeQL [40190718020](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40190718020) passed on the exact main revision. Requirements enforcement passed: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; the 12 mapped exact-RC qualification rows remain deferred and enforced as such.\n337:- E2 is **partial**: all eight fresh-install/minimum-runtime cells and eight expected negative preflight cells passed across the prepared Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 images. One Ubuntu 22.04 / Node 22 lifecycle cell passed alpha.2 upgrade, repair, rollback and uninstall. The remaining lifecycle cases are not complete. Current-source evaluator host preflight passed 10/10 using synthetic markers only; this is not held-out custody or qualification evidence.\n338:- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\n344:- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n350:| T2/T3 held-out custody | Blocked. Issue #1 has no custodian reply; the public 40-task manifest does not establish private custody acceptance, and the legacy validator contract is incompatible with the current evaluator. No private payload was accessed or run. | Independent custodian confirms author/handoff, compatible immutable corpus or successor, validation, access separation, digests and custody acceptance; only then prepare and execute the approved runs. |\n351:| Evaluator resource/secret boundary | Synthetic current-source host preflight 10/10; no accepted qualification-host/custody result. | Complete independent host and custody acceptance before any held-out execution. |\n352:| Standalone profiles | Not run on the installed RC; T2 subset dependency remains unmet. | After custody and frozen configuration, execute §4.2 profiles and archive exact-artifact receipts. |\n353:| T4 and long-task T3 | Not run. T4 remains nine fault classes × five runs; T3 remains eight tasks × five runs. | Freeze approved workload/configurations and prerequisites, then run exact RC serially with independent scoring. |\n355:| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\n356:| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","create_time":1792984535.6079388}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
