ithub.fetch_issue_comments"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a15643-db25-7cb0-b19b-b1f34bd3c2da","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.update_issue_comment"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15691-fa03-7062-973a-b4e3eaf95fd0","server_name":"codex_app","tool_name":"send_message_to_thread"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156d7-4dfd-7141-94cc-a0e69c18c919","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.mark_pull_request_ready_for_review"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_repo"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.list_pr_changed_filenames"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_pr_diff"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec6293c2481a0b866d2220dd2dd96","order":18265,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17636-136b-7670-b32e-7911c7784b01","text":"While both current-main CI and Kimi’s recovery investigation run, I can preserve the reviewed upgrade fix as a local commit and rebase its isolated branch onto `main@468646b`. That won’t touch the shared checkout or start another test run; exact validation remains queued behind the active suite claim.","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec64a813081a08e4ea5db18c0deef","order":18267,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17636-95c7-71d1-b50d-b4b6cba9dd7e","text":"Kimi’s test processes have ended and the exclusive suite claim is now released. I’ll rerun the upgrade tests and type check on rebased head `64c22d3`; then, if they pass, I’ll run the full required suite under an exclusive claim and prepare the exact-head PR.","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec6d2379881a0820067871a5cf7eb","order":18271,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17638-a753-7133-8963-8e77729b1883","text":"I caught a test-environment mistake: the transaction test was started without the required isolated `HOME` and is writing a backup under the real `/home/mike/.nexus`. I’m stopping only the test processes I started, preserving whatever files they created. I will not delete or repair that state automatically.","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec6ef399881a08187472284efaa0d","order":18272,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17639-1963-7ff0-9ee7-312fa0581b45","text":"I stopped the transaction test once I confirmed it was writing into real Nexus state. It left a 29 MB partial backup without backup metadata and two zero-byte guard files; I’ve left all of them untouched. Kimi’s recovery suite has since completed and its claim is released, so I’m recording this incident and will rerun the transaction checks with an isolated home directory.","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec7268bcc81a08f66762d0e627490","order":18274,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17639-f103-7023-a5c0-52e1dd28e420","text":"The transaction recovery suite now passes 47/47 on rebased head `64c22d3` with an isolated HOME. The earlier interrupted run’s partial backup remains untouched. The independent reviewer also re-accepted the unchanged patch against current `main`; I’m rerunning the other focused checks under the same isolation before requesting exact-head CI.","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec7458e0c81a0ba95a28f8ec2a22e","order":18275,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1763a-6b63-7df3-aee1-3b02d13ffca5","text":"Both upgrade-focused suites pass under isolated HOME: backup/transaction recovery 47/47 and upgrade safety 34/34. TypeScript checking also passes. I’m checking the repository’s full-suite command, then I’ll claim the suite lane and run it from a clean snapshot of `64c22d3`.","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec760362881a097c7b0535cef8a23","order":18276,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1763a-d5f7-7860-821a-742150984f4f","text":"Another agent acquired the suite lane for a full provider-candidate run just before my atomic claim attempt, so I correctly did not start a competing full suite. I’m using that wait to refresh the current-source requirements and version gates; the upgrade fix remains committed, rebased, and independently accepted, with its full-suite check pending.","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adec791065081a0b6cd888dc85ec180","order":18277,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1763b-91b5-77f1-9840-a823c5704c43","text":"The source gate passes at the exact candidate, but I’m tightening one validation gap before calling this ready: the existing tests check that the new GitHub host/path is allowlisted, while the failing real path was a redirect during an actual download. I’m checking whether the test harness can exercise that full redirect flow without making a network request.","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":18281,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco