{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:00:35.028Z","ordinal":374589,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-06638af6-c193-4603-880d-be6c99c50452","process_id":"17394","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'rc tag|release candidate|publish|github release|tag workflow|semantic-release|version-only' docs/v1.0.0 .github/workflows scripts | head -80; gh release view v1.0.0-rc.8 --json tagName,isDraft,isPrerelease,publishedAt,url 2>&1 || true; node -p \"require('./package.json').version\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i 'rc tag|release candidate|publish|github release|tag workflow|semantic-release|version-only' docs/v1.0.0 .github/workflows scripts | head -80; gh release view v1.0.0-rc.8 --json tagName,isDraft,isPrerelease,publishedAt,url 2>&1 || true; node -p \"require('./package.json').version\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/README.md:15:| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\nscripts/check_requirements.mjs:246:      if (typeof record.rcTag !== \"string\" || !/^v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+-rc\\.\\d+$/.test(record.rcTag)) throw new Error(\"RC tag does not point to the current source commit\");\nscripts/check_requirements.mjs:248:      try { taggedCommit = git(\"rev-parse\", `${record.rcTag}^{commit}`); } catch { throw new Error(\"RC tag does not point to the current source commit\"); }\nscripts/check_requirements.mjs:249:      if (taggedCommit !== sourceCommit) throw new Error(\"RC tag does not point to the current source commit\");\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the RC commit | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (ledger enforce mode, final statuses); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:27:| Published package used for installer checks | `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (`a2e94f3`). Assets: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v0.1.0-alpha.2.tar.gz` and `SHA256SUMS`. Installed in scratch HOMEs, plus the operator's existing `~/.local/lib/nexus/v0.1.0-alpha.2` (read only). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:77:5. **Nothing was committed, pushed, tagged, deployed or published by the audit.**\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:48:| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:87:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:3:This is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:24:1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:63:1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:86:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:271:| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 20 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:323:| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:327:G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:342:- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:344:After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:32:| 7 | Server-kind conformance fixtures, built from each project's published API docs with version and source references recorded: llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama. Covers `/models`/`/props`/`/api/v0/models`/`/api/show` shapes, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies. Also record real SSE through the gateway (llama.cpp workers) with `scripts/record_sse.mjs`. Add a replay test. | `cli/test/fixtures/sse/<server>/<case>.sse`; `inference_transport.test.ts` | — (no extra hardware; DEC-16) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:66:2. For vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama, write the fixtures from each project's published API documentation and source. Record the project version and the doc URL in each fixture header.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:49:- **ACC-SUP-03.** Run `gh attestation verify` in a post-release verification job against the published asset.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:15:| C7 | Publish the video's source commits under a tag (`contest-video-2026-10`) together with the run record, or state in the docs that they are unpublished. | git tag push (owner-approved) | Medium |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:196:- Response-shape fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama are written from each project's published API documentation, with source references and versions recorded. They cover `/models`, `/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:218:| X7 | Approve publishing `v1.0.0-rc.N` and `v1.0.0` (tag push triggers public release) | Release | M6 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:22:| Installed launchers | `~/.local/bin/nexus` → published package `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (`a2e94f3`), **first on PATH**. `/usr/local/bin/nexus` → `~/nexus-code/harness.sh` (checkout build, reports `0.1.0-alpha.2 (db1ca5580860, main)`). Plain `nexus` on this host therefore runs the published package, not the checkout. | RT |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:24:| External dependencies | Node ≥ 20 (runtime), GitHub Releases (installer), optional bubblewrap/Docker (sandbox), optional cloud providers (OpenRouter, OpenAI, Anthropic, ChatGPT/Copilot OAuth, compatible), optional MCP servers, DuckDuckGo (default `search_web`). | SRC |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:35:`nexus eval` (the SWE-bench-style command) scores the repo's last commit instead of the agent's change, and runs `git checkout` in the operator's workspace (VER-07). It must not be used for any published number.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:17:| REL-05 | The release archive contains only the project LICENSE. About 150 Rust crates (MIT/Apache-2.0 and others) are statically linked into `harness-core` and `nexus-tui`, with no attribution. No SBOM is published. | RUNTIME + SOURCE (`scripts/package-linux.sh:22`) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:26:| HIST-07 | There is no SECURITY.md vulnerability intake, yet the repository is public and releases are published, so REL-004's patch obligation is live. | SOURCE |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:42:3. **REQ-REL-109.** Release assets carry verifiable provenance (DEC-09: `actions/attest-build-provenance`). The installer can optionally verify it when `gh` is present. The installer is also published as a release asset, so a tag-pinned installer exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:28:| CON-004 | S2 | The video's source commits are not published. | SOURCE (git) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:48:7. **REQ-CON-107.** The video's source commits and run record are published under a tag. Otherwise the docs say plainly that they are unpublished.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:50:| REQ-REL-06..09 | REL-001..004 | Lockfile provenance; SHA-256 + commit-bound release identity; SBOM hooks; patch obligations for supported public lines, EOL marking | P2 §23 | DEMONSTRATED (generate_sbom.sh; make verify-reproducibility) | P | Maturity review 10-12 P1: SBOM from direct deps only, not CycloneDX-validated; top-tier D4 no signing/provenance. Since 10-13: deterministic archive + CI reproducibility (87360e6, fa0959f), SHA256SUMS in releases. REL-004 now live obligation (repo PUBLIC, releases published) with no SECURITY.md process (D4) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:81:| REQ-DX-01 | Install promise | Linux x86-64 glibc≥2.35, Node≥20; installer verifies SHA-256; no root, no shell rc edits; manual uninstall keeps user data | quickstart.md:7-27,59-68; DEVELOPMENT.md:19 | Published alpha.2 (release run 38539108878) | N |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/BRIEF.md:11:- No publishing, deploys, pushes, paid API calls, live-infrastructure mutation. Do not print credentials; redact any secret values (config.env, .env, tokens).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:5:- **Contest:** the code and its local tests are real and fail closed. But **no fresh-account Cloudflare-backed run is possible from the published tree**. The documented deploy deploys the wrong Worker, and CI checks the wrong Worker. The deadline was 2026-10-14, which is today (CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:11).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:81:| CON-004 | S2 (contest) | Provenance of submitted evidence | docs/cloudflare/VIDEO_ASSET.md:17-19; docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:5 | SOURCE (git). The video's recorded source commits are `731f5d44…` (Nexus) and `98a8a813…` (contest-demo). Neither is an ancestor of main. They exist only on local branches (`dogfood/*`, `candidate/*`, `contest-demo`) and are on no remote-tracking branch. The run record and freeze manifest the doc cites are not committed. VIDEO_ASSET itself records a CLI bundle hash delta and says \"No clean Cloudflare-backed replay has been made from the target tree\". | Judges cannot tie the video to published source. The video is HISTORICAL evidence of an operator-host run only. | Publish the run record and freeze manifest, plus a tag or branch containing 98a8a813. Alternatively, state plainly that the source behind the video is unpublished. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:92:| EVL-001 | S1 (v1 task-quality claim) | Qualification evidence | eval/README.md:42,47-58; docs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md:62-63 | DOC-CLAIM + SOURCE. The only scored evidence is 6 in-repo T2 fixture tasks. RESULT.md itself says \"These six tasks were used to find and fix the issues … it does not qualify Nexus. Qualification needs a fresh task set.\" Missing: held-out tasks, the T3 long-task set, the T4 fault injector, the T3 fact-sheet scorer, and runs on the release candidate. The measured builds are 76f4081, ed17e99 and 4fcbe68-dirty; their rebased equivalents (fe576f1, d116e99, 0090f9c) are on main, but db1ca55 itself was never evaluated. | No basis for a v1 claim about task quality. The pilot verdict was \"NOT QUALIFIED (false VERIFIED=2)\". The rerun had 0 false VERIFIED, but on tuned tasks. | A v1 protocol is in §7. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:168:| CON-R5 | The video's source commits and run record are published (tag) | evidence | RELEASE-REQUIRED (contest) | `git branch -r --contains 98a8a813` is non-empty |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:58:| VER-07 | S2 | `nexus eval` benchmark scores | evaluator.ts:128, 155-166, 173-190, 213 | SOURCE. (a) `git checkout base_commit` runs in the operator's workspace before the worktree exists, and failure is ignored. (b) The patch is `git diff HEAD~1..HEAD`, the last commit and not the agent's change, so `hasCodeChanges` is true for almost any repo with history. (c) A `test_patch` apply failure is swallowed and grading continues on the existing suite. (d) `fail_to_pass`/`pass_to_pass` are ignored and the whole suite runs via detectTestCommand (`npm test` fallback). (e) `testRes.command === \"none\"` is unreachable. Net effect: an agent that does nothing on a repo whose tests pass scores RESOLVED. evaluator.test.ts never calls `evaluateInstance`. ISSUE12 matrices mark EXEC-011 \"DEMONSTRATED\". | Any published `nexus eval` pass rate is invalid. The workspace HEAD may be detached unexpectedly. | BLOCKER for any benchmark claim; otherwise RELEASE-REQUIRED: remove the command or label it experimental, or fix it (diff vs base in the worktree, fail on test_patch error, run FAIL_TO_PASS/PASS_TO_PASS ids, never touch the operator checkout). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:140:| R-VER-7 | `nexus eval` is either removed/hidden or grades by FAIL_TO_PASS/PASS_TO_PASS against a base-relative worktree diff. It fails on test_patch errors and never touches the operator checkout. | honesty | BLOCKER only if benchmark numbers are published; else POST-V1 (hide) | Fixture instance where the agent makes no change → UNRESOLVED. A broken test_patch → ERROR. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:3:Auditor: scope E agent, 2026-10-14. Repo HEAD db1ca55. Published releases are v0.1.0-alpha.1 (61057cf) and v0.1.0-alpha.2 (a2e94f3). Both are prereleases, and no stable release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:28:| Published release assets | `gh release view` + installed and executed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:62:| REL-04 | S2 | versioning | core/Cargo.toml:3 (`1.2.1`) vs package.json:3 / cli/package.json:3 (`0.1.0-alpha.2`); doctor.ts:491-492; local tags v1.1.0/v1.2.0/v1.2.1 | RUNTIME. A fresh clean install gives `WARN engine.binary: The engine reports version 1.2.1, the CLI 0.1.0-alpha.2 → Rebuild with make build`. Every release user sees a warning, and its remedy is impossible in a packaged install (there is no Makefile). Local v1.x tags (not on origin, not ancestors of main, no release.yml at those commits, so not publishable by accident) conflict with the future v1.0.0 ordering. | A permanent false warning on a healthy install trains users to ignore doctor. Version identity is inconsistent across components. | Single-source the version: release workflow asserts Cargo.toml == package.json == cli/package.json == tag. Delete stale local v1.x tags. Make doctor remedies context-aware (packaged → \"reinstall\"). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:63:| REL-05 | S2 | compliance | scripts/package-linux.sh:22; release assets | RUNTIME + SOURCE. The archive contains only the project LICENSE. About 150 Rust crates are statically linked (Cargo.lock: 152 packages, MIT/Apache-2.0 etc.), and there is no third-party notice for them. Node deps ship their own LICENSE files (20 found). No SBOM is published. | MIT/Apache attribution obligations are not met for redistributed binaries. Enterprise intake (SBOM) is blocked. | Generate THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES (cargo-about / cargo-deny licenses + npm license list) and a real lockfile-based SBOM, and attach both to releases. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:76:| MNT-05 | S4 | changelog | docs/releases/*.md; release.yml:47 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. The GitHub release bodies are only \"Full Changelog: compare…\". The curated notes in docs/releases are not attached, and there is no CHANGELOG.md. | Users on GitHub do not see known limits or breaking changes (e.g. `spawn_subagent max_steps` removed). | Use `body_path: docs/releases/${tag}.md`, and fail the release if the file is missing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:126:  - The full test suite, including PTY TUI e2e, runs before publish (CI log: 905/905).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:130:  - Published assets match the docs (2 assets each; alpha.1 and alpha.2 marked prerelease; `gh release view`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:137:- **Cross-machine reproducibility is unproven.** The CI repro check runs on the same runner with the same toolchain. To qualify: build the tag on two different machines or runner images with a pinned toolchain, then `cmp` the tarballs and the published SHA256SUMS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:154:| E-R7 | The no-version installer resolves v1.0.0 as latest stable. Errors distinguish \"no stable release\", \"rate-limited\" and \"network\". | workflow | RELEASE-REQUIRED | After v1.0.0 is published, the documented command without NEXUS_VERSION installs it. A simulated 404 or 403 shows distinct messages. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:160:| E-R13 | GitHub release body comes from docs/releases/<tag>.md. | docs | POST-V1 | Release view shows the curated notes. |\nrelease not found\n0.1.0-alpha.2\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":393086473}},"started_at_ms":1792990834634,"completed_at_ms":1792990835027}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:00:36.122Z","ordinal":374590,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17694-f599-7682-830a-481e9abb3edb","call_id":"call_e9f118d4f17a4008916e707ccc5ccfa6","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5018)\nTotal output lines: 58\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:15:| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\nscripts/check_requirements.mjs:246:      if (typeof record.rcTag !== \"string\" || !/^v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+-rc\\.\\d+$/.test(record.rcTag)) throw new Error(\"RC tag does not point to the current source commit\");\nscripts/check_requirements.mjs:248:      try { taggedCommit = git(\"rev-parse\", `${record.rcTag}^{commit}`); } catch { throw new Error(\"RC tag does not point to the current source commit\"); }\nscripts/check_requirements.mjs:249:      if (taggedCommit !== sourceCommit) throw new Error(\"RC tag does not point to the current source commit\");\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the RC commit | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (ledger enforce mode, final statuses); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:27:| Published package used for installer checks | `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (`a2e94f3`). Assets: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v0.1.0-alpha.2.tar.gz` and `SHA256SUMS`. Installed in scratch HOMEs, plus the operator's existing `~/.local/lib/nexus/v0.1.0-alpha.2` (read only). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:77:5. **Nothing was committed, pushed, tagged, deployed or published by the audit.**\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:48:| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:87:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:3:This is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:24:1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance di…2818 tokens truncated…teInstance`. ISSUE12 matrices mark EXEC-011 \"DEMONSTRATED\". | Any published `nexus eval` pass rate is invalid. The workspace HEAD may be detached unexpectedly. | BLOCKER for any benchmark claim; otherwise RELEASE-REQUIRED: remove the command or label it experimental, or fix it (diff vs base in the worktree, fail on test_patch error, run FAIL_TO_PASS/PASS_TO_PASS ids, never touch the operator checkout). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:140:| R-VER-7 | `nexus eval` is either removed/hidden or grades by FAIL_TO_PASS/PASS_TO_PASS against a base-relative worktree diff. It fails on test_patch errors and never touches the operator checkout. | honesty | BLOCKER only if benchmark numbers are published; else POST-V1 (hide) | Fixture instance where the agent makes no change → UNRESOLVED. A broken test_patch → ERROR. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:3:Auditor: scope E agent, 2026-10-14. Repo HEAD db1ca55. Published releases are v0.1.0-alpha.1 (61057cf) and v0.1.0-alpha.2 (a2e94f3). Both are prereleases, and no stable release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:28:| Published release assets | `gh release view` + installed and executed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:62:| REL-04 | S2 | versioning | core/Cargo.toml:3 (`1.2.1`) vs package.json:3 / cli/package.json:3 (`0.1.0-alpha.2`); doctor.ts:491-492; local tags v1.1.0/v1.2.0/v1.2.1 | RUNTIME. A fresh clean install gives `WARN engine.binary: The engine reports version 1.2.1, the CLI 0.1.0-alpha.2 → Rebuild with make build`. Every release user sees a warning, and its remedy is impossible in a packaged install (there is no Makefile). Local v1.x tags (not on origin, not ancestors of main, no release.yml at those commits, so not publishable by accident) conflict with the future v1.0.0 ordering. | A permanent false warning on a healthy install trains users to ignore doctor. Version identity is inconsistent across components. | Single-source the version: release workflow asserts Cargo.toml == package.json == cli/package.json == tag. Delete stale local v1.x tags. Make doctor remedies context-aware (packaged → \"reinstall\"). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:63:| REL-05 | S2 | compliance | scripts/package-linux.sh:22; release assets | RUNTIME + SOURCE. The archive contains only the project LICENSE. About 150 Rust crates are statically linked (Cargo.lock: 152 packages, MIT/Apache-2.0 etc.), and there is no third-party notice for them. Node deps ship their own LICENSE files (20 found). No SBOM is published. | MIT/Apache attribution obligations are not met for redistributed binaries. Enterprise intake (SBOM) is blocked. | Generate THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES (cargo-about / cargo-deny licenses + npm license list) and a real lockfile-based SBOM, and attach both to releases. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:76:| MNT-05 | S4 | changelog | docs/releases/*.md; release.yml:47 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. The GitHub release bodies are only \"Full Changelog: compare…\". The curated notes in docs/releases are not attached, and there is no CHANGELOG.md. | Users on GitHub do not see known limits or breaking changes (e.g. `spawn_subagent max_steps` removed). | Use `body_path: docs/releases/${tag}.md`, and fail the release if the file is missing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:126:  - The full test suite, including PTY TUI e2e, runs before publish (CI log: 905/905).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:130:  - Published assets match the docs (2 assets each; alpha.1 and alpha.2 marked prerelease; `gh release view`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:137:- **Cross-machine reproducibility is unproven.** The CI repro check runs on the same runner with the same toolchain. To qualify: build the tag on two different machines or runner images with a pinned toolchain, then `cmp` the tarballs and the published SHA256SUMS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:154:| E-R7 | The no-version installer resolves v1.0.0 as latest stable. Errors distinguish \"no stable release\", \"rate-limited\" and \"network\". | workflow | RELEASE-REQUIRED | After v1.0.0 is published, the documented command without NEXUS_VERSION installs it. A simulated 404 or 403 shows distinct messages. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:160:| E-R13 | GitHub release body comes from docs/releases/<tag>.md. | docs | POST-V1 | Release view shows the curated notes. |\nrelease not found\n0.1.0-alpha.2\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","create_time":1792990836.1219323}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
