{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:00:50.783Z","ordinal":374605,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2aea313b-9dc3-4ae3-975c-0ec8b29ab69c","process_id":"50088","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n '^##|^###|G0|G1|G2|G3|G4|RC' | head -80; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '20,36p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | rg -n 'REQ-REL-116|REQ-QUAL-108|pre-RC|G0|G1|G2|G3|G4' | head -50"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n '^##|^###|G0|G1|G2|G3|G4|RC' | head -80; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '20,36p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | rg -n 'REQ-REL-116|REQ-QUAL-108|pre-RC|G0|G1|G2|G3|G4' | head -50"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"3:This is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\n15:| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\n18:A gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n20:## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\n22:The release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\n24:1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n36:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n37:### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n39:| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n41:| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n44:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n45:| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n46:| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n47:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n48:| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n52:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n55:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n60:<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n62:## 1. Rules\n64:1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n75:## 2. Environments\n85:## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n97:| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n104:### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n115:| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n123:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n125:### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n128:2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n138:### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n150:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n155:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n161:### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n208:## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n212:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n214:- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n215:- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n216:- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n231:  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n247:### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n251:### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n269:## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n273:| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n275:| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n276:| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n286:## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n292:- the RC package;\n309:2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n314:## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n327:## 10. Release decision (G6)\n329:G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n331:- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n332:- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n338:- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n339:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n  (from M1) held-out task authoring, standalone proxy, fixtures (parallel) ─────────────────┘\n```\n\n| Milestone | Scope (plans) | Deliverables | Exit gate | Effort |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **M0 Foundation** | PLAN-08 task 1 (test HOME isolation); PLAN-06 task 3 (version sync). Owner action X1 (stale local tags deleted) is already done.; PLAN-09 tasks 1, 2, 5 (ledger checker in report mode, historical banners, cheap doc truth fixes) | Tests never touch the real HOME. One version identity. The ledger is enforced in CI. | **G0**: ACC-PER-03, ACC-PKG-03, ACC-GOV-01/03 | 2–4 ed |\n| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\n| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\n| **M3 Continuity and inference** | PLAN-04 (resume, durable work units, accounting, error path, stagnation, team semantics); PLAN-05 code tasks (server-kind discovery, compact-and-retry, error bounds, timeouts, parser robustness, receipts, startup probe, decoupling, CA); PLAN-11 PR-11c..e; PLAN-10 harness tasks 1–7, 9, 10, 13 | Resume and compaction never lose state. Standalone sizing works. Eval harness ready. | **G3**: ACC-CONT-01..09, ACC-INF-01..09, ACC-VER-05..09, eval self-tests | 15–25 ed |\n| **M4 Persistence hygiene** (parallel with M2/M3) | PLAN-08 tasks 2–10 | Private state permissions, retention/GC, corruption reporting, schema policy | **G4**: ACC-PER-01..07 | 5–8 ed |\n| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\n| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\n| **Fix loop(s)** | Defects found in M5, landed as `rc.N` | Re-run the failed gate subsets, plus regression subsets | G5 | 0–15 ed per loop (unknown) |\n| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\n\n**Total implementation:** about 46–78 ed (the sum of M0–M4 and M6). **Qualification:** 2–4 calendar weeks. **Fix loops:** unknown. A plausible range is 0–2 loops.\n\n176:| REQ-PRV-107 | TOP_TIER I-07 | Local receipts (opt-out). | evidence | `client.ts:561-569`, `usage.ts` | TEST (B §6 G1; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"local receipts are recorded with origin_class: local and opt out with NEXUS_RECEIPTS=0 (REQ-PRV-107)\") | tested | ACC-INF-06 | RR | B §6 G1 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\n205:| REQ-REL-116 | Scope addition | Machine-readable compatibility metadata, download origin & archive extraction safety, pre-migration backups, downgrade state protection, durable provenance, crash recovery, and runtime verification. | installation integrity & lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/compatibility.ts`, `cli/src/tar_safety.ts`, `cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts`, `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md` | TEST (ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14; test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"rejects malicious tar archive with path traversal\", test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"creates protected config and state backups with 0600 file and 0700 dir permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"upgrades from previous release v0.1.0-alpha.2 to v1.0.0 preserving state, configuration and permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"refuses downgrade when target release has incompatible state schema version\") | tested | ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14 | **B** | REL-15 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\n241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":30623}},"started_at_ms":1792990850782,"completed_at_ms":1792990850783}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:00:51.857Z","ordinal":374606,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17695-3311-7cd3-afc0-f01cc0febc49","call_id":"call_d255c9d162394f5b97623f0dde20c39b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5476)\nTotal output lines: 98\n\n3:This is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\n15:| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\n18:A gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n20:## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\n22:The release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\n24:1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate an…4176 tokens truncated…dar weeks. **Fix loops:** unknown. A plausible range is 0–2 loops.\n\n176:| REQ-PRV-107 | TOP_TIER I-07 | Local receipts (opt-out). | evidence | `client.ts:561-569`, `usage.ts` | TEST (B §6 G1; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"local receipts are recorded with origin_class: local and opt out with NEXUS_RECEIPTS=0 (REQ-PRV-107)\") | tested | ACC-INF-06 | RR | B §6 G1 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\n205:| REQ-REL-116 | Scope addition | Machine-readable compatibility metadata, download origin & archive extraction safety, pre-migration backups, downgrade state protection, durable provenance, crash recovery, and runtime verification. | installation integrity & lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/compatibility.ts`, `cli/src/tar_safety.ts`, `cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts`, `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md` | TEST (ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14; test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"rejects malicious tar archive with path traversal\", test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"creates protected config and state backups with 0600 file and 0700 dir permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"upgrades from previous release v0.1.0-alpha.2 to v1.0.0 preserving state, configuration and permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"refuses downgrade when target release has incompatible state schema version\") | tested | ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14 | **B** | REL-15 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\n241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","create_time":1792990851.8577409}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
