{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:00:54.011Z","ordinal":374610,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adede85704081a08d56e2a4597cb846","status":"completed","call_id":"call_4be7853f224f42698ba68f2e503a291a","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '34,120p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '20,38p'\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":2400}); text(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","create_time":1792990853.440359}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:00:54.175Z","ordinal":374611,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adede841ba881a09151b1178c081c05","usage":{"input_tokens":201350,"cached_input_tokens":199296,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":177,"reasoning_output_tokens":72,"total_tokens":201527},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":51713885,"cached_input_tokens":51431680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":91296,"reasoning_output_tokens":49832,"total_tokens":51805181},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6840042364,"cached_input_tokens":6766599296,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":19686517,"reasoning_output_tokens":11416725,"total_tokens":6859728881}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:00:55.050Z","ordinal":374612,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dd5c1787-5561-4775-8ad9-1fc2fbedba1a","process_id":"98265","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '34,120p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '20,38p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '34,120p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '20,38p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n  (from M1) held-out task authoring, standalone proxy, fixtures (parallel) ─────────────────┘\n```\n\n| Milestone | Scope (plans) | Deliverables | Exit gate | Effort |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **M0 Foundation** | PLAN-08 task 1 (test HOME isolation); PLAN-06 task 3 (version sync). Owner action X1 (stale local tags deleted) is already done.; PLAN-09 tasks 1, 2, 5 (ledger checker in report mode, historical banners, cheap doc truth fixes) | Tests never touch the real HOME. One version identity. The ledger is enforced in CI. | **G0**: ACC-PER-03, ACC-PKG-03, ACC-GOV-01/03 | 2–4 ed |\n| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\n| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\n| **M3 Continuity and inference** | PLAN-04 (resume, durable work units, accounting, error path, stagnation, team semantics); PLAN-05 code tasks (server-kind discovery, compact-and-retry, error bounds, timeouts, parser robustness, receipts, startup probe, decoupling, CA); PLAN-11 PR-11c..e; PLAN-10 harness tasks 1–7, 9, 10, 13 | Resume and compaction never lose state. Standalone sizing works. Eval harness ready. | **G3**: ACC-CONT-01..09, ACC-INF-01..09, ACC-VER-05..09, eval self-tests | 15–25 ed |\n| **M4 Persistence hygiene** (parallel with M2/M3) | PLAN-08 tasks 2–10 | Private state permissions, retention/GC, corruption reporting, schema policy | **G4**: ACC-PER-01..07 | 5–8 ed |\n| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\n| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\n| **Fix loop(s)** | Defects found in M5, landed as `rc.N` | Re-run the failed gate subsets, plus regression subsets | G5 | 0–15 ed per loop (unknown) |\n| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\n\n**Total implementation:** about 46–78 ed (the sum of M0–M4 and M6). **Qualification:** 2–4 calendar weeks. **Fix loops:** unknown. A plausible range is 0–2 loops.\n\n## Critical path\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":38772}},"started_at_ms":1792990855049,"completed_at_ms":1792990855050}}
