{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:01:22.092Z","ordinal":374640,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adedea13c0081a0a00ee618fc9b8f0f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_8b7d17a0846a4d668ec2c72b35917e2e","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show origin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md | sed -n '1,80p'; cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1_0_0-rc_8_md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true; ls /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims | rg 'rc_8|RC8'\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":700}); text(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","create_time":1792990881.2363846}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:01:22.260Z","ordinal":374641,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adede9e675481a0943c5ee541b43970","usage":{"input_tokens":207904,"cached_input_tokens":206976,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":368,"reasoning_output_tokens":224,"total_tokens":208272},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":52539249,"cached_input_tokens":52249984,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":93045,"reasoning_output_tokens":51002,"total_tokens":52632294},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6840867728,"cached_input_tokens":6767417600,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":19688266,"reasoning_output_tokens":11417895,"total_tokens":6860555994}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:01:23.115Z","ordinal":374642,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4503bd58-83e1-4ed9-8c9f-a616e951aa5d","process_id":"72729","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md | sed -n '1,80p'; cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1_0_0-rc_8_md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true; ls /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims | rg 'rc_8|RC8'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md | sed -n '1,80p'; cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1_0_0-rc_8_md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true; ls /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims | rg 'rc_8|RC8'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\n\n## Changes since RC7\n\n- **Checkpoint safety:** checkpoint creation now detects a present or unreadable Git index lock before publishing a checkpoint reference, and reports why it stopped. It rechecks the lock after validation and stash creation so a concurrent Git operation is less likely to publish a stale checkpoint.\n- **Read-only mode consistency:** the effective permission posture is applied consistently when an agent and its workspace extensions start or change modes. A temporary checkpoint-safety fallback stays separate from the configured mode, allowing recovery without silently changing the operator's selected mode.\n- **Recovered operation continuity:** recovered operation context is retained across session restoration, while prior verifier baselines remain untrusted and require fresh verification before a recovered result can be treated as verified.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.8` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":26939}},"started_at_ms":1792990883114,"completed_at_ms":1792990883114}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:01:24.047Z","ordinal":374643,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17695-b0cf-7431-b8af-128e80daf747","call_id":"call_8b7d17a0846a4d668ec2c72b35917e2e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\n\n## Changes since RC7\n\n- **Checkpoint safety:** checkpoint creation now detects a present or unreadable Git index lock before publishing a checkpoint reference, and reports why it stopped. It rechecks the lock after validation and stash creation so a concurrent Git operation is less likely to publish a stale checkpoint.\n- **Read-only mode consistency:** the effective permission posture is applied consistently when an agent and its workspace extensions start or change modes. A temporary checkpoint-safety fallback stays separate from the configured mode, allowing recovery without silently changing the operator's selected mode.\n- **Recovered operation continuity:** recovered operation context is retained across session restoration, while prior verifier baselines remain untrusted and require fresh verification before a recovered result can be treated as verified.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.8` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","create_time":1792990884.0471826}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
