{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T06:37:00.245Z","ordinal":375984,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","turn_id":"01a17631-4fbf-7c42-94d2-9588e023f6c0","last_agent_message":"The error you sent confirms the upgrade was blocked by Nexus’s redirect allowlist. GitHub redirected the download from `github.com` to its signed release-assets host, and RC7 rejected that host.\n\nThe fix is merged on `main`: it accepts only HTTPS GitHub release-asset URLs with the expected path, while keeping GitHub credentials off the asset-host request. Regression tests cover the redirect. See [the fix](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/248).\n\nRC7 itself is unchanged, so retrying that upgrade will hit the same error. RC8’s corrected release notes are merged at `bbafae8`, and requirements enforcement passes there. Exact-main CodeQL has passed; the Node 22 and 24 CI suites are still running. **RC8 is not tagged or published yet.** Once those checks pass, I’ll proceed with the authorized RC8 release workflow. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**.","started_at":1792984305,"completed_at":1792996620,"duration_ms":12314607,"time_to_first_token_ms":2335}}
