d independently reviewed.\n- **T3 and terminal lanes:** PR #27 T3 harness head `12edf74` has independent code review ACCEPT. Its CI run [39119197191](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119197191) has the contest-contract and Node 20/22/24 jobs successful; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress. The custodian recorded an 8/8-task T3 corpus seal at 10:43:02 UTC, with corrected private manifest digest `dcbd794ed2998423787fdead4957b38b0c4a8a641855d87304d065d01c3fae37` at 10:43:22 UTC, and released both authoring claims. This is sealed, custodian-validated corpus evidence; no T3 qualification run has occurred. PR #24's real-terminal procedure is integrated, but all required five environments × three sizes still require the exact installed RC and genuine operator evidence; no matrix cell is claimed complete.\n- **RC and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-main candidate. No RC artifact, exact-RC test, cross-runner RC comparison, installed provider/standalone run, T2/T3/T4 qualification, or independent RC acceptance exists. Final stable publication remains authorized but gated on all mandatory exact-RC acceptance and release checks.\n\n## Superseded checkpoint (2026-10-18, `a7126aa`)\n\n- **Authoritative integration revision and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is at `a7126aa811044b45357440b5aee9228500a480a8` (draft PR [#8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/8) targeting `main`). GitHub Actions CI run [39108774170](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39108774170) on `a7126aa` completed with **success** across all five jobs (`cloudflare-contest-contract`, `test-matrix (20)`, `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`: Rust 281/281, CLI 1,152/1,152 with 0 skipped, security gates, deterministic double-build packaging, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke). Source CI is green; installed-RC product qualification has not yet executed.\n- **Sealed held-out T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`, PR [#16](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/16), merged at `f776903`):**\n  - Committed public manifest: `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`), containing 40 external-repository T2 tasks pinned to full 40-hex baseline commits across Go (10), JavaScript (10), Python (10), and Rust (10), and across bugfix (10), debug (10), feature (10), and refactor (10).\n  - Custody record: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` (updated at `ce3f590`).\n  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n- **Evaluator isolation and kernel resource contract (PRs [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), [#18](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/18), [#19](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/19)):**\n  - `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10) runs private oracle checks outside the candidate workspace while mounting the candidate workspace read-only (`--ro-bind`), superseding the historical shared-workspace oracle exposure noted in the 2026-10-17 review below.\n  - Repository workspace history isolation (`96aeef2`, PR #18, `eval/workspace.mjs`) stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`) without `--shared`, `objects/info/alternates`, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits, preventing candidates from reading upstream fix commits in git history.\n  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\n- **Governance, tokenizer, and acceptance lifecycle reconciliations (PRs [#11](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/11)–[#15](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/15), [#17](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/17)):**\n  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\n  - `DEC-17` (`f771a3c`, PR #11), `REQ-AGT-118` reconciliation (`d2c4bfc`, PR #12), and published independent review records (`19dedc6`, PR #14; `f8e19e4`, PR #15; `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/`) resolve the CJK/Hangul admission-safety floor vs `≤ 1.5×` accuracy band conflict: the `≥ 1` token/character safety floor takes precedence, `≤ 1.5×` applies to corpora not dominated by the floor, and recorded Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) exceptions remain preserved. `REQ-AGT-118` is `tested` at the source level (`tokens.test.ts` 3/3 pass); this does not claim installed-RC product qualification.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28516}},"started_at_ms":1792998151775,"completed_at_ms":1792998151775}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:02:33.272Z","ordinal":376297,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17704-9c38-7ca1-a680-55c318e28400","call_id":"call_4cde6542a8dd4253825c47258d776f2e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 19041)\nTotal output lines: 320\n\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\n\nThis is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\n\n- the environments;\n- the workflow matrix;\n- the evidence each step must produce;\n- explicit pass/fail gates.\n\nThree separate questions are judged and recorded separately:\n\n| Question | Who answers it |\n|---|---|\n| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\n| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\n| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\n\nA gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n\n## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\n\nThe release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\n\n1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n\nThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n\nExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n\nThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec …14041 tokens truncated…aee9` in run [39117464186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39117464186); its accepted procedure does not replace the human terminal matrix.\n- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was run from a clean archive of exact `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`; it exited 1 as required. The ledger has 121 rows (107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below-threshold rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` is now `tested` with the DEC-17 accuracy exceptions preserved. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its `CTX-001` blocking marker/mapping is under owner reconciliation against DEC-04. No requirement was promoted by this checkpoint.\n- **PR #26 evaluator boundary:** PR #26 head `c019575` contains the independently reviewed dedicated-tmpfs preflight and adversarial staged-Git/external-store canary; it is rebased on `886766b`, while integration has since advanced to `5193984`. Exact-head CI run [39119705161](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119705161) is still running its Node 20/22/24 CLI suites at this checkpoint. It must be rebased and requalified on `5193984` before merge. A local synthetic permission probe passed (0711 accepted; 0755 and 0721 rejected); the targeted TypeScript test could not run on this host because no dedicated tmpfs was mounted, and the shared `/dev/shm` correctly failed preflight. That failed local attempt is not counted as a pass.\n- **Qualification host:** PR #22 is still based on `a7126aa` (head `7d30494`); its historical exact-head CI passed, but it is not current-base evidence. The owner confirmed the file split with PR #26 and requested owner approval before running `eval/host/provision.sh`. No host account, sudoers, mount unit, or runtime directory has been provisioned. Resource-limit qualification and held-out execution remain blocked until this host boundary is installed and validated.\n- **Held-out T2 custody:** The custodian reported re-derived manifest, 40 task, and 40 private-payload digest matches; isolated author-session audits; and 40/40 reference validation. The public manifest identity is `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`. At 10:38:44 UTC the custodian recorded moving the store and quarantine to `root:root` mode `0700` (task/reference subdirectories `0500`) without changing contents or manifest identity, and explicitly accepted sealed-manifest custody under this boundary. Coordinator verification was limited to metadata (`stat`, `namei`, and a denied `ls` as uid `mike`); private payloads were not inspected. This is custody evidence, not T2 qualification: held-out execution remains blocked on host provisioning, frozen resources, and an installed RC.\n- **Continuity PR #25:** Latest head is `db44e0b`; exact CI run [39119984308](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119984308) is running. Previous exact head `8907703` failed Node 20/22/24 matrices (run `39118809319`); Node 24 reported 9 behavioral failures among 1,157 tests, including convergence recovery and tester-verifier completion cases. The owner has been given the exact failures; no merge is authorized until the latest head is green and independently reviewed.\n- **T3 and terminal lanes:** PR #27 T3 harness head `12edf74` has independent code review ACCEPT. Its CI run [39119197191](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119197191) has the contest-contract and Node 20/22/24 jobs successful; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress. The custodian recorded an 8/8-task T3 corpus seal at 10:43:02 UTC, with corrected private manifest digest `dcbd794ed2998423787fdead4957b38b0c4a8a641855d87304d065d01c3fae37` at 10:43:22 UTC, and released both authoring claims. This is sealed, custodian-validated corpus evidence; no T3 qualification run has occurred. PR #24's real-terminal procedure is integrated, but all required five environments × three sizes still require the exact installed RC and genuine operator evidence; no matrix cell is claimed complete.\n- **RC and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-main candidate. No RC artifact, exact-RC test, cross-runner RC comparison, installed provider/standalone run, T2/T3/T4 qualification, or independent RC acceptance exists. Final stable publication remains authorized but gated on all mandatory exact-RC acceptance and release checks.\n\n## Superseded checkpoint (2026-10-18, `a7126aa`)\n\n- **Authoritative integration revision and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is at `a7126aa811044b45357440b5aee9228500a480a8` (draft PR [#8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/8) targeting `main`). GitHub Actions CI run [39108774170](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39108774170) on `a7126aa` completed with **success** across all five jobs (`cloudflare-contest-contract`, `test-matrix (20)`, `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`: Rust 281/281, CLI 1,152/1,152 with 0 skipped, security gates, deterministic double-build packaging, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke). Source CI is green; installed-RC product qualification has not yet executed.\n- **Sealed held-out T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`, PR [#16](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/16), merged at `f776903`):**\n  - Committed public manifest: `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`), containing 40 external-repository T2 tasks pinned to full 40-hex baseline commits across Go (10), JavaScript (10), Python (10), and Rust (10), and across bugfix (10), debug (10), feature (10), and refactor (10).\n  - Custody record: `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md` (updated at `ce3f590`).\n  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\n- **Evaluator isolation and kernel resource contract (PRs [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), [#18](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/18), [#19](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/19)):**\n  - `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10) runs private oracle checks outside the candidate workspace while mounting the candidate workspace read-only (`--ro-bind`), superseding the historical shared-workspace oracle exposure noted in the 2026-10-17 review below.\n  - Repository workspace history isolation (`96aeef2`, PR #18, `eval/workspace.mjs`) stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`) without `--shared`, `objects/info/alternates`, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits, preventing candidates from reading upstream fix commits in git history.\n  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\n- **Governance, tokenizer, and acceptance lifecycle reconciliations (PRs [#11](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/11)–[#15](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/15), [#17](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/17)):**\n  - `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`, PR #11) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`, PR #13) resolve the historical eight-vs-nine T4 denominator conflict by retaining all **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (including SIGTERM + `run --resume`).\n  - `DEC-17` (`f771a3c`, PR #11), `REQ-AGT-118` reconciliation (`d2c4bfc`, PR #12), and published independent review records (`19dedc6`, PR #14; `f8e19e4`, PR #15; `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/`) resolve the CJK/Hangul admission-safety floor vs `≤ 1.5×` accuracy band conflict: the `≥ 1` token/character safety floor takes precedence, `≤ 1.5×` applies to corpora not dominated by the floor, and recorded Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) exceptions remain preserved. `REQ-AGT-118` is `tested` at the source level (`tokens.test.ts` 3/3 pass); this does not claim installed-RC product qualification.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","create_time":1792998153.2724056}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
