{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:31:32.673Z","ordinal":376788,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf01d3bf4081a0b8b544c6a81b7ac6","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"A targeted upgrade test exposed an important boundary: the old RC7 executable still rejects the signed redirect while downloading RC8, because it runs its own old updater code. The fix is in RC8’s updater and applies to future upgrades; it cannot change binaries already released. I’m validating the documented installer-based RC7→RC8 path now, including that it switches the launcher while retaining the prior version and user state."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792999891876,"completed_at_ms":1792999892673}}
