{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:32:57.301Z","ordinal":376845,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3dfe73ad-e089-4463-80ee-7168adb0e8e4","process_id":"2496","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","ssh -o BatchMode=yes mike@10.0.8.3 '/tmp/nexus-rc8-acceptance-final/prefix/bin/nexus --help' | sed -n '1,140p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"ssh -o BatchMode=yes mike@10.0.8.3 '/tmp/nexus-rc8-acceptance-final/prefix/bin/nexus --help' | sed -n '1,140p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Usage: nexus [options] [command]\n\nNexus Code - Custom Autonomous Coding Harness for Local AI (LM Studio / vLLM)\n\nOptions:\n  -V, --version                                output the version number\n  --repl                                       Start interactive coding session (REPL)\n  --live                                       Start live TUI\n  -r, --resume [id]                            Resume previous session (defaults to latest if id omitted)\n  --approve                                    Require human approval before destructive actions (edits, shell commands)\n  -y, --yes                                    Run non-interactively without approval prompts (forces auto mode)\n  --mode <mode>                                Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\n  --read-only                                  Reject all mutating tool executions and commands\n  -e, --endpoint <url>                         Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\n  -m, --model <name>                           Model name identifier (default: active model in vLLM)\n  -w, --workspace <path>                       Workspace directory (default: current directory)\n  -s, --max-steps <number>                     Steps per segment; continuation checkpoints there instead of stopping (default: 30)\n  --max-total-steps <number>                   Continuation: an explicit total-step limit for one turn (default: none; progressing work continues)\n  --strict-token-count                         Refuse a request the connection could not count on a worker (default: proceed on the labelled estimate)\n  --max-turn-minutes <number>                  Continuation: an explicit wall-clock limit for one turn in minutes (default: none)\n  --stagnation-steps <number>                  Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\n  --no-continuation                            End a turn at --max-steps instead of continuing while it makes progress\n  -t, --temperature <number>                   Model temperature (default: 0.2)\n  --shell <type>                               Linux shell to use: bash, zsh, or sh (default: bash) (default: \"bash\")\n  --fallback <urls>                            Comma-separated fallback LLM endpoints if primary is unavailable\n  --context-limit <tokens>                     Context window limit in tokens; below the provider's advertised capacity it is kept, above it the advertised capacity applies (default: advertised capacity, else 65536)\n  --dry-run                                    Simulate file modifications without writing changes to disk\n  --sandbox [mode]                             Isolate command execution using bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default: auto)\n  --worktree                                   Isolate execution inside an ephemeral git worktree under .nexus/worktrees/<task-id>\n  --authoritative-verifier <command>           Trusted command that must pass before any task completion; its success may authorize automatic worktree merge\n  --deliverable-file <path>                    Operator-declared workspace-relative product file used for VERIFIED binding (repeatable) (default: [])\n  --record-flight                              Record execution into an append-only deterministic .flightlog\n  --planner-model <name>                       Deep reasoning model for architecture planning (o3, R1, Sonnet)\n  --planner-endpoint <url>                     Dedicated inference endpoint for planner model\n  --coder-model <name>                         High-throughput model for surgical code implementation (Qwen 2.5 Coder)\n  --coder-endpoint <url>                       Dedicated inference endpoint for coder model\n  --provider <id>                              Cloud inference provider: openrouter, openai, anthropic, compatible (default: appliance endpoint)\n  --base-url <url>                             Override the provider's base URL (operator-only; required for 'compatible')\n  --planner-provider <id>                      Cloud provider for the planner model (requires --planner-model)\n  --coder-provider <id>                        Cloud provider for the coder model (requires --coder-model)\n  -h, --help                                   display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  repl [options]                               Start interactive coding session (REPL / TUI)\n  run [options] [prompt...]                    Run an autonomous coding task\n  models [options]                             List loaded models from your local LM Studio or vLLM server\n  doctor [options]                             Diagnose configuration, endpoint, credentials, engine, shell, state and extensions without starting an agent\n  check [options]                              Compatibility alias for `doctor` (the former health check)\n  sessions                                     List past interactive sessions and saved transcripts\n  gc [options]                                 Clean up old sessions, tasks, checkpoints, and flights according to retention policy (REQ-PER-102, DEC-11)\n  skills [options]                             List installed agent skills and their descriptions\n  mcp [options]                                Check connected MCP servers and inspect exposed tools\n  plugins [options]                            List loaded custom plugins and lifecycle hooks\n  trust [options] [path]                       Trust a workspace so its own .mcp.json servers and plugins are loaded (they run code from the workspace)\n  checkpoints [options]                        List saved workspace snapshots and rollback checkpoints\n  audit [options]                              Inspect tool execution audit log and execution metrics\n  serve-mcp [options]                          Run Nexus Code as a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server over stdio\n  flights [options]                            List recorded deterministic flight logs\n  replay [options] <flight>                    Replay a deterministic flight log step by step\n  worktrees [options]                          List active speculative git worktrees\n  stage [options]                              Inspect and manage granular git diff hunks\n  eval [options] <dataset>                     [experimental] Evaluate SWE-bench / benchmark dataset against Nexus Code harness\n  knowledge [options] [action] [key] [val...]  Inspect or manage persistent project knowledge graph\n  browse [options] <url>                       Verify local or remote web frontend using headless browser driver\n  upgrade [options]                            Compare installed version with a published release and safely upgrade\n  operation                                    [experimental] Convergence-scheduled multi-unit operations (reroute, park, wait, resume)\n  connect [options] <provider>                 Connect a cloud provider: save an API key (verified first) or sign in\n  disconnect <provider>                        Remove the credential Nexus saved for a provider (environment and other clients are untouched)\n  providers                                    List cloud inference providers, credential status and the selected destinations\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":866517505}},"started_at_ms":1792999976431,"completed_at_ms":1792999977298}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:32:59.087Z","ordinal":376846,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17720-784e-7702-ba34-6738cd08049d","call_id":"call_c8f8d3ca0c714e92bb15a6d913e9d5eb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Usage: nexus [options] [command]\n\nNexus Code - Custom Autonomous Coding Harness for Local AI (LM Studio / vLLM)\n\nOptions:\n  -V, --version                                output the version number\n  --repl                                       Start interactive coding session (REPL)\n  --live                                       Start live TUI\n  -r, --resume [id]                            Resume previous session (defaults to latest if id omitted)\n  --approve                                    Require human approval before destructive actions (edits, shell commands)\n  -y, --yes                                    Run non-interactively without approval prompts (forces auto mode)\n  --mode <mode>                                Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\n  --read-only                                  Reject all mutating tool executions and commands\n  -e, --endpoint <url>                         Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\n  -m, --model <name>                           Model name identifier (default: active model in vLLM)\n  -w, --workspace <path>                       Workspace directory (default: current directory)\n  -s, --max-steps <number>                     Steps per segment; continuation checkpoints there instead of stopping (default: 30)\n  --max-total-steps <number>                   Continuation: an explicit total-step limit for one turn (default: none; progressing work continues)\n  --strict-token-count                         Refuse a request the connection could not count on a worker (default: proceed on the labelled estimate)\n  --max-turn-minutes <number>                  Continuation: an explicit wall-clock limit for one turn in minutes (default: none)\n  --stagnation-steps <number>                  Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\n  --no-continuation                            End a turn at --max-steps instead of continuing while it makes progress\n  -t, --temperature <number>                   Model temperature (default: 0.2)\n  --shell <type>                               Linux shell to use: bash, zsh, or sh (default: bash) (default: \"bash\")\n  --fallback <urls>                            Comma-separated fallback LLM endpoints if primary is unavailable\n  --context-limit <tokens>                     Context window limit in tokens; below the provider's advertised capacity it is kept, above it the advertised capacity applies (default: advertised capacity, else 65536)\n  --dry-run                                    Simulate file modifications without writing changes to disk\n  --sandbox [mode]                             Isolate command execution using bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default: auto)\n  --worktree                                   Isolate execution inside an ephemeral git worktree under .nexus/worktrees/<task-id>\n  --authoritative-verifier <command>           Trusted command that must pass before any task completion; its success may authorize automatic worktree merge\n  --deliverable-file <path>                    Operator-declared workspace-relative product file used for VERIFIED binding (repeatable) (default: [])\n  --record-flight                              Record execution into an append-only deterministic .flightlog\n  --planner-model <name>                       Deep reasoning model for architecture planning (o3, R1, Sonnet)\n  --planner-endpoint <url>                     Dedicated inference endpoint for planner model\n  --coder-model <name>                         High-throughput model for surgical code implementation (Qwen 2.5 Coder)\n  --coder-endpoint <url>                       Dedicated inference endpoint for coder model\n  --provider <id>                              Cloud inference provider: openrouter, openai, anthropic, compatible (default: appliance endpoint)\n  --base-url <url>                             Override the provider's base URL (operator-only; required for 'compatible')\n  --planner-provider <id>                      Cloud provider for the planner model (requires --planner-model)\n  --coder-provider <id>                        Cloud provider for the coder model (requires --coder-model)\n  -h, --help                                   display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  repl [options]                               Start interactive coding session (REPL / TUI)\n  run [options] [prompt...]                    Run an autonomous coding task\n  models [options]                             List loaded models from your local LM Studio or vLLM server\n  doctor [options]                             Diagnose configuration, endpoint, credentials, engine, shell, state and extensions without starting an agent\n  check [options]                              Compatibility alias for `doctor` (the former health check)\n  sessions                                     List past interactive sessions and saved transcripts\n  gc [options]                                 Clean up old sessions, tasks, checkpoints, and flights according to retention policy (REQ-PER-102, DEC-11)\n  skills [options]                             List installed agent skills and their descriptions\n  mcp [options]                                Check connected MCP servers and inspect exposed tools\n  plugins [options]                            List loaded custom plugins and lifecycle hooks\n  trust [options] [path]                       Trust a workspace so its own .mcp.json servers and plugins are loaded (they run code from the workspace)\n  checkpoints [options]                        List saved workspace snapshots and rollback checkpoints\n  audit [options]                              Inspect tool execution audit log and execution metrics\n  serve-mcp [options]                          Run Nexus Code as a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server over stdio\n  flights [options]                            List recorded deterministic flight logs\n  replay [options] <flight>                    Replay a deterministic flight log step by step\n  worktrees [options]                          List active speculative git worktrees\n  stage [options]                              Inspect and manage granular git diff hunks\n  eval [options] <dataset>                     [experimental] Evaluate SWE-bench / benchmark dataset against Nexus Code harness\n  knowledge [options] [action] [key] [val...]  Inspect or manage persistent project knowledge graph\n  browse [options] <url>                       Verify local or remote web frontend using headless browser driver\n  upgrade [options]                            Compare installed version with a published release and safely upgrade\n  operation                                    [experimental] Convergence-scheduled multi-unit operations (reroute, park, wait, resume)\n  connect [options] <provider>                 Connect a cloud provider: save an API key (verified first) or sign in\n  disconnect <provider>                        Remove the credential Nexus saved for a provider (environment and other clients are untouched)\n  providers                                    List cloud inference providers, credential status and the selected destinations\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","create_time":1792999979.0869334}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
