{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:41:43.419Z","ordinal":377244,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a17728-787b-7220-8a63-4ef504e9855d","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2641)\nTotal output lines: 108\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...388 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-26 7:41am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (16,022t read) | 101,522t work | 84% savings\n\n### Oct 23, 2026\nS1692 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session investigating missing startup feature while monitoring active CI runs for post-PR177 main and PR #175 (Oct 23, 11:17 PM)\nS1693 User set approval mode to \"Default to review\" — session continuing RC.4 release gate monitoring (Oct 23, 11:19 PM)\nS1694 RC.4 release gate monitoring — CI status check on main and PR #175 while holding CR bypass blocker (Oct 23, 11:21 PM)\nS1701 RC.4 release gate session recovery — assess PR #175 CR bypass blocker and CI status across main and PR #175 branches (Oct 23, 11:22 PM)\nS1707 RC.4 release gate — monitoring CI for PR #175 (CR bypass fix needed) and main branch while holding merge pending blocker resolution (Oct 23, 11:25 PM)\nS1709 RC.4 release gate — PR #175 CR bypass fix blocked on safe-boundary handoff; monitoring main CI while waiting for claim transfer confirmation (Oct 23, 11:26 PM)\nS1718 Kimi agent handover for agent.ts — monitoring CI for PR #240 refreshed branch while main CI run 40227786412 completes (Oct 23, 11:30 PM)\n### Oct 25, 2026\nS1723 Kimi agent waiting for agent.ts handover — PR #240 REPL checkpoint failure recovery review and CI monitoring (Oct 25, 8:05 PM)\nS1730 RC6 upgrade failure diagnosis — \"Disallowed download origin\" error from nexus upgrade, and relationship to checkpoint fix shipped in RC7 (Oct 25, 8:36 PM)\n22273 9:47p ○ RC7 File Claim Confirmed — docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.7.md Claimed by codex-root on rc7-version-bump Branch\n22339 \" ○ RC7 Worktree — PR #241 Not Found on v1/rc7-version-bump Branch, cli/node_modules Missing\n22275 \" ○ RC7 Worktree Confirmed Active — HEAD at f28861a, No Other Agent Modifying Release Files\n22278 9:48p ○ PR #239 Terminal Controls Fix Confirmed — safeTerminal Applied to Token Stream and Task Prompt in agent.ts\n22340 \" ○ repl_checkpoint_choices.test.ts — 5/5 Tests Pass on RC7 Worktree HEAD\n22279 \" ✓ RC7 Release Notes Provenance Bullet Refined — Added NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION Detail and Validation Behavior\n22280 \" ✓ RC7 Release Notes Refinement Committed as Separate Commit — Branch Now 2 Ahead of Main\n22341 \" ○ v1/rc7-version-bump Branch Not Yet Pushed to Origin\n22342 9:49p ✓ RC7 Version Bump Branch Pushed to Origin — Fresh Push, Not a Re-push\n22281 \" ○ RC7 Final Source Gate Passes — Clean Worktree at HEAD 7eeb386, Branch Pushed to origin\n22344 \" ○ Agent Pool Status — Three Subagents Completed: PR #232 ACCEPT, Heldout Audit, PR #240 ACCEPT\n22286 \" ○ PR #241 CI Started — CodeQL and CI Runs Triggered on 7eeb386\n22348 \" ○ PR #241 CI Started — Three Checks In Progress at 7eeb386\n22288 \" ○ PR #241 Status — BLOCKED Pending CI; CodeRabbit Skipped, 3 Checks Pending\n22351 \" ○ RC6 repl.ts Checkpoint Behavior — Only 5-Choice Sensitive Dialog, No Generic Failure Handling\n22356 \" ○ RC7 Upgrade \"Disallowed Download Origin\" Error — Full Redirect URL Confirmed\n22358 \" ○ REPL Checkpoint File Claims Still Active — codex-root Holds Both Test Files\n22359 9:50p ○ PR #240 Merged — REPL Checkpoint File Claims Are Stale and Should Be Released\n22360 \" ○ PR #241 CI Still Running — Three Checks In Progress, Merge Blocked\n22362 \" ✓ Stale REPL Checkpoint Claim Released and New Slice Claimed for Initial Failure Test\n22364 9:51p ◆ New REPL Checkpoint Regression Test Added — Initial Protected Git Verification Failure\n22309 \" ○ PR #241 CodeQL Run Completed Suc…172 tokens truncated…ered for Head 99217b0 — Fresh CodeQL and Test Matrix Queued\n22315 9:52p ○ RC7 PR #241 Independent Review ACCEPT — rc5_candidate_review Agent Approved Exact Diff\n22316 \" ○ PR #241 CI Step-Level Progress — CodeQL Analysis Complete, Test Matrix at cargo test Step\n22317 9:53p ○ PR #241 CodeQL Check Completed Successfully — Test Matrix Still Running\n22318 \" ○ PLAN-10 Issue #1 Custody Requests Remain Unanswered — Three Follow-Up Comments Posted\n22332 10:06p ○ PR #241 test-matrix Node 24 Job Completed Successfully\n22333 10:09p ○ PR #241 Both Test-Matrix Jobs Passed — Linux x86_64 Packaging Job Now Running\nS1731 RC7 candidate PR #241 — source verification, independent review, and CI monitoring through linux-x86_64 packaging job (Oct 25, 10:20 PM)\n22343 10:21p ○ PR #241 CI Full Step Timing Confirmed — linux-x86_64 Job Step Sequence and Pending Steps Enumerated\n22345 \" ○ Release Tag Inventory — RC7 Not Yet Tagged, Latest Release is RC6\n22347 \" ○ PR #241 CI — linux-x86_64 Job at npm test Step, Packaging Steps Pending\n22350 10:24p ○ PR #241 CI — npm Test Passed, Now Running package-linux.sh for v1.0.0-rc.7\n22352 10:26p ○ PR #241 Base Ref Changed — Main Advanced While PR #241 CI Running\n22354 \" ○ PR #241 Branch Rebased onto Main After PR #242 Merged — New Head d18cd95\n22355 \" ○ PR #241 New CI Run 40240148899 Started on Head d18cd95 — Fresh Full Matrix\n22357 \" ✓ RC7 Release Notes Security Disclosures Corrected — Terminal Safety and Provenance Bullets Expanded\n22363 10:27p ○ RC7 and RELEASE_PUBLISHER Claims Still Reference Old Head 99217b0 — Stale After Rebase\n22365 \" ○ Main Branch CI Running on ed72323 (PR #242 Merge Commit) — Both CI and CodeQL In Progress\n22372 \" ○ nexus-claims.log Confirms RC7 Release Note Correction History — Independent Review Requested Changes Before d18cd95\n22373 \" ✓ RC7 Claims Updated to New Head d18cd95 — Prior Independent Review Marked Stale\n22375 \" ○ RC7 Source Gates Pass at d18cd95 — sync-version and requirements --enforce Both Green\n22376 10:28p ✓ RC7 Fresh Independent Review ACCEPT Recorded — Diff SHA-256 06ac7420 at Head d18cd95\n\nAccess 102k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n⚠️ Heads up: claude-mem can't save memories right now.\n\nThe memory observer's allowance on claude is used up (since 2026-10-26T05:36:25.857Z).\n\nLatest error: Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.\n\nUntil the allowance resets or you add capacity, nothing from this session — or any\nother — will be remembered.\n\nRestarting will NOT help here: it does not replenish the allowance or clear the\npersisted cooldown — so please leave the worker alone.\nSwitch the observer to another provider in ~/.claude-mem/settings.json if you need\nmemory capture before the allowance resets.\n\n(Assistant: tell the user about this outage at the very start of your first reply,\nquoting the error above. Do NOT restart the worker and do NOT suggest restarting it.)\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only.\nServer runtime: use Smart search by default in three steps—search({query}) for an index, timeline({anchor: ID}) for context, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records selected after reviewing the index and timeline. These tools use the configured server project; optional projectId selects another authorized server project. No auto or guided modes. Dumb search is unavailable in this runtime.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed.\n\nFull hook output saved to: /tmp/hook_outputs/01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92/d9dde681-0695-4a76-96f4-ac7e0c379773.txt"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","create_time":1793000503.419463,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
