{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:34.310Z","ordinal":377294,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-15c7e635-e999-4033-8300-3d2c8d1be42b","process_id":"10858","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"installer|nexus upgrade|v1\\.0\\.0-rc\\.8\" README.md docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md docs -g '*.md' | head -90"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-v1-main-bbafae","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"installer|nexus upgrade|v1\\\\.0\\\\.0-rc\\\\.8\" README.md docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md docs -g '*.md'","query":"installer|nexus upgrade|v1\\.0\\.0-rc\\.8","path":"README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:26:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.8` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\nREADME.md:7:- **[Install and use Nexus Code](quickstart.md)** — supported platform, one-line installer, configuration, and first task.\nREADME.md:14:The unversioned installer follows the latest stable release. If no stable release has been published yet, it exits with a hint to select a prerelease tag. To install a prerelease or pin a version, use the tag shown on [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases) and set `NEXUS_VERSION`; see the [quickstart](quickstart.md).\nREADME.md:20:This follows the latest stable release and installs the Linux x86-64 package under your home directory. The installer verifies its SHA-256 checksum and requires Node.js 22 or newer. To pin a specific version or install a prerelease, set `NEXUS_VERSION` to that release's tag. See [release status and platform requirements](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md).\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:65:### Upgrading Nexus Code (`nexus upgrade` & `/upgrade`)\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:68:nexus upgrade --check\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:77:nexus upgrade\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:83:nexus upgrade --version v1.0.0\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:91:  nexus upgrade --recover\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:95:  nexus upgrade --rollback-binary\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:99:  nexus upgrade --restore-backup ~/.config/nexus/backups/config.env.bak\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md:1009:- **Ordinary Engineering Decisions:** Selection of open-source SBOM generator (e.g. CycloneDX or SPDX script); pre-commit hook installer approach.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:80:| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:279:| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:281:| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:282:| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:283:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:284:| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:27:| Published package used for installer checks | `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (`a2e94f3`). Assets: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v0.1.0-alpha.2.tar.gz` and `SHA256SUMS`. Installed in scratch HOMEs, plus the operator's existing `~/.local/lib/nexus/v0.1.0-alpha.2` (read only). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:90:| All RT and MEAS rows in AUDIT §5 | On the RC (G5) | The scripts in `evidence/` are ported into `cli/test` by the plans. The remaining manual probes (installer, doctor, memory) follow ACCEPTANCE §7 and ACC-PROC-05/06. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:102:- **Platforms:** only Linux x86-64 was exercised. Other distributions only had their installer failure messages checked in docker.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:142:**Tradeoff:** verification needs the `gh` CLI or the Sigstore tooling. The installer verifies only when `gh` is present, and checksums are always verified.\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:5:This document establishes the trust boundaries, security controls, and cryptographic authenticity architecture for the `nexus upgrade` and `/upgrade` update engine introduced in Nexus Code v1.0.0 (Workstream 12, REQ-REL-115, REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-07..14).\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:60:- The installer and updater write `.provenance.json` (mode 0644) inside `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION`.\ndocs/DEVELOPMENT.md:36:The installer uses these stable URLs:\ndocs/DEVELOPMENT.md:41:The no-version installer path follows the latest stable release. While only prereleases are published, use `NEXUS_VERSION` to pin a prerelease as shown in the [quickstart](../quickstart.md).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:81:| REQ-DX-01 | Install promise | Linux x86-64 glibc≥2.35, Node≥20; installer verifies SHA-256; no root, no shell rc edits; manual uninstall keeps user data | quickstart.md:7-27,59-68; DEVELOPMENT.md:19 | Published alpha.2 (release run 38539108878) | N |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:238:- **Public promises:** one-line installer pinned to v0.1.0-alpha.2 with SHA-256 verification, no root; Linux x86-64 glibc≥2.35 + Node≥20 only; OpenAI-compatible local endpoint first (LM Studio/vLLM), cloud opt-in; honest outcome labels (VERIFIED only from passing verifier); no default step ceiling; secrets tokenized on egress; workspace code needs trust; uninstall keeps user data. Maturity explicitly \"alpha, pre-1.0\".\ndocs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:65:**Reproducibility status: blocked pending clean-account acceptance.** Resource identity is now configurable in the demo adapter and Worker rather than pinned to the recorded account. However, the included protected broker installer is still an operator-specific upgrade bundle: it requires a prior root-owned `/opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker` installation, a host-specific runtime/manifest, and credential files provisioned outside the repository. Its launcher clears inherited configuration, so the new per-run configuration has not yet been proven through that installed broker. The restricted validator also requires Linux `sudo`, `setpriv`, `node`, and `tsc` with the specific no-capability UID 65534 boundary. The repo does not yet provide a clean judge bootstrap for those components. The commands above can typecheck and deploy the Worker, but they do not establish a complete fresh-account run. Do not treat local synthetic broker tests or offline fixtures as Cloudflare-backed evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**RC7 artifact evidence:** The tag's release workflow produced the public assets and attestations. `gh attestation verify` passed for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS` under the exact repository, workflow, tag, and source constraints; the checksum-index attestation is [59728626](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/attestations/59728626). Cross-runner workflow [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Both manifests validated, and the archive, checksum manifest, notices, compatibility file, installer, and CycloneDX SBOM matched byte-for-byte across the two runner outputs and the public release. An isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)`. These are artifact and installation checks, not product qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:21:**Exact `main` source gates:** Current `origin/main` is `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Post-merge CodeQL run [40243331241](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331241) passed on this exact SHA. Post-merge CI run [40243331324](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331324) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility, SBOM, smoke, and installer checks passed. At this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in a detached worktree with isolated HOME/XDG: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source gates do not constitute installed-RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:31:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `1f3c655971ade086f55347926db16cf2ecd52d1f`, merging PR #161's pinned Linux builder/reproducibility changes. Exact-main CI [39957281380](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281380) completed successfully: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 jobs all passed, including the full CLI suite, security gates, requirements check, reproducible package builds, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. Exact-main CodeQL [39957281390](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281390) also passed. On a clean detached checkout of this exact SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`. These are source-gate results; the CI package is validation output, not a new published RC.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:33:**Distribution scope:** The release owner confirmed the supported distribution target is the GitHub installer/archive only; npm publication is inapplicable. The current release workflow is the authority for published assets.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:45:**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:49:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:73:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:87:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:188:- **PR state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, and #44 are integrated. PR #9's stale readiness changes were merged earlier and are retained in history. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c`, based on now-stale `faf9580`; its exact CI run `39141771002` passed all five jobs, including 1,243 CLI tests with zero failures, resource enforcement fixtures, staged Git-history/external-store canaries, security gates, deterministic package/SBOM comparison, and installer/package smoke. Independent review found a release-critical gap: preflight does not compare protected corpus paths with the evaluator's unconditional system mounts such as `/usr/local/lib`. The reviewer requested refusal of protected paths beneath every mounted host path and regression coverage. The evaluator claim remains active; no transfer or remediation checkpoint has been reported. Do not run held-out qualification. PR #33 must incorporate `4bce876`, fix this finding, pass exact-head checks, and receive independent re-review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:209:- **Authoritative integration revision and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is at `a7126aa811044b45357440b5aee9228500a480a8` (draft PR [#8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/8) targeting `main`). GitHub Actions CI run [39108774170](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39108774170) on `a7126aa` completed with **success** across all five jobs (`cloudflare-contest-contract`, `test-matrix (20)`, `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`: Rust 281/281, CLI 1,152/1,152 with 0 skipped, security gates, deterministic double-build packaging, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke). Source CI is green; installed-RC product qualification has not yet executed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:311:| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:321:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:336:- Published asset hashes and provenance attestations verified against the release workflow and exact tag. The official installer installed the archive on the authenticated engineering host; its version, package manifest and provenance sidecar matched the candidate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:338:- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:76:run. The installer must establish one of these complete roots, not just a\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:114:represented as a qualified installer by this document.\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_TRUST_ROOT_INSTALL_PLAN_2026-10-02.md:167:Node's resolved system runtime libraries. The root-only installer is\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:10:- `cli/src/upgrade.ts` (upgrade engine: SemVer, release lookup, installer logic, provenance, rollback, PATH shadowing)\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:16:- `install.sh` (installer durable provenance recording)\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:17:- `cli/src/index.ts` (register `nexus upgrade` CLI options `--recover`, `--rollback-binary`, `--restore-backup`)\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:43:| 5 | CLI command: register `nexus upgrade` with options `--check`, `--version <v>`, `--yes`, `--allow-downgrade`, `--force`, `--json`, and `--timeout <ms>`. Implement exit codes (0: success/current, 1: update available/declined, 2: error). | `cli/src/index.ts`, `harness.sh` | 4 |\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:15:- Upgrades fail closed when `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and no trusted GitHub CLI is available. The installer now verifies provenance by default through `/usr/bin/gh` or `/usr/local/bin/gh`; setting `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` explicitly skips that check.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md:38:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.5` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER**: packaged TUI default, documented commands work, single version identity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: launcher routing, doctor fixes, installer messaging. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:36:**Installer issues.**\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:48:5. **REQ-REL-105.** The installer:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:53:6. **REQ-DX-101.** Doctor's stderr is empty on a healthy run, and its remedies are valid for the install type: packaged installs say \"re-run the installer\" or \"add ~/.local/bin to PATH\", never `make` or `harness.sh`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:88:### 3.4 Installer\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:109:| ACC-PKG-05 | Installer: bad tag `v1.2.3/../x` is rejected before network. No-version with only prereleases prints the latest-prerelease hint. Deleting a dist file then reinstalling repairs it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:14:- `scripts/installer-smoke.sh`\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:37:| 7 | Installer: strict tag regex; `-fsSL --show-error`; no-stable-release hint naming the latest prerelease; rate-limit message; `MANIFEST.sha256` repair on reinstall; `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. | `install.sh:21-49`; `package-linux.sh` (write manifest) | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:47:5. **PR-6e:** task 7 (installer).\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:56:| `installer-smoke.sh` additions: bad tag, no-stable hint (mock API via `NEXUS_RELEASES_API` override used only in smoke), manifest repair | ACC-PKG-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:14:| scripts/package-linux.sh, smoke-package.sh, installer-smoke.sh, package-smoke-*.{py,mjs}, security_gates.sh, audit_rust_deps.py, generate_sbom.sh, token_accounting.py | full read |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:32:- **Release pipeline.** A tag `v*.*.*` triggers `release.yml`. The workflow checks that the tag commit is an ancestor of origin/main and that the tag matches `package.json` version. It then runs `npm ci`, the cli build, `cargo test --locked`, the release build, `npm test`, and security_gates. Next it runs `package-linux.sh` twice and `cmp`s the outputs (a reproducibility check), then `smoke-package.sh` and `installer-smoke.sh`. Finally `softprops/action-gh-release` uploads `nexus-linux-x86_64-<tag>.tar.gz` + `SHA256SUMS`, setting prerelease when the tag contains `-`. Release notes come from `generate_release_notes`; `docs/releases/*.md` is not used.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:39:- **Installer.**\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:66:| REL-08 | S3 | installer, latest path | install.sh:21-24 | RUNTIME. Without NEXUS_VERSION: `curl: (22) ... 404` / `nexus installer: could not find latest stable release.` (only prereleases exist). The same message appears for API rate-limit (60/h unauthenticated) or network failure. There is no hint to set NEXUS_VERSION and no list of available prereleases. | The first-time \"omit version\" path fails opaquely until v1.0.0 exists, and later under rate limiting. | Tell the 404 apart from other errors. On 404 say \"no stable release yet; use NEXUS_VERSION=vX (latest prerelease: …)\". Fall back to the `releases/latest/download` redirect, which avoids the API. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:67:| REL-09 | S3 | integrity | install.sh:33-35; release.yml:44-48 | SOURCE. SHA256SUMS is fetched from the same release as the archive. There is no signature, cosign/sigstore, or GitHub build-provenance attestation, and the installer script itself is served from mutable `main`. | A compromise of the release or repo is not detectable. The checksum only protects against transport corruption. | v1: add `actions/attest-build-provenance` (verifiable with `gh attestation verify`), or minisign/cosign signatures. Offer an installer pinned to a tag URL. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:68:| REL-10 | S3 | installer, reinstall/repair | install.sh:48-49 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. When the version dir already exists, the verified archive is discarded and the existing tree is reused after checking only 3 executables + VERSION. A corrupted or partially edited install (e.g. deleted dist files) cannot be repaired by re-running the installer. Versions accumulate forever with no prune (two versions measured at 14M+15M). | Reinstall is not a repair path. Disk use grows. | Compare a manifest hash, or reinstall into a temp dir and swap. Add `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. Document or implement uninstall/prune (`nexus self uninstall`). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:69:| REL-11 | S4 | installer input validation | install.sh:26 | RUNTIME. `case v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*` accepts `v1.2.3/../../x`. That string flows into the URL and into `VERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"`, though the run failed at download. The input is user-controlled only. | Low. Path traversal is possible if combined with a malicious base URL. | Use a strict SemVer regex via `grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$'`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:70:| REL-12 | S4 | installer UX | install.sh:32-33 | RUNTIME. `curl -fL` without `-s` prints two progress meters inside a `curl \\| sh` pipeline. The PATH hint prints the expanded absolute path. The failure message on Ubuntu 22.04 (distro node v12.22.9) is correct but gives no install pointer. | Cosmetic. | Use `-fsSL --show-error`. Link Node 20 install docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:73:| MNT-02 | S4 | maintainability | .gitlab-ci.yml | SOURCE. A GitLab pipeline remains (Node 24, rust 1.89), but the origin is GitHub-only, and it diverges from the GitHub workflow (no packaging, installer, or repro checks). | A dead config misleads contributors. | Delete it or mark it as a mirror. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:79:| DX-02 | S3 | doctor (packaged) | doctor.ts:332, 492, 316, 520 | RUNTIME + SOURCE. In a packaged install the remedies point at checkout artifacts: \"Optionally link …/v0.1.0-alpha.2/harness.sh into a PATH directory\" (that file does not exist in the package; seen with `~/.local/bin` off PATH), \"Rebuild with `make build`\", and \"Run `make build`\". | Wrong instructions on the supported install path. | Branch every remedy on `PACKAGED_HOME`. Packaged remedies: add `~/.local/bin` to PATH, re-run the installer. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:93:→ curl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 404 / nexus installer: could not find latest stable release.   exit 1, HOME untouched\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:94:# NEXUS_VERSION=v9.9.9 → nexus installer: download failed for nexus-linux-x86_64-v9.9.9.tar.gz.  HOME untouched\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:121:- **Installer is safe by default.** It installs as non-root under `$HOME/.local`, never edits shell rc files, and never overwrites a foreign `nexus` (install.sh:41-47; covered by installer-smoke.sh:48-51). Checksum failure leaves the existing install unchanged (installer-smoke.sh:43-46). The symlink swap is atomic (`ln` + `mv -f`). Failures leave HOME untouched (RUNTIME, h2/h3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:123:- **Upgrade and rollback work** by re-running the installer with the tag (RUNTIME). Versioned dirs make rollback instant.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:129:  - Installer smoke covers install, reinstall, upgrade, bad checksum and conflict.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:140:- **Behaviour when the installer is interrupted mid-mv, and concurrent installs, are untested.** To qualify: kill the installer between `mv \"$PACKAGE\"` and the link swap, re-run, and verify recovery.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:153:| E-R6 | Release provenance: signed or attested assets, and the installer can verify them. | supply chain | RELEASE-REQUIRED | `gh attestation verify nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0.tar.gz -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` passes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:154:| E-R7 | The no-version installer resolves v1.0.0 as latest stable. Errors distinguish \"no stable release\", \"rate-limited\" and \"network\". | workflow | RELEASE-REQUIRED | After v1.0.0 is published, the documented command without NEXUS_VERSION installs it. A simulated 404 or 403 shows distinct messages. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:174:- Installer runs with `env -i HOME=<scratch>/h{1,2,3,3b,4} PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=<scratch> bash -c 'curl -fsSL …/install.sh | [NEXUS_VERSION=…] sh'`, covering alpha.2, none, v9.9.9, no-v, traversal, and alpha.1→alpha.2→alpha.1.\ndocs/cloudflare/CONTEST_CREDENTIAL_LIFECYCLE_PREQUALIFICATION_2026-10-02.md:84:| Installer Python boundary | Passed |\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:26:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.8` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:29:| 5 | Add provenance with `actions/attest-build-provenance` on the tarball and SHA256SUMS, and upload `install.sh` as a release asset. The installer optionally runs `gh attestation verify` when `gh` is available. | `release.yml:44-48`; `install.sh` | — |\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:27:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.3` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_INSTALLER_RETRY_EVIDENCE_2026-10-02.md:1:# Brokerage installer retry and installed-boundary evidence\ndocs/cloudflare/BROKERAGE_INSTALLER_RETRY_EVIDENCE_2026-10-02.md:7:- The original reviewed installer failed once. Root cause: `INSTALLER_IMPLEMENTATION_DEFECT` at `npm ci`, exit 1. npm was configured with `/dev/null` as both user and global config and rejected the duplicate config path. The failure preceded the install-tree move; the target did not exist afterward.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":817261814}},"started_at_ms":1793000553490,"completed_at_ms":1793000554308}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:35.361Z","ordinal":377295,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17729-4360-7812-9d20-2e05ce1d29e5","call_id":"call_abe25c931edc4cf5bf28eb9a5a130235","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7411)\nTotal output lines: 90\n\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:26:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.8` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\nREADME.md:7:- **[Install and use Nexus Code](quickstart.md)** — supported platform, one-line installer, configuration, and first task.\nREADME.md:14:The unversioned installer follows the latest stable release. If no stable release has been published yet, it exits with a hint to select a prerelease tag. To install a prerelease or pin a version, use the tag shown on [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases) and set `NEXUS_VERSION`; see the [quickstart](quickstart.md).\nREADME.md:20:This follows the latest stable release and installs the Linux x86-64 package under your home directory. The installer verifies its SHA-256 checksum and requires Node.js 22 or newer. To pin a specific version or install a prerelease, set `NEXUS_VERSION` to that release's tag. See [release status and platform requirements](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md).\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:65:### Upgrading Nexus Code (`nexus upgrade` & `/upgrade`)\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:68:nexus upgrade --check\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:77:nexus upgrade\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:83:nexus upgrade --version v1.0.0\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:91:  nexus upgrade --recover\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:95:  nexus upgrade --rollback-binary\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:99:  nexus upgrade --restore-backup ~/.config/nexus/backups/config.env.bak\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md:1009:- **Ordinary Engineering Decisions:** Selection of open-source SBOM generator (e.g. CycloneDX or SPDX script); pre-commit hook installer approach.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:80:| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:279:| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:281:| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:282:| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:283:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:284:| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:27:| Published package used for installer checks | `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (`a2e94f3`). Assets: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v0.1.0-alpha.2.tar.gz` and `SHA256SUMS`. Installed in scratch HOMEs, plus the operator's existing `~/.local/lib/nexus/v0.1.0-alpha.2` (read only). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:90:| All RT and MEAS rows in AUDIT §5 | On the RC (G5) | The scripts in `evidence/` are ported into `cli/test` by the plans. The remaining manual probes (installer, doctor, memory) follow ACCEPTANCE §7 and ACC-PROC-05/06. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:102:- **Platforms:** only Linux x86-64 was exercised. Other distributions only had their installer failure messages checked in docker.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:142:**Tradeoff:** verification needs the `gh` CLI or the Sigstore tooling. The installer verifies only when `gh` is present, and checksums are always verified.\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:5:This document establishes the trust boundaries, security controls, and cryptographic authenticity architecture for the `nexus upgrade` and `/upgrade` update engine introduced in Nexus Code v1.0.0 (Workstream 12, REQ-REL-115, REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-07..14).\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:60:- The installer and updater write `.provenance.json` (mode 0644) inside `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION`.\ndocs/DEVELOPMENT.md:36:The installer uses these stable URLs:\ndocs/DEVELOPMENT.md:41:The no-version installer path follows the latest stable release. While only prereleases are published, use `NEXUS_VERSION` to pin a prerelease as shown in the [quickstart](../quickstart.md).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:81:| REQ-DX-01 | Install promise | Linux x86-64 glibc≥2.35, Node≥20; installer verifies SHA-256; no root, no shell rc edits; manual uninstall keeps user data | quickstart.md:7-27,59-68; DEVELOPMENT.md:19 | Published alpha.2 (release run 38539108878) | N |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:238:- **Public promises:** one-line installer pinned to v0.1.0-alpha.2 with SHA-256 verification, no root; Linux x86-64 glibc≥2.35 + Node≥20 only; OpenAI-compatible local endpoint first (LM Studio/vLLM), cloud opt-in; honest outcome labels (VERIFIED only from passing verifier); no default step ceiling; secrets tokenized on egress; workspace code needs trust; uninstall keeps user data. Maturity explicitly \"alpha, pre-1.0\".\ndocs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.…4411 tokens truncated…rsions measured at 14M+15M). | Reinstall is not a repair path. Disk use grows. | Compare a manifest hash, or reinstall into a temp dir and swap. Add `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. Document or implement uninstall/prune (`nexus self uninstall`). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:69:| REL-11 | S4 | installer input validation | install.sh:26 | RUNTIME. `case v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*` accepts `v1.2.3/../../x`. That string flows into the URL and into `VERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"`, though the run failed at download. The input is user-controlled only. | Low. Path traversal is possible if combined with a malicious base URL. | Use a strict SemVer regex via `grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$'`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:70:| REL-12 | S4 | installer UX | install.sh:32-33 | RUNTIME. `curl -fL` without `-s` prints two progress meters inside a `curl \\| sh` pipeline. The PATH hint prints the expanded absolute path. The failure message on Ubuntu 22.04 (distro node v12.22.9) is correct but gives no install pointer. | Cosmetic. | Use `-fsSL --show-error`. Link Node 20 install docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:73:| MNT-02 | S4 | maintainability | .gitlab-ci.yml | SOURCE. A GitLab pipeline remains (Node 24, rust 1.89), but the origin is GitHub-only, and it diverges from the GitHub workflow (no packaging, installer, or repro checks). | A dead config misleads contributors. | Delete it or mark it as a mirror. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:79:| DX-02 | S3 | doctor (packaged) | doctor.ts:332, 492, 316, 520 | RUNTIME + SOURCE. In a packaged install the remedies point at checkout artifacts: \"Optionally link …/v0.1.0-alpha.2/harness.sh into a PATH directory\" (that file does not exist in the package; seen with `~/.local/bin` off PATH), \"Rebuild with `make build`\", and \"Run `make build`\". | Wrong instructions on the supported install path. | Branch every remedy on `PACKAGED_HOME`. Packaged remedies: add `~/.local/bin` to PATH, re-run the installer. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:93:→ curl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 404 / nexus installer: could not find latest stable release.   exit 1, HOME untouched\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:94:# NEXUS_VERSION=v9.9.9 → nexus installer: download failed for nexus-linux-x86_64-v9.9.9.tar.gz.  HOME untouched\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:121:- **Installer is safe by default.** It installs as non-root under `$HOME/.local`, never edits shell rc files, and never overwrites a foreign `nexus` (install.sh:41-47; covered by installer-smoke.sh:48-51). Checksum failure leaves the existing install unchanged (installer-smoke.sh:43-46). The symlink swap is atomic (`ln` + `mv -f`). Failures leave HOME untouched (RUNTIME, h2/h3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:123:- **Upgrade and rollback work** by re-running the installer with the tag (RUNTIME). Versioned dirs make rollback instant.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:129:  - Installer smoke covers install, reinstall, upgrade, bad checksum and conflict.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:140:- **Behaviour when the installer is interrupted mid-mv, and concurrent installs, are untested.** To qualify: kill the installer between `mv \"$PACKAGE\"` and the link swap, re-run, and verify recovery.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:153:| E-R6 | Release provenance: signed or attested assets, and the installer can verify them. | supply chain | RELEASE-REQUIRED | `gh attestation verify nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0.tar.gz -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` passes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:154:| E-R7 | The no-version installer resolves v1.0.0 as latest stable. Errors distinguish \"no stable release\", \"rate-limited\" and \"network\". | workflow | RELEASE-REQUIRED | After v1.0.0 is published, the documented command without NEXUS_VERSION installs it. A simulated 404 or 403 shows distinct messages. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:174:- Installer runs with `env -i HOME=<scratch>/h{1,2,3,3b,4} PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=<scratch> bash -c 'curl -fsSL …/install.sh | [NEXUS_VERSION=…] sh'`, covering alpha.2, none, v9.9.9, no-v, traversal, and alpha.1→alpha.2→alpha.1.\ndocs/cloudflare/CONTEST_CREDENTIAL_LIFECYCLE_PREQUALIFICATION_2026-10-02.md:84:| Installer Python boundary | Passed |\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8 release candidate\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md:26:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.8` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md:29:| 5 | Add provenance with `actions/attest-build-provenance` on the tarball and SHA256SUMS, and upload `install.sh` as a release asset. The installer optionally runs `gh attestation verify` when `gh` is available. | `release.yml:44-48`; `install.sh` | — |\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md:27:The release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.3` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\ndocs/