{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:38.861Z","ordinal":377300,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adf046b9bdc81a0a1d9eb22f489c728","usage":{"input_tokens":85376,"cached_input_tokens":81408,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":246,"reasoning_output_tokens":147,"total_tokens":85622},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":27813286,"cached_input_tokens":27575040,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":62331,"reasoning_output_tokens":33214,"total_tokens":27875617},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6905422705,"cached_input_tokens":6831608960,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":19787174,"reasoning_output_tokens":11466668,"total_tokens":6925209879}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:40.831Z","ordinal":377301,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8b626f3f-7c6c-4e72-8a01-1847e2109bd5","process_id":"99597","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,34p' quickstart.md; sed -n '1,70p' install.sh; git -C /tmp/nexus-v1-main-bbafae status --short --branch"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-v1-main-bbafae","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,34p' quickstart.md; sed -n '1,70p' install.sh; git -C /tmp/nexus-v1-main-bbafae status --short --branch"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Nexus Code quickstart\n\nNexus Code is a local coding client. It is separate from the Cloudflare Workers and Artifacts collaboration service in the contest entry.\n\n## Install\n\nOn Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer and Node.js 22 or newer:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\n```\n\nThe installer downloads the matching versioned client archive and `SHA256SUMS` from this repository's GitHub Release, verifies the archive, and installs under `~/.local/lib/nexus`. It adds a `nexus` symlink in `~/.local/bin`; it does not edit shell startup files or use root. If `~/.local/bin` is not in `PATH`, add it yourself:\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n```\n\nWithout `NEXUS_VERSION`, the installer follows the latest stable release. If no stable release has been published yet, the installer exits with a hint to select a prerelease tag from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases). To install a prerelease or pin a version, set `NEXUS_VERSION` to its published tag. The `v1.0.0-rc.1` example below works after that tag appears on [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases); before then, replace it with a prerelease tag already listed there:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.1 sh\n```\n\nFor inspect-before-running, download [install.sh](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh), read it, then run `sh install.sh`.\n\nThe release package includes the TypeScript client, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, and the Ratatui `nexus-tui` binary. Node is an external runtime prerequisite. Current release support is limited to Linux x86-64/glibc; macOS, Windows, ARM, musl, and other architectures are not claimed.\n\n## Configure an inference endpoint\n\nNexus works with an OpenAI-compatible local endpoint such as LM Studio or vLLM. Start that server and load a model first. For example:\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p \"$HOME/.config/nexus\"\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\n\nREPO=mikeholownych/nexus-code\nBASE=${NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL:-\"https://github.com/$REPO/releases\"}\nVERSION=${NEXUS_VERSION:-latest}\nPREFIX=${NEXUS_PREFIX:-\"$HOME/.local\"}\n\nfail() { printf 'nexus installer: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncase \"$(uname -s):$(uname -m)\" in\n  Linux:x86_64|Linux:amd64) ;;\n  *) fail \"unsupported system $(uname -s)/$(uname -m); supported: Linux x86-64 (glibc).\" ;;\nesac\ncommand -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required; install Node.js and retry.\"\nNODE_MAJOR=$(node -p 'Number(process.versions.node.split(\".\")[0])' 2>/dev/null || printf 0)\n[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\ncommand -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"curl is required.\"\ncommand -v tar >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"tar is required.\"\ncommand -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"sha256sum is required.\"\n\nVERIFY_ATTESTATION=${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION-auto}\ncase \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" in\n  auto|0|1) ;;\n  *) fail \"NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION must be auto (verify when a trusted GitHub CLI is present), 1 (require verification) or 0 (skip verification).\" ;;\nesac\nTRUSTED_GH=\nif [ -x /usr/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/bin/gh\nelif [ -x /usr/local/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/local/bin/gh\nfi\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ] && [ -z \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  fail \"provenance attestation is required (NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1) but no trusted GitHub CLI was found at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; install gh or set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0.\"\nfi\n\nvalidate_tag() {\n  printf '%s' \"$1\" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[-0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$' || fail \"version must be a release tag like v1.2.3 or v1.2.3-alpha.1 (got: $1).\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" != \"latest\" ]; then\n  validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\nfi\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" = \"latest\" ]; then\n  API_BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASES_API:-\"https://api.github.com/repos/$REPO/releases\"}\n  API_TMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-api.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\n  api_cleanup() { rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"; }\n  trap api_cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\n\n  LATEST_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -D \"$API_TMP/headers\" -o \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE/latest\" 2>\"$API_TMP/curl.err\" || echo \"000\")\n\n  if [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    VERSION=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" | head -n 1)\n    [ -n \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"GitHub returned no stable release tag.\"\n    validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    if grep -qiE 'x-ratelimit-remaining:[[:space:]]*0' \"$API_TMP/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      fail \"GitHub API rate limit exceeded; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup, or set GITHUB_TOKEN.\"\n    fi\n    fail \"GitHub API returned HTTP 403; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup.\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"404\" ]; then\n    PREREL_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -o \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE?per_page=1\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"000\")\n    if [ \"$PREREL_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n      PREREL_TAG=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" | head -n 1)\n      if [ -n \"$PREREL_TAG\" ]; then\n        fail \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is $PREREL_TAG — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=$PREREL_TAG\"\n      fi\n    fi\n    fail \"could not find latest stable release (HTTP 404 from $API_BASE/latest).\"\n  else\n## HEAD (no branch)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":895719197}},"started_at_ms":1793000559935,"completed_at_ms":1793000560831}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:41.852Z","ordinal":377302,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17729-5cbc-7d42-9711-e6ca06c75ffa","call_id":"call_456ef28b2cf641c69d493795cfc965d1","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Nexus Code quickstart\n\nNexus Code is a local coding client. It is separate from the Cloudflare Workers and Artifacts collaboration service in the contest entry.\n\n## Install\n\nOn Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer and Node.js 22 or newer:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\n```\n\nThe installer downloads the matching versioned client archive and `SHA256SUMS` from this repository's GitHub Release, verifies the archive, and installs under `~/.local/lib/nexus`. It adds a `nexus` symlink in `~/.local/bin`; it does not edit shell startup files or use root. If `~/.local/bin` is not in `PATH`, add it yourself:\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n```\n\nWithout `NEXUS_VERSION`, the installer follows the latest stable release. If no stable release has been published yet, the installer exits with a hint to select a prerelease tag from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases). To install a prerelease or pin a version, set `NEXUS_VERSION` to its published tag. The `v1.0.0-rc.1` example below works after that tag appears on [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases); before then, replace it with a prerelease tag already listed there:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.1 sh\n```\n\nFor inspect-before-running, download [install.sh](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh), read it, then run `sh install.sh`.\n\nThe release package includes the TypeScript client, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, and the Ratatui `nexus-tui` binary. Node is an external runtime prerequisite. Current release support is limited to Linux x86-64/glibc; macOS, Windows, ARM, musl, and other architectures are not claimed.\n\n## Configure an inference endpoint\n\nNexus works with an OpenAI-compatible local endpoint such as LM Studio or vLLM. Start that server and load a model first. For example:\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p \"$HOME/.config/nexus\"\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\n\nREPO=mikeholownych/nexus-code\nBASE=${NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL:-\"https://github.com/$REPO/releases\"}\nVERSION=${NEXUS_VERSION:-latest}\nPREFIX=${NEXUS_PREFIX:-\"$HOME/.local\"}\n\nfail() { printf 'nexus installer: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncase \"$(uname -s):$(uname -m)\" in\n  Linux:x86_64|Linux:amd64) ;;\n  *) fail \"unsupported system $(uname -s)/$(uname -m); supported: Linux x86-64 (glibc).\" ;;\nesac\ncommand -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required; install Node.js and retry.\"\nNODE_MAJOR=$(node -p 'Number(process.versions.node.split(\".\")[0])' 2>/dev/null || printf 0)\n[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\ncommand -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"curl is required.\"\ncommand -v tar >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"tar is required.\"\ncommand -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"sha256sum is required.\"\n\nVERIFY_ATTESTATION=${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION-auto}\ncase \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" in\n  auto|0|1) ;;\n  *) fail \"NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION must be auto (verify when a trusted GitHub CLI is present), 1 (require verification) or 0 (skip verification).\" ;;\nesac\nTRUSTED_GH=\nif [ -x /usr/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/bin/gh\nelif [ -x /usr/local/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/local/bin/gh\nfi\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ] && [ -z \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  fail \"provenance attestation is required (NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1) but no trusted GitHub CLI was found at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; install gh or set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0.\"\nfi\n\nvalidate_tag() {\n  printf '%s' \"$1\" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[-0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$' || fail \"version must be a release tag like v1.2.3 or v1.2.3-alpha.1 (got: $1).\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" != \"latest\" ]; then\n  validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\nfi\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" = \"latest\" ]; then\n  API_BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASES_API:-\"https://api.github.com/repos/$REPO/releases\"}\n  API_TMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-api.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\n  api_cleanup() { rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"; }\n  trap api_cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\n\n  LATEST_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -D \"$API_TMP/headers\" -o \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE/latest\" 2>\"$API_TMP/curl.err\" || echo \"000\")\n\n  if [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    VERSION=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" | head -n 1)\n    [ -n \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"GitHub returned no stable release tag.\"\n    validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    if grep -qiE 'x-ratelimit-remaining:[[:space:]]*0' \"$API_TMP/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      fail \"GitHub API rate limit exceeded; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup, or set GITHUB_TOKEN.\"\n    fi\n    fail \"GitHub API returned HTTP 403; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup.\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"404\" ]; then\n    PREREL_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -o \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE?per_page=1\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"000\")\n    if [ \"$PREREL_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n      PREREL_TAG=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" | head -n 1)\n      if [ -n \"$PREREL_TAG\" ]; then\n        fail \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is $PREREL_TAG — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=$PREREL_TAG\"\n      fi\n    fi\n    fail \"could not find latest stable release (HTTP 404 from $API_BASE/latest).\"\n  else\n## HEAD (no branch)\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","create_time":1793000561.8527956}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:41.856Z","ordinal":377303,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6826297709,"cached_input_tokens":6753708544,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18768909,"reasoning_output_tokens":11466668,"total_tokens":6845066618},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":85376,"cached_input_tokens":81408,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":246,"reasoning_output_tokens":147,"total_tokens":85622},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":23.0,"window_minutes":300,"resets_at":1793012946},"secondary":{"used_percent":4.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1793599746},"credits":{"has_credits":false,"unlimited":false,"balance":"0"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"plus","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:45.416Z","ordinal":377304,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0473754881a097b6143ad84eca81","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"This is the RC6→RC7 updater bug. GitHub redirected the download to its signed `release-assets.githubusercontent.com` host, but RC6 only allowed `github.com` and `objects.githubusercontent.com`. It rejected the valid redirect before downloading. RC6 also printed the full signed URL in its error, so avoid sharing that URL further; its temporary signature has expired.\n\nThe fix is in RC8: it allows only GitHub’s release-asset path, avoids forwarding GitHub credentials to that host, and redacts signed query details from errors. An already-installed RC6/RC7 updater can’t use that fix because it runs its own older code. Install RC8 through the official installer instead:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh \\\n  | NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.8 sh\n```\n\nThat installs RC8 alongside the old version and switches the launcher. The RC8 prerelease is still not an accepted release candidate."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793000563479,"completed_at_ms":1793000565416}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:45.420Z","ordinal":377305,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0473754881a097b6143ad84eca81","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"This is the RC6→RC7 updater bug. GitHub redirected the download to its signed `release-assets.githubusercontent.com` host, but RC6 only allowed `github.com` and `objects.githubusercontent.com`. It rejected the valid redirect before downloading. RC6 also printed the full signed URL in its error, so avoid sharing that URL further; its temporary signature has expired.\n\nThe fix is in RC8: it allows only GitHub’s release-asset path, avoids forwarding GitHub credentials to that host, and redacts signed query details from errors. An already-installed RC6/RC7 updater can’t use that fix because it runs its own older code. Install RC8 through the official installer instead:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh \\\n  | NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.8 sh\n```\n\nThat installs RC8 alongside the old version and switches the launcher. The RC8 prerelease is still not an accepted release candidate.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","create_time":1793000563.4628487,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0473754881a097b6143ad84eca81","turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a17729-6aac-7022-af1e-4b6ada130501","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18550}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:45.425Z","ordinal":377306,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adf04722ca481a09fabc091516a1693","usage":{"input_tokens":87336,"cached_input_tokens":85248,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":216,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":87552},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":27900622,"cached_input_tokens":27660288,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":62547,"reasoning_output_tokens":33214,"total_tokens":27963169},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6905510041,"cached_input_tokens":6831694208,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":19787390,"reasoning_output_tokens":11466668,"total_tokens":6925297431}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:42:45.430Z","ordinal":377307,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6826385045,"cached_input_tokens":6753793792,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18769125,"reasoning_output_tokens":11466668,"total_tokens":6845154170},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":87336,"cached_input_tokens":85248,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":216,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":87552},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":23.0,"window_minutes":300,"resets_at":1793012946},"secondary":{"used_percent":4.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1793599746},"credits":{"has_credits":false,"unlimited":false,"balance":"0"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"plus","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:43:11.716Z","ordinal":377308,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","turn_id":"01a176ed-37ea-76a2-9958-cddd74a6f333","last_agent_message":"This is the RC6→RC7 updater bug. GitHub redirected the download to its signed `release-assets.githubusercontent.com` host, but RC6 only allowed `github.com` and `objects.githubusercontent.com`. It rejected the valid redirect before downloading. RC6 also printed the full signed URL in its error, so avoid sharing that URL further; its temporary signature has expired.\n\nThe fix is in RC8: it allows only GitHub’s release-asset path, avoids forwarding GitHub credentials to that host, and redacts signed query details from errors. An already-installed RC6/RC7 updater can’t use that fix because it runs its own older code. Install RC8 through the official installer instead:\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh \\\n  | NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.8 sh\n```\n\nThat installs RC8 alongside the old version and switches the launcher. The RC8 prerelease is still not an accepted release candidate.","started_at":1792996620,"completed_at":1793000591,"duration_ms":3971419,"time_to_first_token_ms":1626}}
