{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:43:17.644Z","ordinal":377317,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17729-d173-7ea0-aeae-81952db7e099","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17729-d173-7ea0-aeae-81952db7e099","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0490101081a0aa846f3777106280","usage":{"input_tokens":88775,"cached_input_tokens":87168,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":357,"reasoning_output_tokens":268,"total_tokens":89132},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":88775,"cached_input_tokens":87168,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":357,"reasoning_output_tokens":268,"total_tokens":89132},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6905598816,"cached_input_tokens":6831781376,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":19787747,"reasoning_output_tokens":11466936,"total_tokens":6925386563}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:43:18.627Z","ordinal":377318,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17729-ec63-7b42-be6d-f5f8f9c34060","call_id":"call_d5267c419c1448998627e122e332d2f2","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT for REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08 on RC7 only.**\\n\\nWorkflow run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) completed successfully. It ran from reviewed workflow commit `1b741144a76fb32de75a750c966be611d0618f3c` and resolved `v1.0.0-rc.7` to source commit `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`.\\n\\nThe Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds used the pinned toolchains and exact RC source. The comparison job passed checksum validation and byte comparisons between both builds and the published RC for the archive and five selected packaging artifacts. The public RC7 archive digest is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`.\\n\\nThe downloaded evidence JSON matches the official workflow artifact byte-for-byte; its SHA-256 is `ffb14aeefe28f2fee3e90eae617a7ca3dc23ea0e90f121d38a432b6f286f9abc`.\\n\\nThis satisfies the cross-runner reproducibility gate for RC7. A later RC requires its own exact-tag run; this result does not establish overall RC acceptance.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"At `origin/main@6dadeaf6796375589ee4c51ee71f722e3c8adc77`, both public manifest identities remain unchanged:\\n\\n- T2: SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`; 40 external tasks, evenly distributed across four classes and four languages.\\n- T3: SHA-256 `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4fba0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`; 8 tasks. Its historical report records blackbox-v1 and validation checks.\\n\\nIssue #1 remains open. New coordinator comments #6393169429 and #6394571756 request custodian status and a T2 compatibility or replacement path; no custodian/author response or handoff is visible. PR #16 remains closed.\\n\\nThe historical T2 report records corpus custody acceptance and 40/40 digest matches, while explicitly treating evaluator-boundary acceptance separately. The current public readiness record still requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest identity; qualification remains blocked on independent custody.\\n\\nThe same external dependency remains: an independent custodian or replacement author must acknowledge ownership and provide the current acceptance and compatibility/supersession status. No private material was accessed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed commit `efb6e38a74e16555178910474f2ae2b72ec1ab89` against base `a7880b64c98d5f3f6522a18a97b2a10489f9461e`; the diff SHA-256 is `f29f8b6f125ead6110210fd9c354953a9cca5fe987f0a505f0c8a85c7ea96630`.\\n\\nThe single RC8 bullet accurately describes PR #248’s merged redirect handling, credential isolation, aggregate backup progress, and batched directory syncing. The release note separately says RC8 is a prerelease for exact-artifact qualification and does not establish acceptance or stable promotion. No edits or tests were performed.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17729-d173-7ea0-aeae-81952db7e099","create_time":1793000598.6272182}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
