{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:50:07.183Z","ordinal":377627,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17729-d173-7ea0-aeae-81952db7e099","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0610d8d9-26bd-4ff5-84f8-5ead37d691d1","process_id":"98405","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"REQ-AGT-118|REQ-AGT-110|verification|independent\" docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | head -80; rg -n \"ACC-SAFE-09|ACC.*VERIF|independent\" docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | head -70"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-discovered-verifier-baseline","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'REQ-AGT-118|REQ-AGT-110|verification|independent' docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md","query":"REQ-AGT-118|REQ-AGT-110|verification|independent","path":"REQUIREMENTS.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'ACC-SAFE-09|ACC.*VERIF|independent' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","query":"ACC-SAFE-09|ACC.*VERIF|independent","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"5:**Status-evidence baseline for this ledger:** `db1ca55` (main, `v0.1.0-alpha.2-2-gdb1ca55`), audited 2026-10-14. A full isolated source-suite run also passed on candidate `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` on 2026-10-16 after `make build`; this does not reclassify behavioral, live, visual, product-qualification, or independent-acceptance statuses. See [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) and [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) for the exact evidence boundary.\n17:| `visually-accepted` | A human or independent PTY review accepted the rendered behaviour. |\n20:Independent acceptance is recorded separately in the \"Indep.\" column: **Y** = an independent review accepted it; **N** = self-assessed only; **—** = not applicable.\n56:| REQ-AGT-002 | quickstart; TOP_TIER B3; EXEC-005 | Truthful outcome taxonomy. VERIFIED requires a passing, deliverable-bound verifier run, plus fail-before/pass-after independence for discovered verifiers. UNVERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE, BLOCKED and LIMIT_REACHED are distinct, with exit codes 0/2/1/130. | `agent.ts:5726-5764`; `tester.ts:371-430,541-627`; `turn.ts:318-351` | TEST at db1ca55; candidate suite at `6151a23` passes ACC-VER-03/04/09 regression tests. Historical VER-04/05 findings and tuned-set/live evidence remain in [A2_verification.md](evidence/A2_verification.md) and the dated evidence files. | partial | N | M5 false-VERIFIED threshold remains unqualified pending held-out T2/T3/T4 evidence; historical VER-04/05 implementation defects have regression coverage at the candidate. | ACC-VER-03/04/09, ACC-QUAL-T2 | B | SPEC-11 |\n64:| REQ-AGT-010 | CTX-001 (Issue #12 blocker) | Injected context carries provenance and classification metadata. | `agent.ts:3301,3789` | SRC; TEST (v1 subset: `cli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts` ACC-TRUST-04, 5/5 at 2c70d39, source unchanged through 19dedc6) | partial | Y (v1 subset only: ACC-TRUST-04 skills/knowledge source annotations independently accepted 2026-10-18; not the full provenance graph) | DEC-04: v1 scope = skills, knowledge and other injected items carry source path and trust state (REQ-SEC-113); full provenance graph post-v1. Not an installed-RC acceptance. | ACC-TRUST-04 | RR (partial), P (rest) | SPEC-03 |\n119:| REQ-SEC-101 | Audit; DEC-01 (amended 2026-10-24) | Without operator opt-in, model-initiated exec and egress require the configured permission decision. Folder trust does not select or change approval mode; unset mode defaults to review. | safety | `config.ts`, `sidecar.ts`, `repl.ts`, `index.ts`, `core/approval_policy.ts` | TEST `test:cli/test/approval_policy.test.ts::\"REQ-SEC-101: the unset mode stays review in trusted and untrusted workspaces\"`; `test:cli/test/config.test.ts::\"workspace trust does not select the tool approval mode\"`; PTY `test:cli/test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts::\"ACC-SAFE-01: launcher permission mode is independent of folder trust\"`; evidence `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md` | tested | ACC-SAFE-01 | **B** | SEC-01, TUI-07 | SPEC-01 / PLAN-01 |\n150:| REQ-AGT-114 | quickstart promise | Deliverable binding uses path tokens, not basename substrings. | outcome honesty (false VERIFIED) | `tester.ts:488-570` | TEST (ACC-VER-03; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts, test:cli/test/repro_false_verified.test.ts) | tested | ACC-VER-03 | **B** | VER-04 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\n151:| REQ-AGT-115 | Audit | A zero-executed-tests pass is UNVERIFIED (NO_TESTS_EXECUTED) and keeps the obligation. | honesty | `tester.ts:356-430`; `agent.ts:3516-3675,5360-5410` | TEST (ACC-VER-04; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts) | tested | ACC-VER-04 | RR | VER-05 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\n152:| REQ-AGT-116 | Audit | One verifier selector. `run_tests` uses the verifier deadline. | consistency | `tester.ts:19-145`; `tools.ts:1119` | TEST (VER-06; test:cli/test/verification_binding.test.ts::\"ACC-VER-05: discoverVerifier and run_tests return no verifier for Makefile with only pytest: or empty workspace\") | tested | ACC-VER-05 | RR | VER-06 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\n153:| REQ-AGT-118 | Audit | Conservative token estimation; `/tokenize` used when available. | failure (context overflow) | `tokens.ts`, `client.ts`, `agent.ts` | TEST (VER-09; test:cli/test/tokens.test.ts; fixture measured on llama.cpp worker b0-live-llama-worker1, limits_version a3c2fcbc2f2b977c). 12/14 corpora within the 1.5x band (max non-floor over-estimate 1.428x, base64); 4 corpora under-estimate within the 0.8x conservative guard (worst 601/748 = 1.245x, whitespace-indented code); the 2 floor-bound exceptions are recorded per DEC-17. **Amended (DEC-17, 2026-10-17):** the ≥1 token/char floor (admission safety) takes precedence over ACC-VER-07's accuracy band for merging scripts (CJK word composition, Hangul syllables); the floor-driven over-estimate (CJK 2.00x, Hangul 1.67x) is preserved as recorded, failed accuracy evidence. Executed: `tokens.test.ts` 3/3 on snapshot `8cf3e82` and post-merge on `f771a3c` (GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS test-evidence record); independent coordinator rerun 3/3 at exact `2c70d39` with independent reviewer **ACCEPT** (docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-11_PR-11d_REVIEW_AGT-118/independent-review.md, branch v1/review-plan-11-pr-11d-ag118 @ bc9fd2c). Floor-bound accuracy exceptions preserved as recorded evidence; reconciled 2026-10-18. | tested | ACC-VER-07 | RR | VER-09 | SPEC-11 / PLAN-11 |\n163:| REQ-AGT-110 | HIST-09 | Independent acceptance of continuity, compaction and truncation recovery. | qualification | — | DOC (\"pending\") | open | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | RR | HIST-09 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-09 |\n204:| REQ-REL-115 | Scope addition | CLI (`nexus upgrade`) and TUI (`/upgrade`) compare installed version with releases and safely upgrade to latest stable or pinned version. | user maintenance / lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/slash/session_commands.ts` | TEST (ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-06; test:cli/test/upgrade.test.ts::\"successfully performs an end-to-end upgrade with atomic symlink swap and verification\", test:cli/test/upgrade_cli.test.ts::\"returns exit code 1 when update is available in --check mode\", test:cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts::\"exercises deliberate approval interaction when executing /upgrade in TUI\") | tested | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-06 | **B** | REL-14 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\n205:| REQ-REL-116 | Scope addition | Machine-readable compatibility metadata, download origin & archive extraction safety, pre-migration backups, downgrade state protection, durable provenance, crash recovery, and runtime verification. | installation integrity & lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/compatibility.ts`, `cli/src/tar_safety.ts`, `cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts`, `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md` | TEST (ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14; test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"rejects malicious tar archive with path traversal\", test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"creates protected config and state backups with 0600 file and 0700 dir permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"upgrades from previous release v0.1.0-alpha.2 to v1.0.0 preserving state, configuration and permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"refuses downgrade when target release has incompatible state schema version\") | tested | ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14 | **B** | REL-15 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\n214:| REQ-PER-103 | Audit | The test suite never writes to the real HOME. | hygiene; prerequisite | `state.ts:278-288`; test setup | TEST (ACC-PER-03; test:cli/test/home_isolation.test.ts; docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-08_PR-8a/verification.md) | tested | ACC-PER-03 | RR (M0 prerequisite) | PER-03 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\n27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n46:| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n300:1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n312:**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n337:- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n346:After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":788497733}},"started_at_ms":1793001006393,"completed_at_ms":1793001007182}}
