{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:50:24.048Z","ordinal":377648,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17730-6a30-7d30-8511-8f62e5de78d2","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed against base `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`. Source diff SHA-256: `81dd7c103eb3d683b323eb81a8b1bc67f8889a28609a1e92f105ac0c8a943e3a`; regression file SHA-256 matches `0452e68b96deeba0ce1c059c4cffd0dcbc49265044fa6ca2621bd220b4eea1e2`.\n\nThe change closes the discovered-verifier gap for registered workspace-mutating capabilities such as `run_command`, and the new regression exercises that path. But the condition at [agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-discovered-verifier-baseline/cli/src/agent.ts:4760) skips `spawn_subagent`: its capability is marked `mutating: false` ([capabilities.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-discovered-verifier-baseline/cli/src/core/capabilities.ts:618)), even though `mayWrite()` explicitly treats it as potentially workspace-mutating ([agent.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-discovered-verifier-baseline/cli/src/agent.ts:2100)) and the surrounding comment says subagent edits need a pre-change snapshot. A subagent can therefore mutate before the discovered verifier baseline is captured.\n\nInclude `spawn_subagent` in the pre-capture condition, ideally using the existing conservative `mayWrite()` classification, and add coverage for that path. No tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17729-d173-7ea0-aeae-81952db7e099","create_time":1793001024.0485306}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18559}}
